{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1481552-case-files-slashers","id":1481552,"title":"Case Files: Slashers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-20T13:07:02-07:00","id":1481552,"title":"Case Files: Slashers","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> Presented here are a collection of Slashers that I have developed for my home games. I wanted to share them for anyone that might need a Slasher for their games. I will try to post a few every couple of days. Let me know what you think. And if you have any Slashers of your own, feel free to contribute.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>The Anarchist</b><br /> Simone Delacour, from even an early age, was as rebellious as she was intelligent. Her love of philosophy, mathematics, and especially computer sciences earned her admission to special schools for the gifted and talented, but her difficulties with those in positions of authority always made her an outsider. During her college years, she began associating with anarchist and discordian organizations, becoming increasingly radical over time. She adopted the pseudonym \u201cEris\u201d, and dedicated herself full-time to tearing down a society that she perceives as hopelessly flawed and corrupt. She is brilliant programmer, hacker, and blackmailer, and she uses the information she gathers to manipulate individuals, inflame conflicts, and erode institutions. She is a hardened cynic, with every dirty secret she uncovers only confirming her misanthropy. Eris takes a particular delight in orchestrating the death and ruin of key individuals, then watching the often far-reaching fallout.<br /> Eris is an African-American woman in her late thirties, with a dark complexion and close cropped hair. She dresses for comfort and has a \u201cpunk\u201d sense of style. She is reclusive and lives comfortably on money earned through blackmail and laundered through various business ventures.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking: </b>Puppeteer; <b>Virtue: </b>Idealistic; <b>Vice: </b>Anarchist<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Disrupt the Status Quo<br /> <b>Tell: </b>Eris strikes at targets she perceives as upholding a flawed society<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2 (Psychology), Computers 5 (Doxing, Hacking), Crafts 2 (Electronics), Firearms 2, Investigation 4 (Blackmail), Persuasion 2, Politics 2, Socialize 2 (Extremists), Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Alternate Identity 2 (Eris), Area of Expertise (Hacking), Library 3 (Investigation), Mystery Cult 4 (Nihil), Professional Training 3 (Hacker; Computer, Crafts, Investigation), Resources 4<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>0, <b>Potency: </b>3, <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 3 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 5 dice]<br /> <b>Talent: </b>Compelling <b>Frailty: </b>Falter<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Damnation (Radicalize), Eye Spy (Hack Surveillance), Interface<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling:</b> A Puppeteer can profile a victim much like a Virtuoso, but additionally benefits from the 8-again quality on any contested roll against a profiled target. They also impose a penalty equal to the scourge\u2019s Intelligence on victims\u2019 rolls to notice traps or react to ambushes set for them in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Falter:</b> Whenever a Puppeteer fails a Social roll, it becomes a dramatic failure.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Mystery Cult: Nihil</b><br /> No one is certain who founded the hacker collective known as Nihil, they have been responsible for several campaigns of cyber-terrorism, harassment, and information warfare that only increase with frequency and severity as the years go by. They do not seem to have an agenda beyond sowing anarchy and chaos, and on the few occasions the group has made a statement, the speak of \u201cmaking the world pure once more\u201d.<br /> Nihil recruits by finding individuals with a demonstrated talent for hacking or other high-end digital skills, and who display an anarchic or overall contemptuous persona. From there they begin to indoctrinate the individual, often having them perform criminal acts that incriminate them deeper into the organization. While authorities are well aware of Nihil (and worse yet, copy cats and pranksters that claim to members), they have little concrete evidence and feel it is only a matter of time before something truly horrific happens.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Purpose:</b> To use advanced computing and information technology to breakdown infrastructure and erode society.<br /> <b>Relic:</b> Nihil.Exe \u2013 a difficult to detect and remove virus that gives access to photos, cameras utilities, and social media credentials on the infected device. <br /> <b>Doctrine: </b>The Only Purity is Oblivion<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation Benefits</b><br /> \u25cf - Prospective Members are savvy computer users, who are coached in using their talents more effectively, and gain a Computer Specialty in Programming.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - Members of Nihil known how to hide their true identities and erase evidence, gaining a dot of the Anonymity Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Members of Nihil support each other on any of their schemes and projects, gaining the Hobbyist Clique (Computers) Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Veteran Members of Nihil are ghosts, leaving nothing but dead ends and false leads; gaining an additional two dots of the Anonymity Merit and the Untouchable Merit.<br /> <b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b> - the most hard-line Members of Nihil develop a web of influence and talents that seem almost other worldly; they gain three dots of Merits, which they may distribute as they see fit between Allies, Contacts, and the two dot version of the Technopathy Merit (Hurt Locker) </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T13:09:43-07:00","id":1481553,"title":"","content":"<b>The Anti-Christ</b><br /> Jeremiah Black believes he is the anti-Christ, and that it is his destiny to usher in the apocalypse. Born Jeffry Moorhead, he was raised by a struggling family that indulged in petty crime (drug dealing and theft) to makes ends meet. Jeffry became interested in occultism at a young age, captivated by the dark images and grim themes he discovered, eventually becoming a practicing Satanist and changing his name to \u201cJeremiah Black\u201d. From there his obsessions grew, with his beliefs becoming extreme enough to alienate his peers. By the time he progressed to murder, he had gathered a coterie of followers swayed by his considerable charisma. He now has begun the next phase of his plans, a series of ritual murders that when completed will call his Father into the world to begin the End of Days.<br /> Jeremiah is a handsome Caucasian man in his late twenties, with wavy dark hair and piercing blue eyes. He dresses the part of a seductive occultist, but eschews tattoos and piercings (fewer identifying marks and a persistent fear of needles).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking: </b>Hypno; <b>Virtue: </b>Certainty; <b>Vice: </b>Arrogance<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b> To usher in 1000 years of darkness<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Victims must be ritually marked<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Expression 1, Empathy 3, Firearms 2, Larceny 2 (Intrusion), Intimidate 2, Medicine 1, Occult 3 (Evil), Persuasion 4 (Cultists), Socialize 2, Subterfuge 2 (Lies), Streetwise 2 (Drugs), Weaponry 2 (Knife, Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Damnable Certainty, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Professional Training 3 (Criminal; Larceny, Streetwise, Weaponry<b>), </b>Pusher, Staff 2 (Cultists), Striking Looks 1, Untouchable<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>0, <b>Potency: </b>3, <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 5, <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 3 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 5 dice; 9-again]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 4 dice]<br /> <b>Talent: </b>Compelling Words; <b>Frailty: </b>Can\u2019t Let Go<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Damnation (Corrupt), Glitch 1, Know Soul<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling Words:</b> When making a Social roll of any kind to get a target to drop their guard for a moment or to heed the slasher\u2019s words, the Hypno treats any success as an exceptional success. If using this moment to get close to the target and attack them, the scourge treats the victim as vulnerable to a Killing Blow, dealing damage equal to their dice pool for the attack plus any bonus for a weapon, with no roll required. If using this to demoralize or sow doubt in a target\u2019s mind, the scourge can instead drain a point of Willpower from the victim to regain it; they cannot drain Willpower from a target more than once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Can\u2019t Let Go:</b> Whenever a Hypno experiences a failure on a Social roll against a target she intends to kill, she becomes absolutely obsessed with the desired victim. She loses a point of Willpower at the end of every scene wherein she does not directly attempt to torment or attack the target. This effect ends when the target dies, or if the target manages to inflict damage on the Hypno. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T14:33:05-07:00","id":1481860,"title":"","content":"New posts <hr /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Arsonist</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Even as a boy, John Everett was a strange individual. Despite a fairly typical suburban upbringing by moderately religious parents, John was noted for sardonic sense of humor, fondness for pranks, and problems with authority. When John was sixteen, his family perished in a house fire (which was due to faulty wiring) and he himself suffered severe, disfiguring burns. After recovering from his injuries, John became fascinated with fire. He claims that the flame speaks to him, and compels him to burn away the world to make room for a new beginning. He has little regard for the life and well being of others, and will burn people as readily as he burns objects and structures. After getting kicked out of the foster care system for acts of arson and vandalism, John has become a drifter, supporting himself with odd jobs and petty theft. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">John is a plain-faced young man, with freckled skin, bad teeth and bright red hair he keeps at shoulder length. He has ugly burn scars on this hands, arms and left side of his face, and dresses in dark clothing.</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Undertaking: </b></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Undesirable; <b>Virtue: </b>Mirthful; <b>Vice: </b>Rebellious<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Burn down the old to make way for the new<br /> <b>Tell:</b> John takes up residence in abandoned places, burning them down when he moves on<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 5, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Crafts 3, Expression 1, Firearms 2 (Incendiary), Larceny 3, Persuasion 2, Science 2 (Fire), Stealth 2, Streetwise 2(Homeless), Survival 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 2, Area of Expertise (Incendiary), Professional Training 2 (Criminal; Larceny, Streetwise), Natural Tinkerer, Resources 1, Safe Place 2 (Abandoned Warehouse), Tight-Lipped<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 5 dice]<br /> Flame Thrower [max 3L ranged;-2 Initiative; 7 dice, Incendiary]<br /> <b>Talent: </b>Natural Compass; <b>Frailty: </b>Rejection<br /> <b>Natural Compass:</b> An Undesirable has a near-perfect sense of direction, and gains a +3 bonus to Perception, Athletics, Investigation, and Survival rolls when present in their nest.<br /> <b>Rejection:</b> The Undesirable suffers a \u22124 penalty on Social rolls that do not involve slashers and other monsters.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: Abandoned Warehouse</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The sign on the outside say \u201ccondemned\u201d, and rightly so. The warehouse is severely dilapidated and despite being targeted for demolition years ago, a complicated web of bureaucratic red keeps it standing. The place is a firetrap; with stacks of wooden pallets, broken furniture, and old newspaper just waiting for a firebugs torch. Despite this, the warehouse often houses squatters, drug addicts, and other transients.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Safe Place Features:</b></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Escape Hatch, Home Security<br /> <b>Traps:</b> Collapsing Building, Fire Bomb<br /> <b>Collapsing Building: </b>The warehouse is slowly falling apart and has become dangerously unstable. Once the trap is triggered, the ceiling caves in and deals two levels of lethal damage and imposes the <i>Immobilized</i> Tilt, as the victim is pinned beneath the debris. If immobilized, escaping requires a Strength+ Athletics roll to shift aside the rubble. Dramatic failures often inflict the Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt to reflect twisted ankles and the like.<br /> <i>Trigger:</i> Structure damage to the Abandoned Warehouse. A successful Dexterity + Athletics roll with a -2 penalty downgrades to bashing damage and an exceptional success negates the damage entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Fire Bomb: </b>Improvised incendiary devices placed around the warehouse are primed to turn the place into an all-consuming blaze.Once triggered, the trap inflicts one lethal damage to anyone within 3 yards of the device and imposes the Inferno Tilt on the area. Any Dramatic Failures rolled inflict one aggravated damage.<br /> <i>Trigger:</i> Tripwire. A successful Dexterity + Larceny OR Wits + Composure roll with a -2 penalty avoids the trap.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 05-24-2022, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T14:42:22-07:00","id":1481862,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Beast of the Backwoods</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">His family had foraged and hunted the woodlands on the far side of the mountains for generations. Over time, the family moved on, either by death or moving far away and never looking back. Only the Beast remains. If the he had a name, he has likely forgotten it. The locals only see him when he stops by a small country store for supplies, thrusting a fistful of old bills at the cashier and disappearing into the night. In the woods he calls home, he does not abide the presence of trespassers. Government surveyors, deep country hikers, hunters, and other people exploring the outdoors have vanished in those woods. When locals are asked about it, they simply shrug and say \u201cThe Beast got\u2019em\u201d, and they warn people to avoid those woods if they know what is good for them. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Beast is a hulking figure, easily 7ft tall and well over 350 lbs of muscle. His features are coarse, with dim eyes, a broken nose and a wide mouth filled with oddly pristine teeth. His hair and beard are hacked away with a knife and his cloths are a patchwork of old leather, flannel, and denim. Most of the time he spends his days hunting, foraging and erecting beautifully carved totems to strange gods. When hunting trespassers, he dons a cloak of skins and a mask fashioned from an elk\u2019s skull. While fully capable of using a rifle, he prefers to trap his prey, then close in for the kill with his trusty axe.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Mask <b>Virtue:</b>Vigilant; <b>Vice:</b> Savage<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Protect These Woods<br /> <b>Tell</b>: The Beast prefers to trap his prey or drive them into natural hazards before hacking them to death with an axe.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 3, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Athletics 4 (Brute Strength, Hiking), Brawl 3, Crafts 3 (Traps), Firearms 2, Intimidate 3, Stealth 3 (Stalking), Survival 4 (Tracking, Woodlands), Weaponry 4 (Axe)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Cover Tracks, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Masked Scent, Professional Training 4 (Hunter; Crafts, Stealth, Survival), Robust Health, Safe Place 3 (Hunter\u2019s Cabin)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency: 2,</b> Willpower: 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 9 dice]<br /> Axe [+3L melee, -4 Initiative; 11 dice; 9-again, Two Handed]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Killing Machine <b>Frailty:</b> Only the Kill<br /> Dread Powers: Home Turf (Woodlands), Unholy Prowess 2 (Strength, Stamina)*<br /> <br /> <b>Killing Machine:</b> Like a Brute, a Mask does not suffer wound penalties and passes rolls to remain conscious due to damage or pain. Additionally, the Mask does not need to sleep or eat, and only suffers a single point of damage from any attack regardless of the damage or number of successes. This applies to mundane and supernatural forms of attack; only environmental damage such as fire, electrocution, or falling bricks applies damage normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Only the Kill:</b> A Mask has lost the ability to communicate. They are illiterate and are limited to simple gestures or grunts. To understand what\u2019s been said to them, they must succeed at an Intelligence + Composure roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Prowess:</b> The creature is quicker, stronger and hardier than it looks. The creature adds one dot of Strength, Dexterity or Stamina per dot of Unholy Prowess.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: Hunter\u2019s Cabin</b></span><br /> The cabin sits in in a densely wooded section of the forest. Many of the trees have been carved with scenes of strange gods and gruesome rites, and chimes made from human bones hang from the branches and clatter in the wind. The cabin itself is a small structure, with two rooms, a root cellar, and tool shed out back. The place is decorated in bones, hides, and old family portraits. The area surround the cabin have been trapped with all manner of hazard, designed to cripple and maim anyone unlucky enough to find their way to the Beast\u2019s home.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Arsenal, Concealed, Home Security<br /> <b>Tilts:</b> Foreboding<br /> <b>Traps:</b> Bear Trap, Deadfall Trap, Pit Trap<br /> <br /> <b>Foreboding (Environmental):</b> The eerie carvings and the tree\u2019s decorated with bones fills the air with an almost palpable sense of dread. Any mortal individual who enter the location must make a Resolve + Composure roll or gain the Spooked Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Bear Trap:</b> There are multiple rusty bear traps scattered around the property. The jaw trap deals two points of lethal damage and ignores two points of armor or Durability. In an action scene, it also imposes the Leg Wrack Tilt. A character trapped in the jaws can attempt to escape as an instant action. Doing so requires a Strength + Stamina roll. Failure causes another point of lethal damage as the jaws dig in further.<br /> <i>Trigger:</i> Pressure Plate. A successful Wits + Composure roll with a -2 penalty avoids the trap.<br /> <br /> <b>Deadfall:</b> A trap comprised of large rocks and lumber hand suspended from the dense canopy of trees. Once the trap is triggered, the trap falls and deals two levels of lethal damage and imposes the Immobilized Tilt, as the victim is pinned beneath the debris. If immobilized, escaping requires a Strength+ Athletics roll to shift aside the rubble. Dramatic failures often inflict the Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt to reflect twisted ankles and the like.<br /> <i>Trigger:</i> Tripwire. A successful Dexterity + Larceny OR Wits + Composure roll with a -2 penalty avoids the trap.<br /> <br /> <b>Pit Trap:</b> A deep pit lined with sharped stakes and concealed beneath a tarp and piles of leaves. trap comprised of large rocks and lumber hand suspended from the dense canopy of trees. Once the trap is triggered, the victims suffers a point of lethal damage from the fall and the spikes, or one point of aggravated damage on a dramatic failure. Escaping a pit trap requires a Strength + Athletics \u2013 2 roll to climb or jump out.<br /> <i>Trigger:</i> False Floor. A successful Wits + Composure roll with a -2 penalty avoids the trap.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 05-24-2022, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T17:16:55-07:00","id":1481962,"title":"","content":"today's update <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Blacksmith</b></span><br /> Walter Douglas never fit in. Heavy-set and socially awkward, Walter never made many friends and was often the target of ridicule by his peers. He took solace in work, and became a talent mechanic, machinist and blacksmith. Most of his evenings were spent watching television, lifting weights and recreational metalwork. After a dispute with his employer turned violent, Walter experienced a rush of power that he had never felt before and quickly become addicted to the thrill. Now he kills to relive that same rush. In time, his murderous impulses came to include torture and mutilation. He is careful and meticulous, making sure to cover his tracks and dispose of the bodies in ways where they won\u2019t be found.<br /> Walter is a Caucasian man in his early forties, with brown eyes and thinning brown hair. He is plain-faced and stocky, with a muscular build from years of weight lifting and manual labor. He dresses plainly in dark colors, and wears a sturdy coverall when \u201cworking\u201d.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Brute;<b> Virtue:</b> Diligent; <b>Vice:</b> Sadism<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To gain Pleasure from inflicting Pain<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Blacksmith gets a thrill out of using his &quot;special&quot; tools, and his preferred murder weapons are hand-crafted and of his own design.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Brawl 3(Grapple), Crafts 4 (Machines, Metalwork), Drive 2, Expression 1, Firearms 2, Intimidate 3(Torture), Medicine 2(Inflict Pain), Science 2 (Metallurgy), Streetwise 2, Weaponry 3 (Custom, Tools)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Metalwork), Cover Up, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Professional Training 3 (Machinist; Crafts, Science, Weaponry), Resources 2, Safe Place 3 (Machine Shop)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Armor:</b> 1/0 [Reinforced Clothing], <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 7 dice]<br /> Custom Crowbar [+2L melee; -2 Initiative; 8 dice]<br /> Blowtorch [+0L melee; -2 Initiative; 8 dice; Incendiary, AP 2]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 5 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Unstoppable; <b>Frailty:</b> Tunnel Vision<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable:</b> A Brute never suffers wound penalties for any reason, and automatically passes any roll to remain conscious due to damage or pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Tunnel Vision:</b> A Brute suffers a \u22123 penalty to all Perception rolls, and to rolls to avoid being surprised in combat.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: Machine Shop</b></span><br /> The Machine Shop is a sturdy workshop and garage with ample workspace and storage for a number of projects. The shop has a variety of well-used tools lining the walls and several machine used to fashion machine parts. Well-insulated walls swallow sound and the concrete floors are treated to resist even the most persistent stains. The Machine Shop has a ready supply of strong chains for restraining victims, and of tools and hardware that function well as improvised instruments of torture.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Arsenal, Home Security, *Torture Chamber<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Torture Chamber:</b> The Torture Chamber is well equipped with a variety of fearsome implements designed to restrain and torment captive victims. All rolls involving restraining, intimidating, or inflicting pain (mental or physical) gain a +2 equipment bonus when the slasher is present.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T17:20:21-07:00","id":1481964,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Child</span></b><br /> When Child Protective Services found him, the boy known only as \u201cEric\u201d was matted with filth and chained like a dog. When questioned about the boy, his guardians spoke of old religions and special children entrusted to their care. The interviewers and psychologists remarked that his guardians seemed afraid of the boy, and stated that they tried to kill him, but he refused to die. Despite the efforts of therapists, Eric remains uncommunicative and often seems barely aware of the presence of others. His silence is only punctuated by the occasional shockingly intense burst of violence. Eric was entrusted to a group home, since few families were willing or equipped to take in a child with special needs and such a traumatic background. Then, one night during a raging storm, Eric escaped the facility, leaving a trail of corpses in his wake. His current whereabouts are unknown.<br /> Eric is a handsome twelve year old Caucasian boy who is slightly above average height for his age with blond hair and blue eyes. He dresses in stolen clothing and is willing to kill and steal to obtain food, shelter, or any other needs. He possesses an almost unnatural degree of speed and grace and is disturbingly strong for someone of his size and age. He typically shuns the company of others, but a like-minded person (another slasher or similarly dark-hearted individual) might be able to break through to him and give him the family he has never had. He currently travels by bicycle (always stolen) and by bus when he can afford it. He is working his way west, guided by forces that even he does not understand.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Mask; <b>Virtue:</b> Observant; <b>Vice:</b> Impulsive<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Take What I Want<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Eric kills anyone that tries to restrain him, gets in his way or has something that he wants.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 2<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3(Climb), Brawl 4, Crafts 2, Empathy 2, Larceny 2(Escape), Stealth 4 (Silence), Streetwise 2, Survival 3 (Urban), Weaponry 3 (Blades, Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Damnable Certainty, Danger Sense, Fighting Finesse, Fleet of Foot 2, Hands of a Killer, Striking Looks 1, *Style: Relentless Assault 2, Small-Framed, Trained Observer 3<br /> <i>* Beast: The Primordial, pg. 118</i><br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 1, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Box Cutter [+0L melee, 9 dice]<br /> Claw Hammer [+1L melee, -1 Initiative; 9 dice; Improvised]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Killing Machine Frailty: Only the Kill<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Numen (Innocuous, Pathfinder, Speed)<br /> <br /> <b>Killing Machine:</b> Like a Brute, a Mask does not suffer wound penalties and passes rolls to remain conscious due to damage or pain. Additionally, the Mask does not need to sleep or eat, and only suffers a single point of damage from any attack regardless of the damage or number of successes. This applies to mundane and supernatural forms of attack; only environmental damage such as fire, electrocution, or falling bricks applies damage normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Only the Kill:</b> A Mask has lost the ability to communicate. They are illiterate and are limited to simple gestures or grunts. To understand what\u2019s been said to them, they must succeed at an Intelligence + Composure roll. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T18:11:45-07:00","id":1482043,"title":"","content":"Today's Post <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Copy Cat</span></b><br /> Fawne Martin developed a fascination with serial killers and the criminal mind will in middle school, keeping a scrap book of famous cases that she studied obsessively, earning her a reputation as \u201cthat weird killer girl\u201d. Her obsession continued as she become an adult, and in college she studied criminal psychology, and has become well regarded from her skill as a profiler. She has also quietly been killing her own victims, using her knowledge to \u201crecreate\u201d the particular style and tell of other serial killers. So far, all of her murders have been attributed to other killers, and she continues her \u201csecret hobby\u201d with none the wiser.<br /> Fawne is a Caucasian woman in her early thirties with an athletic build. She has fair skin and auburn hair she wears in a bun. She dresses to convey a sense of consummate professionalism.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Virtuoso; <b>Virtue:</b> Meticulous;<b> Vice:</b> Overconfident<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> The replicate a murder so well the authorities blame the wrong killer<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Fawne disguises her killings using the <i>modus operandi</i> of a killer she has studied or profiled.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3 (Psychology), Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Empathy 4 (Profiling), Firearms 2, Investigation 3 (Crime Scene), Medicine 2, Persuasion 2(Isolate Target), Socialize 2, Stealth 3, Subterfuge 3 (Alibi), Weaponry 2 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Cover Up, Face in the Crowd, Professional Training 4 (Profiler; Academics, Empathy, Investigation), Resources 3, Telltale Murder, Untouchable<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 6 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Profiling; Frailty: Control Freak<br /> <br /> <b>Profiling:</b> Roll Intelligence + Empathy, contested by the victim\u2019s Manipulation + Subterfuge if they are actively attempting to conceal their motives or disguise their nature. Predict the victim\u2019s actions; they win ties in contested rolls against them, may raise Initiative one higher than the target\u2019s Initiative result at the beginning of combat. If able to spend an entire scene socially interacting with the target before making a roll, the ripper learns one unique trait: Virtue, Vice, Integrity or Willpower rating, Conditions suffered, Endowments, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Control Freak:</b> Whenever a Virtuoso fails on an Intelligence-based roll, or on a roll using one of the Skills bolstered by their Undertaking, they lose two points of Willpower.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T18:19:56-07:00","id":1482045,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Dark Father</b></span><br /> In his youth during the seventies, Father Raoul Medina ran with a rough crowd and found his faith while serving time for armed robbery. Upon his release, he dedicated himself to the church and became a respected pillar of the community. But while maintaining the public image of the dutiful priest, his private actions were considerably darker. Obsessed with visions of hellfire and damnation, he adopted the personae of \u201cthe Dark Father\u201d; a masked figure in black vestments. His murders involve prolonged, gruesome torture, and his victims always fit Father Medina\u2019s loose definition of \u201csinner\u201d. During the nineties, he began taping his exploits, and distributed them through his remaining criminal connections to collectors of snuff footage. Now in his sixties, Father Medina remains in good shape, but considers himself retired, and rarely wears the mask of the Dark Father anymore. However, particularly egregious \u201csins\u201d might compel the Dark Father to appear once more.<br /> Father Medina is an older gentleman of Mexican descent of average height. His hair has gone silver and the years have lined his face. He is in good shape for a man of his age, but has begun to slow down and no longer exercises with as much frequency or vigor. While wearing the mask of the Dark Father, Father Medina seems blessed with uncanny luck, and has avoided capture despite multiple close calls over the years. If exposed he is likely to retreat into the Dark Father personae and go on a killing spree until he is brought down.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Puppeteer; <b>Virtue:</b> Righteous; <b>Vice:</b> Depraved<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Punish \u201cSinners\u201d<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Dark Father crafts punishments appropriate to the victims &quot;sins&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 4(Research, Religion), Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Crafts 3, Expression 2, Firearms 2, Larceny 3, Intimidate 3 (Dark Father), Investigation 3, Medicine 2 (Torture), Occult 2(Hell), Persuasion 3 (Sermon), Streetwise 3 (Black Market, Prison), Stealth 3 (Follow), Subterfuge 4 (Double Life), Weaponry 4 (Blades)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 3 (Cartels), Alternate Identity 3, Contacts 2 (Human Traffickers, Snuff Film Collectors), Cover Up, Damnable Certainty, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Fame 1(Dark Father), Inspiring, Language (English), Professional Training 4 (Religious Leader; Academics, Occult, Persuasion), Resources 3, Safe Place 2 (The Chapel), Untouchable<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 2, <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 5 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 8 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> Machete [+2L melee;-2 Initiative; 8 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling; <b>Frailty:</b> Falter<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Glitch 3<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling:</b> A Puppeteer can profile a victim much like a Virtuoso, but additionally benefits from the 8-again quality on any contested roll against a profiled target. They also impose a penalty equal to the scourge\u2019s Intelligence on victims\u2019 rolls to notice traps or react to ambushes set for them in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Falter:</b> Whenever a Puppeteer fails a Social roll, it becomes a dramatic failure.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: The Chapel</b></span><br /> The Chapel is an abandoned church several miles outside of town. Despite the fence and \u201cNo Trespassers\u201d signs, the church is marked by years of petty vandalism from drifters and rebellious teens. Long used as a meeting place by the local criminal cartels, it was given over to the Dark Father, as a place to torment sinners (and film content for distribution). The cellar of the building as been converted to a chamber of horrors, where the Dark Father enacts the very torments of Hell upon his victims.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Concealed, Torture Chamber*<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Torture Chamber:</b> The Torture Chamber is well equipped with a variety of fearsome implements designed to restrain and torment captive victims. All rolls involving restraining, intimidating, or inflicting pain (mental or physical) gain a +2 equipment bonus when the slasher is present.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T13:02:47-07:00","id":1482397,"title":"","content":"today's posts <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Doctor</b></span><br /> Dr. Akeem Assad is a respected neurologist, well-renowned for great skill in treating injuries to the brain and nervous system. His theories regarding the functions of the human brain and cognitive processes are revolutionary.<br /> But for all his accomplishment and acclaim, Dr. Assad hungers for more. Not merely an understanding of the physical mind and body, but an inquiry into the nature of the soul. To this end, he has begun acquiring \u201cvolunteers\u201d for his exploratory procedures. He tends to choose subjects that are hard to trace or whose disappearance will go unnoticed, but will risk exposure is a particularly exceptional (displaying high intelligence or great moral character) subject present\u2019s themselves. Most of his subjects do not survive the procedures, but it is a small price to pay for the advancement of medical science. His skills have grown advanced enough that he believes he can literally extract a person\u2019s soul. Of course, much more research is necessary before he can publish is findings.<br /> Dr. Assad is a dark-skinned African man of above average height in in late fifties. He carries a distinguished air and is fit and handsome. He has used his considerable wealth to purchase an out-of-the-way space where he can perform his research in peace, and has a small crew of accomplices to help him procure new subjects.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Puppeteer; <b>Virtue:</b> Inquisitive; <b>Vice:</b> Clinical<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To discern the true nature of the Soul<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Victims are slain in a medical (or pseudo medical) procedure<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3, Athletics 2, Empathy 3, Firearms 3, Investigation 2, Medicine 5(Neurosurgery), Occult 3, Persuasion 2, Science 4, Socialize 2, Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 3 (Medical Implements)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Neurosurgery), Closed Book 2, Cover Up, Damnable Certainty, Fame 1(Surgeon), Hands of a Killer, Language (Arabic, English, others), Professional Training 5(Doctor; Empathy, Medicine, Occult), Resources 4, Safe Place 3 (The Operating Room), Staff 3 (Accomplices), Untouchable<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 3, <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 8, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 3 dice]<br /> Medical Implements [+1L melee, -2 Initiative; 7 dice, Improvised]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 7 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling <b>Frailty:</b> Falter<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Agonize, Madness and Terror, Soul Stealer (Medical Procedure)<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling:</b> A Puppeteer can profile a victim much like a Virtuoso, but additionally benefits from the 8-again quality on any contested roll against a profiled target. They also impose a penalty equal to the scourge\u2019s Intelligence on victims\u2019 rolls to notice traps or react to ambushes set for them in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Falter:</b> Whenever a Puppeteer fails a Social roll, it becomes a dramatic failure.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: The Operating Room</b></span><br /> The property sits on an isolated stretch of road in the industrial district of town. It was once a factory, and to casual observation the building has fallen into disrepair. But hidden in the basement is well-equipped operating room where medical and pseudo-medical procedures are routinely performed. The operating table has thick straps to restrain \u201cuncooperative\u201d patients, and the room has a hose and drain system to clear away spilled fluids. The facility as has several rooms where surviving patients can recover (locked from the outside), and an incinerator to deal with corpses and other medical waste.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> *Holding Cells, Home Security, Infirmary<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Holding Cells:</b> Holding Cells are secure rooms designed to hold captives. Attempts to escape one of these rooms requires an extended Intelligence + Larceny roll with a -2 penalty that requires (2x dots purchased in the Merit) successes, with one roll applied for each day of captivity. For attempts to physically break through the doors or walls, the durability of such barriers gain a +2 bonus. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 06-13-2022, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T13:07:33-07:00","id":1482398,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Enforcer</span></b><br /> The woman nick-named \u201cMaria Muerte\u201d began her life abandoned on the steps of a church in Mexico City when she was only a few weeks old. The child was marked (some would say cursed) with a condition that rendered her hairless, and a facial deformity that gave her a skull-like countenance. Even at an early age, she demonstrated unnatural strength and outbursts of anger that left her peer terrified and the nuns convinced she was the spawn of demons, and all were relieved when she ran away from the orphanage as a teen. Since then, she has become an infamous enforcer for the Cartels, employing her inhuman strength to maim and kill at their behest. True, she would murder on a whim for free (and often does), but has come to appreciate money and notoriety.<br /> Maria is a tall woman with a hard, muscular physique. She is completely hairless, and has thin lips, sunken eyes, and hollow cheeks which make her face a living skull. Her skin (except for her face) is covered in elaborate, beautiful, tattoos.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Mutant; <b>Virtue:</b> Bravery; <b>Vice:</b> Violence<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Finds ways to channel or indulge her violent impulses<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Maria prefers to beat people to death with her bare hands<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 4 (Armed Opponents, Fists), Firearms 2, Larceny 3(Breaking and Entering), Intimidate 3(Frightening, Torture), Persuasion 2, Stealth 2, Subterfuge 2 (Lying to Cops), Streetwise 2(Cartels), Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Iron Will, Language (English), Professional Training 3 (Criminal; Brawl, Larceny, Streetwise), Resources 2, Status 2 (Cartel), Striking Looks 1 (Tattooed), Style: Street Fighting 3<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 3, <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Armor:</b> 2, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Crushing Blows [+2L melee, AP 2; 9 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 6 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Warped Form (Crushing Blows) <b>Frailty:</b> Sensitivity (Cold Temperatures)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Glitch 2, Regenerate<br /> <br /> <b>Warped Form:</b> A Mutant possesses natural weaponry that has a weapon modifier and armor-piercing quality of 2, with no Initiative modifier, as well as 2 points of Armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Sensitivity:</b> As well as the Social penalty suffered by Undesirables, a Mutant is sensitive to a stimulus chosen by the Storyteller. This might include bright light, the scent of roses, the feel of velvet, the sound of classical music, cats, extreme heat, etc. When exposed to the stimulus, the Mutant must spend a Willpower point or attempt to flee the scene immediately; if unable to flee, they either attempt to hide, or lash out to destroy or remove the stimulus. Regardless of spent Willpower, they suffer a \u22122 penalty on all dice pools provided the stimulus remains present.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T17:15:48-07:00","id":1482682,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Flesh Stealer</span></b><br /> The individual called \u201cThe Flesh Stealer\u201d lived a relatively normal life until early adolescence, when he developed a condition where his skin breaks out into painful rashes, hives, and weeping sores. Even after several years of visiting doctors and specialists, he was no closer to either an explanation of the cause, or a cure. As his condition grew worse, and with the family saving exhausted, the he turned to more unorthodox solutions. In his increasingly obscure and occult studies, he learned how to prepare a special restorative bath to relieve his pain. This bath formula contained many odd elements, including freshly killed flesh and blood. This solution worked, and could be made with the flesh of rodents and other small animals. But as time wore one, the salves lost effectiveness, and the more flesh from larger animals needed to be used. Eventually, only human flesh would suffice. Now the Flesh Stealer stalks the night, seeking ingredients for his bath. Only the best will do, and he prefers young, fit people with clear skin. Years of exposure to the strange formula have warped him, his mind broken and his body altered to the degree that he now can tear the flesh from his victims with his bare hands. He also is exceptionally photosensitive (this is mostly psychosomatic) and avoids direct daylight whenever possible.<br /> The Flesh Stealer is a broad shouldered man of average height. His brown hair is long but has started to fall out in patches. His skin is covered in ugly rashes and blisters, and he covers up with dark clothing or medicated bandages as much as possible. These wounds are excruciatingly painful. Bathing in a specially prepared restorative bath relieves the pain for several weeks, but eventually it returns and more ingredients must be obtained.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Mutant; <b>Virtue:</b> Perseverance; <b>Vice:</b> Desperation<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Find the best flesh and blood for preparing the healing bath<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Flesh Stealer\u2019s victims are found mutilated; drained of blood and with large portions of skin, meat, and organs torn away.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3 (Pursuit), Brawl 4 (Rend), Crafts 2, Investigate 3, Larceny 3, Medicine 2 (Skin Conditions), Occult 3 (Bathing Ritual), Science 2, Stealth 4 (Hide), Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 2, Back Road Atlas, Contacts 2 (Dermatologists, Occultists), Hardy 2, Holistic Awareness, Iron Stamina 2, *Ritual Sorcerer (Bathing Ritual), Striking Looks 1 (Pitiable), **Style: Relentless Assault 3<br /> <i>* Mummy: The Cursed 2nd Edition, p.120</i><br /> <i>* Beast: The Primordial, p. 118</i><br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 3, <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Armor:</b> 2, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Rending Hands [+2L melee, AP 2; 7 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Warped Form (Rending Hands) <b>Frailty:</b> Sensitivity (Sunlight)<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Numen (Drain), Regeneration, Shadow Attraction<br /> <br /> <b>Warped Form:</b> A Mutant possesses natural weaponry that has a weapon modifier and armor-piercing quality of 2, with no Initiative modifier, as well as 2 points of Armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Sensitivity:</b> As well as the Social penalty suffered by Undesirables, a Mutant is sensitive to a stimulus chosen by the Storyteller. This might include bright light, the scent of roses, the feel of velvet, the sound of classical music, cats, extreme heat, etc. When exposed to the stimulus, the Mutant must spend a Willpower point or attempt to flee the scene immediately; if unable to flee, they either attempt to hide, or lash out to destroy or remove the stimulus. Regardless of spent Willpower, they suffer a \u22122 penalty on all dice pools provided the stimulus remains present.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Bather:</b> Unknown to the Flesh Stealer, he has become a Blood Bather (Mummy: The Cursed 2nd Edition, p.258). In addition to relieving his painful skin condition, the bathing ritual is maintaining his youth and vigor. All long as he continues to perform the ritual regularly, the Flesh Stealer might continue to stalk his victims for a very long time.<br /> <br /> <b>Relentless Assault:</b> The Flesh Stealer fights with complete abandon. He throws himself at his opponents without thought or hesitation, turning himself into a ruthless killing machine. He may use this with Brawl or Weaponry attacks.<br /> \u2022 <b>Drop of a Hat:</b> The Flesh Stealer always moves to strike first. In the first turn of a fight, he adds 3 to his Initiative score, so long as he intends to make an all-out attack. After the first turn, this bonus fades.<br /> \u2022 <b>Eye of the Tiger:</b> Choose a target. When making an all-out attack against that target, The Flesh Stealer retains his Defense against him. He still loses it against other characters. He\u2019s still considered to have sacrificed his Defense for the purpose of using other Style maneuvers.<br /> \u2022<b> Dig Deep:</b> The Flesh Stealer doesn\u2019t strike for his enemy\u2019s skin; he strikes for a spot a few feet behind it. He can choose to remove one die from his dice pool before rolling an attack. If he does, add a point of weapon damage to his attack.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 06-01-2022, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T17:19:41-07:00","id":1482683,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Gourmet</span></b><br /> Frank Sha (<i>ne</i> Sha Fan) was born to Chinese immigrants and raised in the restaurant business. While initially a humble takeout and delivery place, the family restaurant grew to become an upscale establishment, and Frank grew with it. Expected to take over the business, he graduated culinary school with high marks and spent years traveling the world, working in all manner of restaurants and experiencing new and exotic cuisines. During this time, he developed several curious \u201ctastes\u201d that in time grew to an obsession. Now he runs the family restaurant, elevating it\u2019s success to new heights, while occasionally hosting \u201cspecial dinners\u201d for an exclusive set of clients. But even outside of these events, he is always experimenting with new recipes and is very selective when \u201csourcing ingredients).<br /> Frank is an Asian man in his late thirties. He is of average height but is remarkably fit, being almost as dedicated to physical fitness as he is cooking. He dresses well and spends a great deal of his income on expensive luxuries. He approaches cooking (and hunting his victims) with precision and discipline.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Virtuoso; <b>Virtue:</b> Disciplined; <b>Vice:</b> Insatiable<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Savor Human flesh<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Gourmet eats a portion of each victim<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Athletics 4(Cardio), Brawl 2, Crafts 4 (Cooking), Expression 4(Arrangement, Calligraphy), Medicine 2 (Anatomy), Socialize 3(Dinner Party, Kitchen Staff), Stealth 4, Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 4 (Cooking Utensils, Knife)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Knife), Contacts 2 (Farmer\u2019s Markets, Restaurants), Cover Up, Language (Cantonese, English, French, Japanese),Professional Training 3(Chef; Crafts, Expression, Weaponry), Patient, Resource 4, Safe Place 2, Taste (Culinary)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 6 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 9 dice; 9-again]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Profiling; <b>Frailty:</b> Control Freak<br /> <br /> <b>Profiling:</b> Roll Intelligence + Empathy, contested by the victim\u2019s Manipulation + Subterfuge if they are actively attempting to conceal their motives or disguise their nature. Predict the victim\u2019s actions; they win ties in contested rolls against them, may raise Initiative one higher than the target\u2019s Initiative result at the beginning of combat. If able to spend an entire scene socially interacting with the target before making a roll, the ripper learns one unique trait: Virtue, Vice, Integrity or Willpower rating, Conditions suffered, Endowments, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Control Freak:</b> Whenever a Virtuoso fails on an Intelligence-based roll, or on a roll using one of the Skills bolstered by their Undertaking, they lose two points of Willpower.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nest: The Golden Empress</span></b><br /> The Golden Empress is a sparkling clean upscale Asian restaurant that serves authentic Chinese cuisine, westernized Chinese cuisine, and adventurous fusion offerings. Behind a hidden door in the basement, there is a room dedicated to processing human flesh. If ever discovered, the hidden room will appear as perfectly mundane prep kitchen without a hint of its true purpose. No one that works there has any idea of what has been going on. Characters that get belligerent can expect to have the police notified and be escorted off the property with legal action to follow.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Escape Hatch, Innocent Facade*<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Innocent Facade:</b> To casual observation, a Safe Place with Innocent Facade appears perfectly normal, with not even a hint of anything unusual happening. Any attempts to Investigate or use abilities to detect criminal, supernatural or otherwise unusual activity suffer a penalty equal to dots purchased in the Merit.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mystery Cult: The Banquet Society</span></b><br /> The secret circle of epicureans that would become the Banquet Society first gathered in 1896 in Paris, France. The initial members were wealthy merchants and business men who had traveled across France\u2019s colonial holdings and inspired each other with their tales of culinary adventure. Together they organized great feasts of crocodile, elephant, zebra, and other exotic animals. These early meals were not particularly well prepared, but the quality increased as the members hired professional chefs and expert cooks of all stripes to prepare their meals. This eventually became a secret society of the wealthy and well connected, and increasingly decadent as time wore on. The modern Banquet Society only gathers once or twice each year. These gatherings typically offer other hedonistic pleasures such as orgies or narcotics, but the center piece is always food. It is always a gourmet experience, and bragging rights go to the host that can procure the rarest, most endangered, or most taboo ingredients (some degree of cannibalism is almost expected at a successful soiree).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Purpose:</b> To taste the rarest and most forbidden of culinary delights.<br /> <b>Relic:</b> The Gourmand\u2019s Carver \u2013 A steel carving knife with a wooden handle stained black. It is rumored to impart an almost addictive savor to meat dishes prepared with it.<br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> The Banquet Society gather to show off their wealth and taste by flouting moral and ethical standards of dining. Most commonly this is eating endangered species, but can also include consuming plants and animals that are dangerous if not prepared correctly, and occasional cannibalism.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation Benefits</b><br /> \u25cf - <b>The First Taste.</b> The even be invited to a Banquet Society soiree, one must be well-connected. You gain a dot in the Allies (Wealthy Patrons) merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - <b>Epicurean.</b> You have eaten meals with ingredients others might find...distasteful. You gain a dot in the Tolerance for Biology merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - <b>Gourmand.</b> Your appetite has few limits. Gain the Vice-Ridden merit. The second Vice must be related to lust,, gluttony, or some other form of hedonistic excess.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - <b>Celebrity Chef.</b> No longer content to merely consume, you participate by preparing meals or sourcing ingredients. You gain a dot of Crafts and a Crafts specialty in \u201cCulinary Arts\u201d OR you gain a dot of the Contacts merit (exotic ingredients) and the Fixer merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf -<b> Restaurateur.</b> You become responsible for organizing events, protecting the privacy, of your guests, and making sure each event is grander than the last. Your extensive web of connections grants you three dots of Allies among the \u201cDecadent Elite\u201d of society. In addition, you may call upon your influence to make a Resources \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 purchase once per month without limitation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Relic: The Gourmand\u2019s Carver</b></span><br /> The Gourmand\u2019s Carver is a blade that dates back to France in the late 1800\u2019s. The blade is a steel carving knife with a wooden handle stained nearly black with use, but is in otherwise good condition. The Gourmand\u2019s Carver grants its equipment bonus to rolls involving cooking and food preparation. The Carver was last seen in the personal kitchen tools of a chef who uses the carver during special private engagements.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Damage:</b> +0L <b>Initiative:</b> -1 <b>Strength:</b> 1 <b>Size:</b> 1 <b>Durability:</b> 4 <b>Tags:</b> Piercing 1 <b>Availability:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>Powers</b><br /> <b>Carnivorous Appetite:</b> When Hell\u2019s Kitchen is activated, for the following [10-Integrity] days, the user becomes wholly carnivorous and cannot take any sustenance from fruits, grains, or vegetables. Attempting to consume such fare inflicts the Sick (Moderate) Tilt. The user will even find meats that are cooked through distasteful and will show a preference for rarer cuts.<br /> <br /> <b>Craftsmanship:</b> The Carver is sturdy, well balanced, and honed to a razors edge. This grants the object an additional point of Durability and the Piercing 1 tag.<br /> <br /> <b>Hell\u2019s Kitchen:</b> When the Carver is used to slice and prepare meats, it can impart an almost otherworldly savor to the taste when that meat is consumed. Whenever the knife is used to prepare a dish made primarily of meat, the wielder may spend a point of Willpower to enhance the flavor to an addictive degree. Anyone that partakes of this meal must make Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance roll, or begin to crave meat prepared by the Carver, and will gain the <i>Deprived </i>Condition after [Integrity] days unless the craving is satisfied. The user is not immune to this effect. Fasting for 3 days, subsisting only on water, removes this curse.<br /> <br /> <b>Relic Weapon:</b> Damage dealt by the Gourmand\u2019s Carver is considered supernatural damage.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 06-03-2022, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T17:34:11-07:00","id":1482687,"title":"","content":"A friendly reminder that this thread is being watched with great interest, not just being spoken into the void.<br /> <br /> The Flesh Stealer is interesting - a cross of Slashers with Blood Bathers &amp; Beasts is so obvious in hindsight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T20:11:18-07:00","id":1482890,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Banquet Society is a perfect place for a changeling of the Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue to get tangled in, or a place for one to lose Clarity as their prestige rises. That will be a pretty terrifying surprise to someone who learns who acts as a sous chef for the slasher.<br /> <br /> Regarding the merit itself, what does it provide at five dots alongside the obligation, expectation and prestige? Does it grant the Luxury merit as a reward to those who tantalize with sumptuous feasts? Perhaps 3 dots in Allies, Retainer or Resources so they have everything needed to procure the finest ingredients? Perhaps 3 dots of Contacts with a notable culinary spirit group ? After all, wendigos know how to hunt the most dangerous prey and spirits of gastronomy know where the greatest ingredients can be found, and spirits are known to be sane and reasonable, right ? &quot;You might need to capture a mortal supernatural to trade with a grower at the Goblin Market, but the risk is worth it for the finest ingredients&quot;. Lastly, the Eaters of the Dead have their own Cuisine, so perhaps they would be available contacts.<br /> <br /> The possibilities just grows more unnerving the more you think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T18:09:00-07:00","id":1482997,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback! As long as even one of these ideas can be used or provide some inspiration, then I am pleased.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: The Banquet Society </b><br /> <br /> Good catch! I didn't even notice I had left out the mystery cult benefit for the five-dot level. I have updated it above. I went with Allies and wealth as the bonus. My idea for this cult is that they are the worst kind of greedy, jaded and selfish, but are grotesquely mortal. they don't need any supernatural influence to be complete monsters. That being said, having them making meals of Hedge Fruit, vampire blood and ghost plasm does open up some very cool plot ideas!<br /> <br /> time for more slashers<br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Gravedigger</span></b><br /> The man called \u201cThe Gravedigger\u201d lives in an old house squatting on a hill overlooking a large property with a large collection of rusted and broken vehicles and several acres of crops. The house and property serve as a focal point of the local community, who have long since abandoned conventional religion to worship the God of the Good Earth. The Gravedigger is their favored servant. Made strong by the will of the God he provides the flesh and blood that must be interred in the soil to keep the crops growing, and the God of the Good Earth appeased.<br /> The Gravedigger is nearly 7 ft. tall and weighs over 300lbs. His craggy face is scarred and his eyes are dark. He wears a denim coverall and a hooded coat.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Brute;<b> Virtue:</b> Faithful;<b> Vice:</b> Territorial<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To serve the will of the God of the Good Earth.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Gravedigger must bury his victims in fields that produce crops<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2(Dogs), Athletics 2(Endurance), Brawl 3, Crafts 3, Firearms 2(Rifle), Intimidate 3, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Occult 2, Stealth 2, Survival 2 (Hunting), Weaponry 3 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Damnable Certainty, Danger Sense,<span style=\"font-size:10px\"> Defensive Combat (Brawl), </span>Hands of a Killer, Hardy 2, Mystery Cult Initiation (The Harvesters) 4, Professional Training 3 (Laborer; Athletics, Crafts, Survival), Safe Place 2 (The Old House), Trained Observer<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Armor:</b> 1/0 [Reinforced Clothing], <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> Farming Tools [+1L melee, -2 Initiative; 9 dice, Improvised]<br /> Shovel [+1L melee;-3 Initiative; 8 dice; Knockdown]<br /> Rifle [+4L ranged; -5 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Unstoppable <b>Frailty:</b> Tunnel Vision<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable:</b> A Brute never suffers wound penalties for any reason, and automatically passes any roll to remain conscious due to damage or pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Tunnel Vision:</b> A Brute suffers a \u22123 penalty to all Perception rolls, and to rolls to avoid being surprised in combat.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nest: The Old House</span></b><br /> The Old House is a large multi-bedroom home that could have once be rightly called a mansion. It has since fallen into a state of disrepair, with broken and boarded windows, faded paint, a yard overgrown with weeds. A pack of large dogs patrol the property, and become aggressive towards anyone they do not recognize. The broken and rusted husks of old vehicles litter the property and acres of crops occupy the surrounding fields. Despite the disrepair of the estate, the crops are healthy and well-maintained.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Arsenal, Home Security<br /> <b>Tilts:</b> Foreboding<br /> <b>Traps:</b> Guard Animals<br /> <br /> <b>Foreboding (Environmental):</b> There is a lingering, wrongness about the Old House and the surrounding land, filling trespassers with unease and dread. Any mortal individual who enter the location must make a Resolve + Composure roll or gain the Spooked Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Guard Animals:</b> The Safe Place is patrolled by animals, typical trained guardians or feral creatures that consider the Safe Place their territory, that will attack any intruders. Animals that detect intruders also make enough noise to alert the owners of the property to the presence of unwanted guests. Guard Animals make attacks and perception rolls with a dice pool of twice the dots purchased in the Merit and use Down and Dirty combat rules. All other rolls use a die pool equal to the dots purchased in the Merit.<br /> Trigger: Failed rolls against the Home Security feature. Alerted Guard Animals may be avoided with a Stealth roll, scared off with Intimidate, talked-down with Animal Ken, or defeated in combat. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mystery Cult: The Harvesters</b></span><br /> There are lonely places throughout the American mid-west. Rural, sparsely populated places that have been fading for generations, but are not yet gone. Dark tales of tales of moral, physical and even spiritual decay surround such places, told by tavern patrons and whispered around campfire. Most of these stories are fabrications, fueled by persistent stereotypes about rural degenerates. But some of them are true.<br /> It was during the 1930\u2019s, in the throes of the Great Depression. Farm after farm failed as the Dust Bowl throttled the life out of many farming communities. Many families left to find better opportunities, others stayed. Some that stayed grew desperate and seek other ways to survive when conventional prayer has fallen on deaf ears. It is not known if the people found the God of the Good Earth, or if the God of the Good Earth found them. What is known is a deal was struck; Life for your Crops, Life for your People. Blood for the God. And so it has continued. To ensure the land remains fertile and the animals healthy, sacrifices are offered, buried alive or dead in the fields. Most the time, these sacrifices are unlucky travelers or nosy officials. Occasionally, Harvesters will make a \u201chunting trip\u201d to a nearby city, and in lean years, they will offer one of their own.<br /> Even stranger, the occasional outsider will hear the \u201cVoice of the Good Earth\u201d, and join the community willingly, thus ensuring strong bloodlines and more sacrifices for generations to come.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Purpose:</b> To offer sacrifices to the God of the Good Earth, ensuring health and prosperity for the land and those who dwell upon it.<br /> <b>Relic:</b> The Book of the Good Earth. A thick piecemeal journal, passed from leader to leader, that chronicles community events and details the scripture, rites and rituals of the God of the Good Earth.<br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> The beliefs of the Harvesters are a strange synthesis of Christian, Pagan, and stranger occult practices. The God of the Good Earth makes its will felt through a chosen prophet, who is typically the leader of the community, and most members of the congregation are zealous in their devotion.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation Benefits</b><br /> \u25cf - All who follow the God of the Good Earth know their scripture. They gain an Occult specialty in &quot;Book of the Good Earth&quot;<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - The Harvesters are attuned to the land. They gain the Direction Sense Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - The Harvesters must be prepared to do violence in the name of God of the Good Earth. They gain a dot of Weaponry.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Some among the Harvesters see the signs and hear the voice of God of the Good Earth. They gain the Omen Sensitivity Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - There are leaders among the Harvesters, who direct the congregation and convey the will of God of the Good Earth. They gain the Inspiring Merit.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T18:14:28-07:00","id":1482998,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Hammer</span></b><br /> No one is certain what could have happened that turned Jennifer Kane into a killer. Her life until that point had been fairly typical for a middle class woman with no prior history of violence, abuse or trauma. Then one morning she crushed her husband\u2019s skull with a sledge hammer while he slept. Even when arrested she gave no reasoning or alibi for her crime other than \u201cIt had to be done\u201d. Prison psychologists theorize that Jennifer is operating under the delusion that some individuals \u201cneed\u201d to die to prevent some apocalyptic event from occurring. She served several years of her sentence, becoming increasingly uncommunicative as time wore on. While being transported to a different prison, she snapped her restraints and attacked the driver, causing the bus to crash. She escaped in the ensuing chaos. Jennifer is currently at large, and seems to have vanished into the city\u2019s transient and homeless population. Where once her violence was considered an isolated incident, bodies with their heads dashed in have begun appearing with alarming frequency.<br /> Jennifer is a woman of above average height with a stocky build, brown hair, and blue eyes. She dresses simply in jeans, flannel shirts, and sturdy boots.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Mask; <b>Virtue:</b> Patient; <b>Vice:</b> Dispassionate<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Prevent the Apocalypse<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Jennifer kills by blunt trauma to the head, and prefers to use heavy sledges and hammers<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Athletics 2 (Lifting), Brawl 5, Drive 2, Intimidation 3 (Silent), Streetwise 2, Survival 2 (Squatter), Stealth 3(Urban),Weaponry 5 (Hammer)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Area of Expertise (Hammer), Damnable Certainty, Face in the Crowd, Professional Training 2 (Vagrant; Survival, Streetwise), Style: Heavy Weapons 3<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 3, <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 10 dice]<br /> Sledgehammer [+3L melee; -4 Initiative; 11 dice; Knockdown, Stun]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Killing Machine <b>Frailty:</b> Only the Kill<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Jump Scare, Predator\u2019s Sense (the Marked), Regenerate<br /> <br /> <b>Killing Machine:</b> Like a Brute, a Mask does not suffer wound penalties and passes rolls to remain conscious due to damage or pain. Additionally, the Mask does not need to sleep or eat, and only suffers a single point of damage from any attack regardless of the damage or number of successes. This applies to mundane and supernatural forms of attack; only environmental damage such as fire, electrocution, or falling bricks applies damage normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Only the Kill:</b> A Mask has lost the ability to communicate. They are illiterate and are limited to simple gestures or grunts. To understand what\u2019s been said to them, they must succeed at an Intelligence + Composure roll.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T17:21:24-07:00","id":1483087,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to make a request ? This slasher is a musician who carves instruments from the victim's bones and flesh, dedicating them with occult ceremonies and inscribing binding runes upon them. They trap the souls using a corrupted version of the Ghost Binding Ceremony and build a secret conservatory that has everything from pipe organs to zithers. They are the grand maestro of the orchestra. Each performance is both hauntingly beautiful and carries a tone of urgent panic.<br /> <br /> The mystery cult believes that the end of all existence attempts to encroach upon us each day, but only those who know the signs can see it. More importantly, only those with the right kind of musical instruments, properly tuned to the different resonances of the <i>musica universalis</i> have any chance of driving it back. In their minds, no act can be as vile as the bone chilling horrors they have seen from the void.<br /> <br /> So in short, the idea is inspired by <i>The Music of Erich Zann </i>(the instruments are inspired by SCP-2678), normally they would be a Conspiracy, but they are so out of their depth fighting Abyssal incursions that only a slasher is ruthless enough to lead them, because most others break much faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-04-2022, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T20:51:04-07:00","id":1483100,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: The Musician </b><br /> I don't normally take requests, but your suggestions spark some strong ideas. It may take a few days to workshop, but I can probably squeeze a Slasher, Mystery Cult, Relic, and Nest out of this!<br /> <br /> And here are today's set. <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Handsome Devil</span></b><br /> He looks like a model and dresses like a rockstar, and can either the life of the party or the man who is too cool for the room. He is witty, and charming, confident without being arrogant, and effortlessly fashionable. He has a knack for talking his way into the good graces of nearly anyone he meets. All of this hides a deadly narcissist who will do whatever it takes to support his lavish lifestyle, including murder. He has left a trail of lies, abandoned aliases, and cold corpses in his wake. He is a fit and stunningly handsome man in early thirties, with dark hair and deep, dark eyes. He changes his look frequently, but is always impeccably stylish.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Desirable; <b>Vice:</b> Vanity<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Take the Life I Want<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Earn the victim\u2019s trust before the kill<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1(Well Read), Athletics 2, Computers 2, Crafts 1 (Fashion), Drive 2, Empathy 4 (Confidant), Larceny 2 (Forgery), Firearms 3, Persuasion 4(Seduction), Socialize 3, Stealth 3(Sneak Away), Streetwise 2(Parties), Subterfuge 4(Disguise, Lying), Weaponry 2 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Alternate Identity 2, Anonymity 3, Barfly, Hands of a Killer, Language (Spanish), Professional Training 3(Con Artist; Persuasion, Subterfuge, Streetwise), Resources 2, Striking Looks 2 (Glamorous), Style: Fast Talking 5, Taste (Fashion)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 3 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Caught In A Lie)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T20:56:07-07:00","id":1483101,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Hell\u2019s Belle</b></span><br /> As the story goes, a young woman was stranded on the side of a lonely desert road, her car broken down and the nearest town a few hours away. While trying to flag down help, she was instead set upon by a roving gang of criminals, who kidnapped her and spent days abusing and torturing her before leaving her for dead. But she survived her ordeal and gained a burning desire for revenge. One by one, she tracked down and killed each one of her assailants, before vanishing into the night behind the wheel the gangs leader\u2019s GTO. She is still out there, they say. Prowling the night, seeking the sort of men that have committed acts of violence and cruelty against women. While her goals are sympathetic, her methods are brutal and sadistic. She prefers to use a heavy revolver and stained baseball bat, but will use any tool necessary to enact her revenge. The Belle is a tall, athletic, beauty with cropped black hair and green eyes. Her flesh is crisscrossed with raised scars that seem to accentuate her looks. Her clothing is rugged jeans and tee shirts and she sports a silver crucifix, stained with so much blood it appears red. She wanders the roadways of the southwest in a black Pontiac GTO.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Legend; <b>Virtue:</b> Survivor; <b>Vice:</b> Vengeful<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Seek Revenge upon \u201cBad Men\u201d<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Belle can be summoned by women to seek vengeance against men that have wronged them.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Crafts 2, Drive 3 (Muscle Cars), Firearms 3 (Revolver), Intimidate 3(Men), Investigate 2, Stealth 2, Streetwise 2, Weaponry 3(Clubs)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Crack Driver 2, Damnable Certainty, Iron Stamina 2, Iron Will, Striking Looks 2 (Dangerous Beauty)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 4, <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 8, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Baseball Bat [+1L melee;-1 Initiative; 8 dice]<br /> Heavy Revolver [+2L ranged;-2 Initiative; 9 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Living Legend (Abusive Men) <b>Frailty:</b> Narrative Chains (Cannot harm a Woman)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Predator\u2019s Sense (Abusive Men), Surprise Entrance, Unholy Prowess (Strength)<br /> <br /> <b>Living Legend:</b> Once per scene, when someone fulfills one of the tenets of the Legend\u2019s \u201crules,\u201d the player can roll the slasher\u2019s chosen Attribute + Occult. Successes on this roll may be applied on one of the following: restoring spent Willpower, healing damage (one success for a bashing wound, two for lethal, three for aggravated), or applying the bonuses to rolls in pursuit of their goal. After this has been activated, successes that haven\u2019t been spent are discarded. They may not be banked to use in a following scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Narrative Chains:</b> The Legend gains a unique and specific frailty enforced by the nature of the tales surrounding them. Additionally, characters investigating the scourge\u2019s Tell gain an exceptional success on three successes rather than five.<br /> <br /> <b>Pontiac GTO:</b> The Hell\u2019s Belle drives a souped up black muscle car that shows the dents and scratched paint of multiple vehicular altercations. She may use Living Legend to repair damage to this vehicle.<br /> <b>Dice Modifier:</b> -2, <b>Size:</b> 12, <b>Durability/Structure:</b> 3/15, <b>Speed:</b> 110, <b>Availability:</b> 2<br /> <b>*Modifications:</b> High Acceleration (gain 10 Speed per turn)<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Prowess:</b> The creature is quicker, stronger and hardier than it looks. The creature adds one dot of Strength, Dexterity or Stamina per dot of Unholy Prowess.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 06-08-2022, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T07:56:17-07:00","id":1483374,"title":"","content":"a few for today <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Innocent</span></b><br /> Ashley Chase is a young woman who has been plagued by tragedy her entire life. From her sister\u2019s suicide, to the botched robbery that ended the lives of her parents, to the accidental overdose that killed her grandmother, she has faced this adversity with bravery, good cheer, and faith. Of course, she has been quietly behind each of these incidents, growing bolder and more inventive with her plans as time goes by. She has cultivated a group of friends that share a taste for true crime and other macabre fare, who she hasn\u2019t grown bored with yet. Her appreciable inheritance has allowed her to begin college with few concerns about tuition, and she has plans to join a sorority. Once she is more educated (both academically and practically), she will resume her \u201chobby\u201d in earnest.<br /> Ashley is a slender brunette with blue eyes, who dresses in a fashionable if somewhat conservative manner. She plays the part of a cheerful and pious young woman, and keeps her darker interests a well-guarded secret.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Virtuoso; <b>Virtue:</b> Cautious; <b>Vice:</b> Spoiled<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Getting Away with Murder<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Ashley targets those that get close to her and uses their deaths to garner sympathy from new victims.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2 (Law), Athletics 1, Computers 2, Empathy 4, Expression 2 (Acting), Investigation 4 (Crime Scene), Larceny 3 (Plant Evidence), Occult 1, Persuasion 3 (Sympathy), Socialize 2, Stealth 2, Subterfuge 4 (Alibi), Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Cover Up, Cover Tracks, Eidetic Memory, Hobbyist Clique (True Crime; Investigation), Resources 3, Striking Looks 1 (Innocent), Style: Fast Talking 2, Table Turner, Tight-Lipped, Sympathetic, Untouchable<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 2 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 4 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Profiling; <b>Frailty:</b> Control Freak<br /> <br /> <b>Profiling:</b> Roll Intelligence + Empathy, contested by the victim\u2019s Manipulation + Subterfuge if they are actively attempting to conceal their motives or disguise their nature. Predict the victim\u2019s actions; they win ties in contested rolls against them, may raise Initiative one higher than the target\u2019s Initiative result at the beginning of combat. If able to spend an entire scene socially interacting with the target before making a roll, the ripper learns one unique trait: Virtue, Vice, Integrity or Willpower rating, Conditions suffered, Endowments, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Control Freak:</b> Whenever a Virtuoso fails on an Intelligence-based roll, or on a roll using one of the Skills bolstered by their Undertaking, they lose two points of Willpower.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T08:11:48-07:00","id":1483375,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Kill Doll</span></b><br /> Posie Clarkson had always been fascinated by crime, particularly lurid tales of serial killers and murderous cults. Instead of being figures of revulsion, Posie came to regard such killers as heroes and role models. These dark obsessions became reoccurring motifs in her work as a photographer and film maker. When an acquaintance told her of websites on the so-called \u201cdark web\u201d that streamed snuff footage of actual murder, she was hooked. So much so, the only way to get closer to the action was to make her own content. Now known as \u201cKill Doll\u201d, she has has become a \u201cmurder-streamer\u201d displaying footage of her kills to an exclusive audience that must download a special app and bypass several layers of security before being allowed access to the stream. She has even gathered a coterie of ardent followers and employs several \u201cassistants\u201d that want to get closer to the action. As Kill Doll, Posie dresses in provocative, fetish-style outfits that balance sex appeal with freedom of motion. She always wears a full leather or latex mask to hide her true identity. Behind the mask is an attractive Caucasian woman of above average height in her late twenties with blond hair and blue eyes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer;<b> Virtue:</b> Inspired; <b>Vice:</b> Deviant<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> to show her \u201cart\u201d to the world<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Murders must have an audience<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 5, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Computers 3 (Dark Web), Crafts 2 (Electronics, Restraints), Expression 3 (Video), Investigation 3, Persuasion 2, Stealth 3 (Ambush), Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 3 (Knives, Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 3 (Wealthy Patrons), Alternate Identity 2,Contacts 2 (Dark Web),<span style=\"font-size:10px\"> Defensive Combat (Weaponry),</span> Fighting Finesse (Knives), Hands of a Killer, Language (German), Mystery Cult 4 (The Network), Professional Training 3 (Artist; Crafts, Expression, Weaponry), Resources 3, Staff 2 (Accomplices), Striking Looks 2 (Sex Appeal)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 2 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee, - 1 Initiative; 8 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Criticizing her \u201cArt\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mystery Cult: The Network</span></b><br /> There are persistent rumors that in the deepest recesses of so-called \u201cDark Web\u201d special sites and peer-to-peer networks that offer \u201cRed Room\u201d content. In at least one instance, the rumors are true. A criminal organization known only as \u201cThe Network\u201d provides such content. What started as an operation that traded in illegal snuff films on 8mm film transitioned to video, and evolved with the digital age. Now using a highly encrypted peer-to-peer platform, The Network provides \u201csnuff\u201d footage of violent acts,, from animal cruelty, to torture, to murder,, either recorded or streamed live during special shows (with encrypted currency transfers for \u201ctips\u201d). Needless to stay, several government agencies in the United States and internationally are pursuing the people behind the Network, but thus far have been unable discover their true identities.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Purpose:</b> To make a profit from extreme, illegal content.<br /> <b>Relic:</b> Erebus v.404; a program that grants access to an encrypted peer-to-peer streaming platform.<br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> The Network, in addition to its snuff content, provides support and resources for murder, ranging from one-time assassinations to evidence-removal services for serial killers. While it is rumored that The Network was established by organized crime or wealthy degenerates, its true origins are unknown. <br /> <br /> <b>Initiation Benefits</b><br /> \u25cf -<b> Viewer.</b> Those who discover or are invited to The Network are drawn in by the extreme content, typically out of morbid curiosity, and quickly become desensitized to the cruelty and violence on display. They gain the Tolerance for Biology Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - <b>Subscriber.</b> Regular subscribers log in routinely, following their favorite performers and becoming familiar with the online names of other regular posters. They gain a dot in the Contacts (The Network Community) Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - <b>Patron.</b> Patrons dedicate significant resources to The Network, and are willing to perform the occasional \u201cfavor\u201d for increase their standing in the community. They gain a dot in the Allies (The Network) Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - <b>Content Creator.</b> No longer content to merely observe; content creators actively contribute content and provide services to The Network, and are compensated for their efforts.<br /> They gain three dots that may be distributed between the following Merits; Allies (The Network), Cover Up, Resources, Untouchable<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf -<b> Admin.</b> Admins are privy to the secrets behind The Network, and are sworn to utmost secrecy and discretion. The powers behind The Network are all wealthy, influential, and will not hesitate to make problem individuals \u201cdisappear\u201d. Members at this level practice utmost secrecy, gaining 3 dots in the Alternate Identity or Anonymity Merit.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T08:24:35-07:00","id":1483379,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Kind Fellow</span></b><br /> The Kind Fellow considers what he does to be a higher calling. To those that are in pain and suffer, he frees them from this life to continue on to a better place. He moves from place to place, adopting new names and using false documents to gain employment. He prefers to work in hospitals, retirement homes, and hospices, typically as a nurse, orderly, or even janitor. He ingratiates himself to the patient, subtly convincing them that death is the only way out. He prefers to kill using gentler methods, such as suffocation or poison, but will strangle if necessary. The Kind Fellow sees stabbing and bludgeoning as needlessly cruel, and will rarely employ these methods.<br /> \u201cThe Kind Fellow\u201d is a pleasant faced, slightly balding, dark haired man in his mid-forties. He has a stout build, but cultivates a paunchy physique to appear less intimidating. He changes hair style or sports glasses or other accessories to conceal his true identity.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Compassionate; <b>Vice:</b> Conniving<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Help the Sick and Injured<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Kind Fellow becomes agitated and violent when someone refuses his \u201ckindness\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Brawl 3(Grapple, Suffocate), Crafts 2, Empathy 3, Medicine 2 (Poison), Persuasion 3 (Hospital Patients), Politics 1 (Bureaucracy), Science 1, Socialize 2, Stealth 2, Subterfuge 3 (Disguise), Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Alternate Identity 2, Choke Hold, Closed Book 2, Cover Tracks, Damnable Certainty, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Face in the Crowd, Language (Spanish), Professional Training 2 (Orderly; Brawl, Medicine), Sympathetic<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 5, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Poison [See Description]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming;<b> Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Rebuking his \u201cKindness\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.<br /> <br /> <b>Poison:</b> The Kind Fellow often uses poison and high doses of medication to incapacitate or kill his victims. In combat, he prefers chloroform or other chemicals that can be applied to a struggling victim, applying the <i>Drugged</i> or <i>Insensate</i> Tilt. Outside of combat, he prefers more deadly substances, typically a Toxicity 4 poison that deals damage each minute until the victim accumulates a total of 4 successes on the resistance rolls.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T18:52:20-07:00","id":1483670,"title":"","content":"Here is today's set. <hr /><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Marked</span></b><br /> Debra Stroud had lived a good, if mundane life. She was a single mother who struggled to make ends meet for her and her son. She eventually found love and was looking forward to starting a family with her fiance. All of that changed during a weekend camping trip. During that weekend, while hiking through the woods, Debra walked into a clearing and disappeared in a flash of blinding light. She was found three days later and ten miles away, rambling incoherently, naked except for the strange symbols burned into her body. Except for her head, hands, and feet, these symbols cover every inch of her flesh. She remembered nothing of the time between her disappearance and reappearance. As time passed, she became more and more obsessed with deciphering the meaning of her burn marks, and started to developed a strange cosmology to make sense of it all. She concluded that she was chosen to be a prophet of deity she calls the Great Machine. Her increasing obsession and zeal has alienated her loved ones, with her fiance leaving her and her son sent to live with relatives.<br /> She is compelled by visions to reclaim the Great Machine\u2019s power from those that are unworthy; targeting mediums, psychics, occultists, and similar \u201cgifted\u201d individuals. Only individuals that could be considered mortal are chosen as victims; creatures that no longer fit that definition escape her attention.<br /> Debra is a tall, blond Caucasian woman in her mid-thirties. Once she carried a bit of extra weight, but an intense exercise regimen has given her a lean, athletic physique. She keeps her hair cropped close and dresses in rugged, functional clothing. Her body is covered with faded burn scars that appear to be occult symbols branded into her flesh. It takes considerable effort for her to restrain herself from speaking about the Great Machine, and she is always on the lookout for the next sacrifice.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Hypno; <b>Virtue:</b> Inquisitive; <b>Vice:</b> Zeal<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To reclaim the power of the Great Machine from the \u201cunworthy\u201d<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Marked cuts symbols into the bodies of her victims.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3 (Running), Brawl 2 (Restrain), Computers 2, Empathy 2, Investigation 3 (Public Records), Larceny 2 (Escape), Medicine 2, Occult 3 (Supernaturally Gifted Mortals), Socialize 2, Stealth 3, Streetwise 2, Weaponry 3 (Blades)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Damnable Certainty, Danger Sense, Gut Feeling, Iron Will, Relentless, Striking Looks 1 (Marked Flesh), Style: Light Weapons 2<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 2, <b>Willpower: </b>10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 5 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> Machete [+2L melee;-2 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling Words; <b>Frailty:</b> Can\u2019t Let Go<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Glitch 2, Predator\u2019s Sense (Supernaturally Gifted Mortals)<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling Words:</b> When making a Social roll of any kind to get a target to drop their guard for a moment or to heed the slasher\u2019s words, the Hypno treats any success as an exceptional success. If using this moment to get close to the target and attack them, the scourge treats the victim as vulnerable to a Killing Blow, dealing damage equal to their dice pool for the attack plus any bonus for a weapon, with no roll required. If using this to demoralize or sow doubt in a target\u2019s mind, the scourge can instead drain a point of Willpower from the victim to regain it; they cannot drain Willpower from a target more than once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Can\u2019t Let Go:</b> Whenever a Hypno experiences a failure on a Social roll against a target she intends to kill, she becomes absolutely obsessed with the desired victim. She loses a point of Willpower at the end of every scene wherein she does not directly attempt to torment or attack the target. This effect ends when the target dies, or if the target manages to inflict damage on the Hypno.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T18:58:05-07:00","id":1483671,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mister Suit</span></b><br /> Mister Suit is a name given to a suspected serial killer by the FBI agents that have been tracking the case for over 15 years. Unlike many such killers, who display obsessive and repetitive behaviors, Mister Suit frequently switches methods and tactics; at different points using blades, guns, strangulation and even explosives to dispatch his victims. Even his choice of victims switches often, as they are merely the medium he uses to challenge the authorities and continue to evade justice. If not for his habit of periodically leaving a witness alive, it is likely his murders would never have been connected to each other. So far 24 known victims have been attributed to Mister Suit.<br /> Mister Suit is described as a tall, athletic man who wears a well-tailored suit (typically black or gray). He sports black gloves and an apron if the work is going to be messy. He always wears a mask; the masks design varies but he seems to favor a rubber gas mask. When confronted, he will engage in verbal sparring with his opponent, as he seems to relish such encounters.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Hypno; <b>Virtue:</b> Clever; <b>Vice:</b> Competitive<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To be the most successful killer that ever lived<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Mister Suit likes novelty; and is always devising different ways to kill<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 5, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Athletics 2(Running), Brawl 3, Computers 2, Crafts 2, Firearms 3(Pistols), Investigation 3, Persuasion 3 (Bribery), Politics 3, Stealth 3 (Evade Capture), Subterfuge 3(Alibi), Streetwise 2, Weaponry 4 (Knives, Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Alternate Identity 2, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Hands of a Killer, Professional Training 3 (Executive; Persuasion, Politics, Subterfuge), Resources 4, Tell Tale Murder, Untouchable<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 4, <b>Willpower:</b> 11<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 6 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 8 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 8 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling Words Frailty: Can\u2019t Let Go<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Glitch 3<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling Words:</b> When making a Social roll of any kind to get a target to drop their guard for a moment or to heed the slasher\u2019s words, the Hypno treats any success as an exceptional success. If using this moment to get close to the target and attack them, the scourge treats the victim as vulnerable to a Killing Blow, dealing damage equal to their dice pool for the attack plus any bonus for a weapon, with no roll required. If using this to demoralize or sow doubt in a target\u2019s mind, the scourge can instead drain a point of Willpower from the victim to regain it; they cannot drain Willpower from a target more than once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Can\u2019t Let Go:</b> Whenever a Hypno experiences a failure on a Social roll against a target she intends to kill, she becomes absolutely obsessed with the desired victim. She loses a point of Willpower at the end of every scene wherein she does not directly attempt to torment or attack the target. This effect ends when the target dies, or if the target manages to inflict damage on the Hypno. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T11:18:19-07:00","id":1483730,"title":"","content":"Mister Suit is especially terrifying, like an Agent 47 that broke and goes to greater extremes to perfect his craft. The ability to get a killing blow will probably be a startling wake up call to many supernaturals:<br /> <br /> &quot;Its fine, I have my mage armor or werewolf regeneration, I can survive one round with him and then nuke him to oblivion&quot;<br /> &quot;Hehehehehe, no !&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyone who lives through that will be heavily traumatized and very paranoid of close quarter communications, made even worse by the facts that they don't know who he is and that he varies his approach each time.<br /> <br /> I can also see the possibility that the exposure to so many types of death and such dedication to it would eventually make the gas mask into a Memento (or perhaps a Greater Memento). Something akin to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MYfxMcIhTl0\" target=\"_blank\">SCP-1499</a>, but with the mask convincing the wearer that the creatures adapt and that a different killing method should be used each time. That way there is always a living successor to the legacy of Mr Suit, someone coached by the artifact into becoming a slasher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T15:37:21-07:00","id":1483818,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Mister Suit</b><br /> Mister Suit was one of my earlier slasher ideas, and I have revised him a few times. I deliberately left his identity unknown so that anyone that uses him can fill in the blanks however they see fit. Personally I portray him as a wealthy executive type that gets his kicks through murder. I do like the idea that mask (or perhaps his iconic suit) become relics that can carry one his murderous ways long after he has finally been taken down.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: The Musician.</b><br /> Posted below are the ideas I was able to spin from the request and suggestions offered by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a>. As always feel free to tweak any details to get closer to what you want. <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Musician</span></b><br /> Esme Valdez was gifted composer and musical prodigy that could expertly play nearly any instrument she touched,and compose musical works of sublime beauty. But rather than becoming a conductor or performer, she immersed herself in understanding the concept of music itself. She studied astronomy, musical history, philosophy, and apprenticed under talented instrument makers of all types. The depths of her obsession led down more esoteric paths, and she become well versed in the occult. During a particularly harrowing encounter, her sense of reality broke, and she perceived of a vast, <i>qlippothic</i> entities waiting on the other side. The protect this world, the most dire of sacrifices must be made. Only a symphony of instruments, each one crafted of bone, blood, and souls, tuned to the different resonances of the <i>musica universalis</i>, stand a chance of driving these beings away. She claims that in quiet moments of contemplation, she can hear the strains of the <i>musica universalis</i>. She also has access to an artifact known as the Wailing Void. She must work quickly, the chance of cosmic scale destruction loom closer each day.<br /> She views the lives she takes to create the instruments as necessary casualties in an existential war. The horrors she is willing to commit are a glimmer compared to the horrors she is desperate to prevent. Esme is charismatic and persuasive, and has recruited others to her cause. Such a monumental task can hardly be done alone.<br /> Esme is a Latina woman in her mid-thirties, with dark, curly hair and a broad smile. Her eyes have a tired, worried cast, and her hands tremble, steadying only when making music (or committing murder). She dresses conservatively and wears overlarge glasses.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Puppeteer; <b>Virtue:</b> Martyr; <b>Vice:</b> Driven<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To prevent the Qlippoth from reaching this reality.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Victims are all talented and accomplished musicians.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2 (Philosophy), Crafts 3 (Instruments), Expression 4 (Music), Firearms 2(Close Range), Medicine 2, Occult 4, Persuasion 3 (Recruit), Science 2 (Astronomy), Socialize 3, Subterfuge 4 (Misdirect), Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Music), *Ceremony (Macabre Instrument), Hardened Exorcist**, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Music), Mystery Cult Initiation (Orchestra of Martyrs) 4, Language (English, French, German, Russian), Professional Training 4 (Musician; Crafts, Expression, Occult), Resources 3, Safe Place 2 (The Conservatory), Taste (Music)<br /> <i>* Geist: The Sin-Eaters 2nd Edition, p. 124</i><br /> <i>**Chronicles of Darkness: Hurt Locker p.74</i><br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 3, <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 8, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 3 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 5 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling <b>Frailty:</b> Falter<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Supernatural Merit (Omen Sensitivity)<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling:</b> A Puppeteer can profile a victim much like a Virtuoso, but additionally benefits from the 8-again quality on any contested roll against a profiled target. They also impose a penalty equal to the scourge\u2019s Intelligence on victims\u2019 rolls to notice traps or react to ambushes set for them in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Falter:</b> Whenever a Puppeteer fails a Social roll, it becomes a dramatic failure.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ceremony: Macabre Instrument</span></b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Requirement:</b> The instrument must be crafted from a freshly slain human corpse, preferably one slain by the ritualist\u2019s own hands.<br /> <b>Subject:</b> One musical instrument.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent until the object is destroyed.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Symbolic writing in a language with occult significance.<br /> <b>Rituals:</b> The instrument, after being anointed with oils and washed in purified water, must be played.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Expression vs. Power +Resistance<br /> Success: If it was not already, the instrument becomes an Anchor for the ghost of the person slain to craft it. The ghost becomes bound to the Anchor, in a state of hibernation. The Anchor becomes a Memento with an innate Key based on the bound ghost\u2019s death and Influences. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mystery Cult: The Orchestra of Martyrs</span></b><br /> The Orchestra of Martyrs are an organization that firmly believes that music is all that stands between existence and oblivion. Their founder, a brilliant composer and occultist named Esme Valdez, after an encounter with beings from beyond this world, developed the ceremonies and rites she believes will come the world safe from the things that dwell beyond. She calls them the Qlippoth, and in her beliefs they crave nothing more than the utter annihilation of all that is. Only the flesh and blood of the sacrificed (willing or otherwise), and the musica universalis can keep these beings at bay. She began assembling a collection of musicals instruments, all of which incorporate human body parts, several of which she created herself. In time she recruited others to help in the task. While the organization is currently small, they are expanding and becoming more aggressive in their pursuits, as if racing against a timetable only they are aware of.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Purpose:</b> To prevent the Qlippoth from reaching this reality.<br /> <b>Relic:</b> The Resonance; a work in progress orchestral composition that channels the musica universalis against the enemies of reality.<br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> The Orchestra of Martyrs believe sincerely that the lives and souls sacrificed in the name of protecting reality are transformed into a resonance that joins with the sublime music of the spheres. They treat all instruments they make or discover as holy relics.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation Benefits</b><br /> \u25cf - Initiates are given an education in deeper musical thought. You gain the \u201cMusic\u201d special in your choice Expression, Occult, or Science.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - Members of the Orchestra of Martyrs are sworn to secrecy. You gain the <i>Tight-Lipped</i> Merit (Hunter: The Vigil, 2nd edition, p. 96)<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Violence is a regretful necessity, and not all sacrifices come willingly. You gain a dot in your choice Brawl, Firearms, or Weaponry.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - You hear the music of the Spheres, and it guides you. You gain the <i>Omen Sensitivity</i> Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Even the founder of the Orchestra of Martyrs has yet to reach this level of power and insight. You are empowered by those sacrificed, gaining three dots of the Sacrificial Offering Merit <i>(Chronicles of Darkness: Hurt Locker p.76)</i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Relic: The Black Note</span></b><br /> The macabre item called The Black Note (also called \u201cThe Wailing Void\u201d) is a flute carved from a human femur, with cryptic engravings, brass fittings, and stained black. The object dates back the Spanish Inquisition in the early 1600\u2019s and is reputed to have come from the body of a suspected witch. The maker of the item is unknown, but the craftsmanship has an exceptional (if somewhat rushed) quality. Despite this, when played it has a crisp tone and is in remarkably good condition despite its age and wear. The Black Note grants a +2 equipment bonus to Expression rolls when being played.<br /> <i>Memento:</i> The Black Note has been touched by the power of death, and resists damage and destruction. It is never damaged by accidents or environmental hazards, has a Durability of 5 and twice its normal Structure. If using <i>Geist: The Sin-Eaters 2nd Edition</i>, The Black Note gives access to the Key of Stillness.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Size:</b> 2 <b>Durability:</b> 5 <b>Availability:</b> 3<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence +Expression \u2013 (higher of the targets Resolve or Stamina)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Success:</b> The flute channels a primeval entropy into the target, causing pain and despair. When the user plays the lowest note, the target is overwhelmed by physical pain and crushing existential despair. Each success on the activation roll inflicts one point of lethal damage to the target and they gain the <i>Stunned</i> Tilt. Targets that cannot hear the note are unaffected.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Black Note inflicts the <i>Immobilized</i> Tilt instead.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The relic does not activate.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Black Note reverberates in the users ears, causing the <i>Deafened</i> Tilt. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T15:49:20-07:00","id":1483820,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Pigman</span></b><br /> No one goes out to the Old Mason Slaughterhouse anymore. Once it shut down and the employees were laid off, the only people out there are Old Man Mason, his son Bobby, and a bunch of hogs. While never particularly bright, Bobby does his best to take care for his father, the property and their pigs. This includes dealing with trespassers. He has already dealt with nosy teenagers and squatters. Now, with the county looking to foreclose on his father\u2019s property, he is preparing a proper welcome for anyone seeking to take their land.<br /> Bobby kills in an unrelenting berserk fury, then feeds whatever is left to the hogs. Whatever shred of compassion remains in his heart, Bobby reserves for his animals. Even when slaughtering one of the hogs, Bobby will try to comfort the beast and is nearly inconsolable afterwards, even while chopping the body into dinner. Bobby also revers his father, who is the only one he truly listens to. He is a dutiful son, who obeys his father and will protect him t all costs. Which is notably odd, considering Old Man Mason passed on several years ago.<br /> Bobby is a large man, with a thick-necked, stocky body layered with slabs of fat and muscle. He is unpleasant looking, with thin lips, beady eyes, a lumpy nose, and greasy, unwashed hair and beard. He wears dirty overalls, and a filthy butcher\u2019s smock. His hygiene is poor, and he reeks of filth and body odor. Strangely, his work boots are new, in good repair, and kept remarkably clean.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Undesirable; <b>Virtue:</b> Dutiful; <b>Vice:</b> Reckless<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Slaughter All Trespassers<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Victims are killed, chopped into pieces, and then fed to hogs.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 2, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure 2<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 3 (Pigs), Athletics 3 (Strong Back), Brawl 3, Crafts 2 (Butcher), Empathy 3 (Detect Lies), Intimidate 3 (Terrifying), Medicine 1, Stealth 2, Survival 2, Weaponry 4 (Meat Cleaver)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Fast Reflexes 2, Iron Stamina 3, Professional Training 2 (Butcher; Crafts, Weaponry), Safe Place 3 (The Slaughterhouse), Striking Looks 1 (Ugly), Style: Berserker 2*, Weaponry Obsession (Meat Cleaver)<br /> <i>* Chronicles of Darkness: Hurt Locker, p. 46-47</i><br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> Meat Cleaver [+2L, -2 Initiative; 10 dice; 8-again]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Natural Compass; <b>Frailty:</b> Rejection<br /> <br /> <b>Natural Compass:</b> An Undesirable has a near-perfect sense of direction, and gains a +3 bonus to Perception, Athletics, Investigation, and Survival rolls when present in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Rejection:</b> The Undesirable suffers a \u22124 penalty on Social rolls that do not involve slashers and other monsters.<br /> <br /> <b>Style: Berserker:</b> The Pigman enters a controlled madness in combat.<br /> \u2022 <i><b>The Red Mist:</b></i> The Pigman focuses inward, seeking out his source of rage within. By spending a point of Willpower he inflicts the Traumatized Tilt on himself for the remainder of the scene.<br /> \u2022<i><b> War Cry:</b></i> The Pigman chills an opponent\u2019s blood with his mad howl. Instead of attacking, roll a contested Strength + Intimidation versus opponent\u2019s Resolve + Composure. If he gets the most successes, his opponent suffers a penalty equal to his successes to any action other than Dodging for the next turn.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: The Slaughterhouse</b></span><br /> The once a bustling slaughterhouse and meat packing plant was closed several years ago due to multiple safety violations, and now the land it rests upon is only months away from foreclosure. Despite having fallen into a state a disrepair, the Slaughterhouse still has all the tools and capability to render living creatures into choice cuts of meat. The farmhouse where the owners reside is a short ways away, and there are several healthy (if semi-feral) hogs in the pens and wandering the property.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Concealed, Home Security, *Maze<br /> <b>Traps:</b> Guard Animals<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Maze:</b> By happenstance or by design, the Safe Place or the surrounding landscape is confusing and difficult to navigate by intruder\u2019s and those unfamiliar with the terrain. Failed rolls against the Concealed or Home Security feature imposes the <i>Lost</i> Condition.<br /> \u2022<i><b> Lost (Condition):</b> </i>Your character has no idea where she is, or how to reach her target. She cannot make any headway toward her goal without first navigating and finding out where she is. This requires a successful Wits + Streetwise action (in the city) or Wits + Survival action (in the wilderness).<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Abandoning the goal, successfully navigating<br /> <br /> <b>Guard Animals:</b> The Safe Place is patrolled by animals, typical trained guardians or feral creatures that consider the Safe Place their territory, that will attack any intruders. Animals that detect intruders also make enough noise to alert the owners of the property to the presence of unwanted guests. Guard Animals make attacks and perception rolls with a dice pool of twice the dots purchased in the Merit and use Down and Dirty combat rules. All other rolls use a die pool equal to the dots purchased in the Merit.<br /> <i>Trigger</i>: Failed rolls against the Home Security feature. Alerted Guard Animals may be avoided with a Stealth roll, scared off with Intimidate, talked-down with Animal Ken, or defeated in combat. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:17:46-07:00","id":1484076,"title":"","content":"New post <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Poisoner</span></b><br /> Mariko Tanaka first learned about poison from her mother, when she used doses of anti-freeze to slowly poison her abusive husband, teaching her at an early age that murder is an acceptable solution to her problems. She grew into a lovely young woman who excelled at school, and demonstrated a particular knack for chemistry. While she displays an interest in true crime and other macabre topics, few would suspect that she routinely \u201cfield tests\u201d any number of poisonous concoctions. At first, she tried to only apply her skills against \u201cthose who deserved it\u201d. But now she is more concerned with accumulating a variety of \u201csubjects\u201d, making note of their symptoms and expiration with cool scientific detachment. She has been very financially successful, and has purchased a remote property that should allow her to continue her research under more controlled conditions.<br /> Mariko is a slender, slightly taller than average Japanese woman in her early-thirties. She charming and funny, and can discuss strange topics in way that feels like perfectly normal conversation. Through this veneer of sociability she is studying her targets like an insect in a jar and is drawn to unusual, exceptional, or eccentric people.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Virtuoso; <b>Virtue:</b> Meticulous; <b>Vice:</b> Deceptive<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To study all the ways a toxin can kill<br /> <b>Tell: </b>Mariko kills with drugs, poison, or some other chemical agent.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3(Research), Athletics 2, Crafts 2, Investigation 2 (Background Check), Larceny 3, Medicine 3 (Poison), Science 5 (Chemistry), Persuasion 2, Socialize 2 (Disarming), Stealth 2 (Ambush), Subterfuge 3, Survival 2 (Foraging), Weaponry 2 (Needles)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Cover Up, Eidetic Memory, Holistic Awareness, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Poison), Language (English, Korean),Professional Training 4(Chemist; Academics, Medicine, Science), Resources 3, Sleight of Hand, Striking Looks 1 (Pretty)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 2 dice]<br /> Pepper Spray [6 dice close range; Stun]<br /> Poison [See Description]<br /> Scalpel [+0L melee, 5 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Profiling; Frailty: Control Freak<br /> <br /> <b>Profiling:</b> Roll Intelligence + Empathy, contested by the victim\u2019s Manipulation + Subterfuge if they are actively attempting to conceal their motives or disguise their nature. Predict the victim\u2019s actions; they win ties in contested rolls against them, may raise Initiative one higher than the target\u2019s Initiative result at the beginning of combat. If able to spend an entire scene socially interacting with the target before making a roll, the ripper learns one unique trait: Virtue, Vice, Integrity or Willpower rating, Conditions suffered, Endowments, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Control Freak:</b> Whenever a Virtuoso fails on an Intelligence-based roll, or on a roll using one of the Skills bolstered by their Undertaking, they lose two points of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Poison:</b> Mariko uses a variety of drugs, poisons, toxins, and venom. She favors custom designed cocktails that can impair, incapacitate, or kill, inflicting the Drugged, Insensate, or Poison (Grave) Tilt. Outside of combat, she uses a deadly formula that induces cardiac arrest and is difficult to trace. This is a Toxicity 6 poison that deals damage each minute until the victim accumulates a total of 6 successes on the resistance rolls.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:30:51-07:00","id":1484079,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Relic Hunter</span></b><br /> Cordelia Martin is driven by a fascination with the strange and obscure. Raised in the antiques business, she has a fine eye for quality and value. Over the years, she has discovered that certain objects carried more esoteric properties, many of which could be considered dangerous or malevolent. She became obsessed with obtaining such objects. At first, she was made a point to secure items before they could cause further harm. Perhaps it was the result of too many violent confrontations over a choice artifact, or perhaps a corrupting influence of the artifacts themselves, but eventually, Cordelia found it easier to simply kill the previous owner than to negotiate with them. She is independently wealthy and is a talented thief; more than capable of securing relics without bloodshed. But she finds that not quite as exciting. By means foul and fair, she has secured a collection of occult objects that other collectors would (and have) died for. She has a journal where she keeps a meticulously inventory of every item in her vault. She also has no probably murdering thieves and treasure hunters attempting to pillage her collection.<br /> Cordelia is a fit and attractive Caucasian woman in her early forties, with dark hair that has started to go stylishly gray. She dresses in a sophisticated fashion, and even her rugged \u201cworking cloths\u201d of dark turtlenecks and denim look expensive.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Prudent; <b>Vice:</b> Covetous<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To obtain mystic relics at any cost.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> She murders anyone that stands between her and her desired objects.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 5, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3 (History), Crafts 1 (Restoration), Firearms 2, Larceny 3 (Theft), Investigation 3, Occult 3 (Relics), Persuasion 3 (Negotiation), Politics 1 (International), Stealth 3, Streetwise 2 (Smugglers), Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 2 (Blades)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Relics), Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Relics), Language (Arabic, Greek, Latin, Others), Professional Training 4 (Antiquarian; Academics, Crafts, Occult), Resources 5, Safe Place 3 (Relic Vault), Striking Looks 1 (Sophisticated), Untouchable<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 2 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> Griswold\u2019s Knife [+1L melee; Initiative -1; 5 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Denied a Relic)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nest: The Relic Vault</span></b><br /> The Relic Vault is a custom built secure location built to protect rare and valuable objects from destruction and theft. From the outside, it is a discrete building with few indications about it\u2019s true purpose. The interior is well appointed, with smooth marble floors and tasteful decorations. The valuables are secured behind heavy steel doors with sophisticated locks and the entire place is protected by state of the art surveillance and security systems.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Concealed, Home Security, Vault*<br /> <b>Traps:</b> Alarm System, Surveillance<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Vault:</b> A Vault is a room or large container designed prevent intrusion and protect valuable goods. Attempts to break into a vault requires an extended Intelligence + Larceny roll with a (2+ dots in the Safe Place Merit) penalty that requires (2x dots in the Safe Place Merit) successes, with an interval of one minute per roll. For attempts to physically break into the vault, the durability of the barrier is (2+ dots in the Safe Place Merit).<br /> <br /> <b>Alarm System:</b> The vault door as a built in alarm. This can be either an audible alert or a silent alarm. Audible alerts cause the Deafened Tilt and make anyone nearby aware of the character\u2019s presence. Silent alarms notify the owner of the property and any relevant security agents.<br /> Trigger: Booby-Trap. A successful Wits + Larceny roll with a -2 penalty avoids to triggering the alarm. Any failed rolls while attempting to breach the vault also triggers the alarm.<br /> <br /> <b>Surveillance:</b> Surveillance cameras at key places are connected to a motion detector. Anyone that activates the camera has their actions observed and recorded for the remainder of the Scene.<br /> <i>Trigger:</i> Motion Detector. A successful Wits + Composure roll with a -3 penalty avoids to triggering the camera. A character may also use Larceny to deactivate the camera, Stealth to avoid the camera, or Subterfuge to hide their identity.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Relic: Griswold\u2019s Knife</span></b><br /> This blade was recovered from the personal items of a suspected serial murderer named Linus Griswold. It is a sturdy hunting knife with a handle carved from deer horn. In 1978, authorities discovered several bodies in the backyard of Griswold\u2019s property in Alberta, Canada while investigating reports that Linus Griswold himself had vanished under mysterious circumstances. The case generated some interest in the tabloids and a brief manhunt for Griswold, who was never found. The knife disappeared from police possession, only to appear as an item of interest in a different murder case several years later, where it again vanished.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Griswold\u2019s Knife is of exceptional quality and is a useful tool in the wilderness. It grants a +1 equipment bonus to Survival rolls. The wielder of the knife cannot voluntarily dispose of the weapon. If separated from it by circumstances outside of their control, they gain the Deprived Condition until they get it back.<br /> <i>Memento:</i> Griswold\u2019s Knife has been touched by the power of death, and resists damage and destruction. It is never damaged by accidents or environmental hazards, has a Durability of 5 and twice its normal Structure. If using <i>Geist: The Sin-Eaters 2nd Edition</i>, Griswold\u2019s Knife gives access to the Key of Blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Damage:</b> +1L, <b>Initiative:</b> -1, <b>Strength:</b> 1, <b>Size:</b> 2 <b>Durability:</b> 5, <b>Availability:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + (Survival or Weaponry)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Once per scene, the wielder of the Knife can apply the Bleeding Tilt when she damages her victim with an attack. In addition, damage dealt by the Griswold\u2019s Knife is considered supernatural damage and can injure ghosts and other such ephemeral beings.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The <i>Bleeding</i> Tilt may apply to creatures normally immune to damage from bleeding or blood loss.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The relic does not activate.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The relic cannot be activated for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b> \u2022<i> Tilt: Bleeding:</i></b><i> The character bleeds profusely from an open wound. If she doesn\u2019t staunch the blood flow, she may soon pass out from shock and blood loss.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Bleeding characters suffer a \u20131 wound penalty (or have existing wound penalties increased in severity by +1). Additionally, each turn that she remains bleeding, she suffers one automatic point of bashing damage.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> If the character takes a turn to apply pressure and some sort of cloth or tie a tourniquet around the bleeding limb, she can stop the flow of blood and end the Tilt. Any form of accelerated healing, even a single point of bashing damage, will stop the bleeding as well. Creature that do not bleed are immune to this tilt.<br /> (Chronicles of Darkness: Hurt Locker p. 143)<br /> </i></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Relic: The Questing Compass</span></b><br /> This rare compass is crafted of brass and glass by expert hands, with thirty-two directional points upon its face, a built in sundial, and fits in the palm of the hand. The item was crafted by an unknown artisan in the mid 1700\u2019s, and despite its age, remains in good condition. The instrument has a colorful history, and is rumored to have passed through the hands of sailors, privateers, pirates and explorers. The needle of the compass points the way towards a person, place or thing that whoever is holding the Compass wishes to locate. The Questing Compass is immune to ordinary wear and tear caused by the passage of time.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Size:</b> 1 <b>Durability:</b> 2,<b> Availability:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + (Investigation or Survival) vs. Resolve + (Larceny or Stealth)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Until the next Sunrise<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The user must speak the name of what they seek; the Compass\u2019s needle will point in the direction of the target until the next sunrise. If the target is making an effort to evade pursuit, they may contest this roll with Resolve + (Larceny or Stealth). Once activated, the Questing Compass grants a +3 bonus to rolls involving locating, researching or pursuing the named target. Attempting to locate targets obscured by supernatural powers triggers a Clash of Wills.<br /> While the Compass is active, it\u2019s user gains the <i>Obsessed</i> Condition regarding the named target. This condition does not resolve until the target is obtained, or a new target is chosen.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> In a Chase scene, the user of the Compass has the Edge if they are pursuing the named target.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The relic does not activate.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The relic doe not activate but the user still gains the <i>Obsessed</i> Condition.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Relic: The Scarab of Ra</span></b><br /> The Scarab of Ra is an amulet of gold sculpted into the shape of a scarab and featuring a single large ruby mounted on the carapace. The amulet is an antique of unknown age but has a distinctly Egyptian style.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The Scarab inspires envy and draw hungry gazes. The possessor of the amulet gains the <i>Hunted</i> Condition, and start to encounter those who want to relieve them of their possession.<br /> <b>Vessel:</b> The Scarab of Ra is imprinted with the mystical energy that flows through all living things. The Scarab immune to ordinary wear and tear caused by the passage of time. Wearing the Scarab refreshes an extra Willpower point after a full night\u2019s sleep. If using <i>Mummy: The Curse 2nd Edition</i>, the Scarab of Ra is a Vestige with a Virtue of Resilient, a Vice of Selfish, and up to three Pillar points.<br /> <br /> <b>Size:</b> 0<b> Durability:</b> 2, <b>Availability:</b> 4<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Occult<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One scene<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Upon activation, the amulet provides 2 armor, which applies to both general and ballistic attacks. This armor also provides a defense against supernatural attacks, giving her a +2 bonus to rolls to contest an action or a +1 to her resistance Attribute when targeted by a Dread Power or supernatural effect. The Scarab also protects against fire. Until the end of the scene, reduce any lethal damage from exposure to heat and flames to bashing.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The duration of the activation extends until the next sunrise.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The relic does not activate.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Scarab of Ra does not activate, and cannot be activated until the next sunrise.<br /> <br /> <i> \u2022 <b>Condition: Hunted [Persistent]:</b> Someone who poses a serious threat to the character\u2019s safety and well-being, physically or emotionally (or both), is after her. They may be intent on direct violence, or simply wish to torment her.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> The character\u2019s persecutors find her.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The character stops her persecutors, either through legal means, changes in lifestyle that deny them access to her, or through more direct means, typically violence.<br /> </i></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T19:05:54-07:00","id":1484082,"title":"","content":"I like how Mementos are peppered across slasher profiles. They're the perfect match for crossovers in hindsight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T12:36:46-07:00","id":1484126,"title":"","content":"I appreciate how the Poisoner is physically weak and doesn't have any kind of naturally built poison resistance. That means that she is vulnerable to a ironic death by the same method.<br /> <br /> The Questing Compass being a combination of Jack Sparrow's compass and the Mao Kun map is pretty cool. Its reliable enough in seeking out the supernatural to foster a dependency on it and it can also be very useful when looking for mundane resources. Being able to push the user to be obsessive and rush into danger can be quite a powerful and subtle curse, yet seemingly manageable enough to tempt those that think they can handle it.<br /> <br /> The Scarab is a pretty good defensive tool, generally versatile without being too strong. It is very good when considering all it uses is one Willpower per scene. Being its owner can't be pleasant, its akin to having the Number Two Headband, it will endlessly draw danger to you, which means either you evolve quickly or you will be annihilated. However, I imagine those that would hunt after it would also be connoisseurs of occult relics, so it works out perfectly for this slasher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-15-2022, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T20:07:20-07:00","id":1484167,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: The Poisoner</b><br /> Glad you like her! I wanted to have a Slasher that wasn't much of a direct combat threat. Even a moderately combat capable character can probably take her down. I would use her as an NPC the players don't discover is a Slasher until much, much too late.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Slasher Mementos</b><br /> While I like the idea of bygones, vessels, and other kinds of magical objects ending up in a Slasher's hands, the vast majority of such objects would probably be Mementos. Slashers are beings so seeped in death and pain it eventually warps them into something inhuman. Their weapons, masks and other regalia are prime to become Mementos. And since sin-eaters can often talk to a Slasher's victims directly, I imagine the Bound frequently end up in pursuit of Slashers.<br /> <br /> a few more for today <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Revenant</b></span><br /> The killer known as a Revenant was once an ordinary person; an artist that made a good living as a painter and graphic designer. That life ended with the death of his partner, murdered by a serial killer. With the authorities seemingly helpless, he took it upon himself to avenge his lover, dedicating every resource and several years to becoming a vigilante determined to enact vengeance upon all such killers, even joining a cell of hunters, and learning that monstrous killers were only the beginning of world\u2019s horrors. With each hunt, they became more violent, more relentless, and more determined to destroy their quarry. During a disastrous mission, he was left for dead at the hands of a supernaturally potent killer. But he rose from the dead three days later, and has began his mission in earnest.<br /> The Revenant focuses his wrath on criminals, killers, and slashers, but has killed law enforcement agents and hunters. Anyone that has taken the life of an innocent is a fair target. He see\u2019s himself as an avenger of the \u201cInnocent\u201d, defining innocence as those that have lived lives of peace and have committed no acts of violence. He has been known to \u201cwarn\u201d people that victimize such innocents, but haven't crossed the line to murder. He is able to tell if a person is \u201cguilty\u201d with a glance, and can make this targets experience crippling guilt and anguish. The Revenant is also seemingly immortal, he as been reported dead multiple times, but always re-appears sometime later to continue his mission.<br /> The Revenant is a handsome, athletic man in his early thirties. His fair skin is as smooth and pale as porcelain and he wears his dark hair long. He dresses in rugged, dark clothing that allow movement and flexibility. He uses whatever weapons are at hand, but prefers to gun down his victims with a heavy revolver. <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Legend; <b>Virtue:</b> Focused;<b> Vice:</b> Merciless<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Vengeance against those that have spilled innocent blood<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Revenant\u2019s victims are all those that have taken lives, whether by deliberately or by accident<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Athletics 4 (Pursuit), Brawl 4 (Armed Opponents), Computer 2, Crafts 2, Expression 3 (Illustration), Firearms 3 (Revolver), Intimidate 3, Investigate 3 (Killers), Occult 2, Stealth 3, Streetwise 2, Weaponry 2 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Damnable Certainty, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Fast Reflexes 2, Hands of a Killer, Professional Training 2 (Artist; Crafts, Expression), Style: Martial Arts 4, Style: Parkour 2, Striking Looks 1 (Handsome)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 3, <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 10, <b>Armor:</b> 1/0 (Reinforced Clothing), <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> Heavy Revolver [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 9 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Living Legend (Spilled Innocent Blood) <b>Narrative Chains</b> (Cannot harm an \u201cInnocent\u201d)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Immortal* (Three Days), Know Soul, Madness and Terror<br /> <br /> <b>Living Legend:</b> Once per scene, when someone fulfills one of the tenets of the Legend\u2019s \u201crules,\u201d the player can roll the slasher\u2019s chosen Attribute + Occult. Successes on this roll may be applied on one of the following: restoring spent Willpower, healing damage (one success for a bashing wound, two for lethal, three for aggravated), or applying the bonuses to rolls in pursuit of their goal. After this has been activated, successes that haven\u2019t been spent are discarded. They may not be banked to use in a following scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Narrative Chains:</b> The Legend gains a unique and specific frailty enforced by the nature of the tales surrounding them. Additionally, characters investigating the scourge\u2019s Tell gain an exceptional success on three successes rather than five.<br /> <br /> <b>Immortal:</b> The creature isn\u2019t bound by mortal laws of life and death. It\u2019s not indestructible, per se, but if it\u2019s killed by anything other than its Bane, it just comes back in a later scene like nothing happened. Even if it\u2019s destroyed with its Bane, it\u2019s never really gone \u2014 some accursed ritual, astrological conjunction, or freak occurrence can always bring the creature back for a sequel story.<br /> <i>[Chronicles of Darkness, pg. 145]<br /> </i></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T20:41:22-07:00","id":1484173,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Rictus Grin</b></span><br /> The killer known as \u201cRictus Grin\u201d appeared first on cryptic video clips posted on internet and dark web forums dedicated to true crime and serial killers. The videos depict a figure wearing a grinning mask, often creeping out of closets or looming over people while they sleep. The authenticity of the clips became a matter of debate and many are still certain the clips are to promote an upcoming horror film of some sort. Some of the videos leaked to the local police and FBI, who discovered that the details of the clips matched with several unsolved murder cases. Since then, new clips regularly appear every few months, each one followed by reports of murder. The person wearing the mask of Rictus Grin has left next to no clues about their true identity, baffling and frustrating law enforcement. Even more upsetting, Rictus Grin seems to have developed a fan following that collects his clips and waits for the next \u201ccontent drop\u201d.<br /> Rictus Grin is a tall, broad shouldered man sporting a black long coat, buttoned to the throat. He wears an apparently hand-crafted white leather mask styled with dark eyes and a macabre grin. Anyone other details about the person behind the mask are still unknown.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Brute; <b>Virtue:</b> Methodical; <b>Vice:</b> Theatrical<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To become (in)famous.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Can only kill as \u201cRictus Grin\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes</b>: Intelligence 3, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Computers 2, Crafts 2, Expression 2 (Mime), Firearms 2 (Silenced), Intimidate 3(Menacing), Investigate 3 (Potential Victims), Larceny 3 (Breaking and Entering), Stealth 4, Weaponry 3 (Blades)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 3 (Wealthy Patrons), Cover Up, Danger Sense, Fame 1 (Online), Iron Skin 2, Lucky Charm (Mask), Resources 2, Style: Martial Arts 3, Tell-Tale Murder, Trained Observer<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Armor:</b> 1/0 [Reinforced Clothing, 1 vs. Bashing], <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> Machete [+2L melee; -2 Initiative; 9 dice]<br /> Silenced Light Pistol [+1L ranged, 6 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Unstoppable; <b>Frailty:</b> Tunnel Vision<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable:</b> A Brute never suffers wound penalties for any reason, and automatically passes any roll to remain conscious due to damage or pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Tunnel Vision:</b> A Brute suffers a \u22123 penalty to all Perception rolls, and to rolls to avoid being surprised in combat.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T12:43:41-07:00","id":1484230,"title":"","content":"I feel like The Network would be more than happy to secure a deal for exclusive episodes of Rictus Grin.<br /> <br /> Does the Revenant have a specific Bane to end his immortality and a given ritual to reanimate him ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T19:23:45-07:00","id":1484254,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: The Network</b><br /> I have used Network in a few storylines as a compact of Slashers that the PCs were trying to dismantle. Several of the Slashers presented here were developed for that campaign. I especially had fun with the Gourmet as an evil cannibalistic Anthony Bourdain! I also featured Dark Father, Kill Doll and Rictus Grin as the primary antagonists.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: The Revenant</b><br /> I started with a Slasher version of &quot;The Crow&quot;, who was less discriminating in the targets of his vengeance. I left his bane open ended so that anyone using him could fill in the blanks. If I get to use him in a campaign, I would probably give him a bane that he &quot;can only die by an innocent hand&quot;.<br /> <br /> here is today's set. <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Righteous Man</span></b><br /> Wyatt James was once a member of an organization called \u201cThe Church of Revelation\u201d. He and his wife joined the organization as a way to cope with trauma he experienced while serving in the military. The Church of Revelation was an apocalyptic cult, preparing for the impending End of Days. After moving to the church\u2019s sprawling compound, Wyatt became disenchanted (and frightened) by the increasingly radical tone of the churches sermons. When he and his wife tried to escape, they met with armed resistance, and she was killed in the attempt.<br /> Over the course of a year, Wyatt murdered the leaders of the organization, and burned its compound to ashes.<br /> Wyatt continues his crusade, rooting and extinguishing cults and organizations that he deems \u201cfalse\u201d or \u201cevil\u201d. He tries to limit the carnage to leaders and organizers, but more than a few lay members have been caught in the crossfire, which only compels Wyatt to make sure \u201ctheir sacrifice was not in vain\u201d.<br /> Wyatt James is a solid, athletic man in his early thirties with dark hair and brown eyes. He crops his hair close and favors rugged practical clothing.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Avenger;<b> Virtue:</b> Faithful;<b> Vice:</b> Unforgiving<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To destroy those that pervert or corrupt the Gospel<br /> <b>Tell:</b> He targets professed \u201cChristians\u201d or other &quot;People of Faith&quot; that are hypocrites or fall short of his interpretation of the scripture.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1(Bible), Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Crafts 2(Explosives), Drive 2, Firearms 4(Pistols), Intimidate 2, Investigate 3, Occult 1(Cults), Stealth 2(Surveillance), Subterfuge 2, Survival 2(Doomsday Prep), Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Defensive Combat (Brawl), Iron Stamina 2, Iron Will, Professional Training 3 (Soldier; Crafts, Firearms, Survival), Style: Close Quarters Combat 2, Style: Firefight 2<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, Armor: 1/3 [Kevlar Vest], <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 9 dice; 9 again]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Working the Room; <b>Frailty:</b> Nothing but the Mission<br /> <br /> <b>Working the Room:</b> Avengers might try to kill their victims one by one, but sooner or later they wind up with a roomful of people that require their attention. The rules for Defense vs. multiple opponents do not apply to Avengers. No matter how many times in a turn an Avenger is attacked, apply his full Defense to all incoming attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Nothing but the Mission:</b> Most slashers are obsessive, but Avengers take it to a whole new level. The Avenger has the Obsession Condition in regards to pursuing their chosen targets. When faced with the choice between pursuing a target and taking some other course of action, the Storyteller\u2019s must roll Resolve + Composure. If this roll succeeds, the Avenger can choose to let the target go (for now). If the roll fails, the Avenger remains focused on his mission and ignores the other situation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T19:33:00-07:00","id":1484256,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Road Monster</span></b><br /> \u201cThe Road Monster\u201d has been terrorizing back roads and lonely stretches of highway for years. Survivors recall being forced off the road by a large, rusted truck with blinding lights and seemingly driven by a maniac. Some get away with just a dreadful fright. Others suffer fatal collisions or are run down like dogs. The owner of the vehicle is a man named John Gibson (most locals just call him \u201cGib\u201d). Always a loner and an outsider, he keeps largely to himself, rarely venturing away from the property he inherited from his deceased parents. He has turned the land into an auto-shop, impound lot, and scrap yard. He makes a good living as a mechanic and tow truck operator, and most of the locals that do business with him regard him as a strange man who does good enough work to overlook his peculiarities.<br /> But on certain nights, he crawls into the cab of a custom truck he has named \u201cIron Dog\u201d and goes patrolling for victims. He takes special delight in tracking down those that have slighted him in some way, and making them suffer.<br /> Gib is a tall, lean Caucasian man in his late thirties. His teeth are crooked, his skin is smudged with dirt and motor oil, and his face has a five o\u2019clock shadow no amount of shaving can banish. His brown hair is over-long and stuffed beneath a baseball cap, pulled low over his eyes. He dresses in a dirty dark blue coverall when working (and he always seems to be working). Despite his appearance and occupation, Gib is quite intelligent, and belittling him is a sure way to end up beneath the wheels of his truck.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Undesirable; <b>Virtue:</b> Resourceful; <b>Vice:</b> Resentful<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Rule the Roads<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Road Monster kills with his vehicles, and especially his custom truck \u201cIron Dog\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 5, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Athletics 2 (Strong Back), Computers 1, Crafts 4 (Automobiles, Sabotage), Brawl 2, Drive 4 (Offensive, Truck), Firearms 2, Intimidate 2, Investigation 3, Larceny 2, Persuasion 2 (Haggling), Science 1, Subterfuge 2 (Alibi), Survival 1, Weaponry 3 (Clubs)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Automotive Genius, Back Road Atlas, Crack Driver 2, Demolisher 2, Professional Training 3 (Mechanic; Athletics, Crafts, Drive), Resources 2, Safe Place 2 (The Junkyard), Style: Stunt Driver 4<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 8, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 5 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 5 dice]<br /> Tire Iron [+1L melee; -3 Initiative; 7 dice; +1 Defense]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Natural Compass; <b>Frailty:</b> Rejection<br /> <br /> <b>Natural Compass:</b> An Undesirable has a near-perfect sense of direction, and gains a +3 bonus to Perception, Athletics, Investigation, and Survival rolls when present in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Rejection:</b> The Undesirable suffers a \u22124 penalty on Social rolls that do not involve slashers and other monsters.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nest: The Junkyard</span></b><br /> The Junkyard is several acres of land protected by a high barbed wire fence. It services as an impound lot for those unluckily enough to get their vehicles towed away, and as the final resting place for dozens of disabled vehicles. In addition to the derelict vehicles, the area is littered with heaps broken appliances and worn out furniture. A pair of large, surly dogs patrol the area, eager to take a bite out of trespassers. Near the center of the property is a garage, an office, and a small residence.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Arsenal, Home Security<br /> <b>Tilts:</b> Detritus<br /> <b>Traps:</b> Barbed Wire Fence, Deadfall, Guard Animals<br /> <br /> <b>Barbed Wire Fence:</b> The property is surrounded by a 10ft tall fence, topped with razor sharp barbed wire. Anyone attempting to climb over the fence suffers a point of lethal damage, regardless of their success.<br /> <i>Trigger:</i> Climbing over the fence. A successful Dexterity + Athletics OR Dexterity + Larceny roll with a -2 penalty downgrades to bashing damage. An exceptional success negates the damage entirely. Characters armed with the proper tools can cut through the fence as an extended Wits+Crafts roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Deadfall:</b> Teetering piles of junk are primed to collapse upon the unwary. Once the trap is triggered, the trap falls and deals two levels of lethal damage and imposes the Immobilized Tilt, as the victim is pinned beneath the debris. If immobilized, escaping requires a Strength+ Athletics roll to shift aside the rubble. Dramatic failures often inflict the Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt to reflect twisted ankles and the like.<br /> <i>Trigger:</i> Structure damage to objects in the Junkyard. A successful Dexterity + Athletics roll with a -2 penalty negates the Immobilized Tilt and downgrades to bashing damage. An exceptional success negates the damage entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Guard Animals:</b> The Safe Place is patrolled by animals, typical trained guardians or feral creatures that consider the Safe Place their territory, that will attack any intruders. Animals that detect intruders also make enough noise to alert the owners of the property to the presence of unwanted guests. Guard Animals make attacks and perception rolls with a dice pool of twice the dots purchased in the Merit and use Down and Dirty combat rules. All other rolls use a die pool equal to the dots purchased in the Merit.<br /> <i>Trigger:</i> Failed rolls against the Home Security feature. Alerted Guard Animals may be avoided with a Stealth roll, scared off with Intimidate, talked-down with Animal Ken, or defeated in combat.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Relic: Iron Dog</b></span><br /> \u201cIron Dog\u201d is a beast of a truck born in a junkyard and cobbled together from the rusted hulks of dozens of other vehicles. The vehicle looks like something out of a nightmare; the cab and bed sit high upon rugged tires and an imposing cow catcher covers the grill like a maniacs mask. Its rack of gleaming headlights emit a blinding glare and it is reinforced with a roll cage and armored plates, allowing it to survive an unreal amount of punishment. It\u2019s exhaust pipes spew black smoke and its engine roars with demonic fury.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> The vehicle is heavily modified, with a powerful engine, improved handling, and reinforced with armor plates. It\u2019s over-all appearance strikes fear into the heart\u2019s of motorists and pedestrians, granting a +2 equipment bonus to rolls to harass and intimidate. Iron Dog is also equipped with a set of flood lights that emit a blinding glare. Anyone facing the vehicle must make a successful Wits + Composure roll or gain the Blinded Tilt.<br /> Those who drive Iron Dog become obsessive about the truck\u2019s maintenance, gaining the <i>Deprived</i> Condition if they do not spend at least an hour each day repairing or tinkering with the vehicle.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Modifier:</b> -1, <b>Size:</b> 16, <b>Durability/Structure:</b> 6/22, <b>Speed:</b> 90, <b>Availability:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + (Drive or Intimidate)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Success:</b> Iron Dog is restored by bloodshed and slaughter. Whenever the vehicle deals collision damage to a living target, they may spend a point of Willpower and make a (Drive or Intimidate) roll to activate the relic. Doing so restores a point of Structure to Iron Dog for each success rolled.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T20:06:29-07:00","id":1484570,"title":"","content":"Today's Post <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sawtooth Charlie</span></b><br /> The man they call Sawtooth Charlie once worked as a foreman in a Canadian lumber camp. He had a reputation as a tough-but-fair man who enjoyed strong booze, but never let it get in the way of his work. He had the respect of most of his workers, but not all. After a night of drinking, he was confronted by a group of disgruntled employees, and what began as a heated argument quickly escalated to violence, with Charlie being struck in the head with an ax and seemingly falling dead. The men quickly staged an accident, hoping that by the time the body was found, it would be written off as a mishap common to such dangerous work. And yet the body was never found. Shortly thereafter, the men involved began to die. The bodies appeared dismembered with a powerful chainsaw. Witnesses remember the roar of the saw, but no one recalls seeing the perpetrator. Despite the events happening over thirty years ago, dismembered corpses still appear around logging camps and campsites in the forests of the western Canada. It\u2019s said that Charlie developed a thirst for blood that rivals his taste for drink. So always leave shot out for Charlie, it could save your life.<br /> Charlie looks like the quintessential lumberjack. He is dressed in denim and flannel, with strong arms, a broad chest and a thick, black beard. He has a deep, gruesome scar over his left eye, and smells of pine-tar, motor oil, and blood.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Legend; <b>Virtue:</b> Thorough; <b>Vice:</b> Stern<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Punish those who show disrespect to Charlie or the traditions of the camp.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> dismembers the bodies of his victims<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 2, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2 (Balance, Lifting), Brawl 3, Crafts 3 (Mechanic), Drive 2, Firearms 2, Intimidation 5, Occult 1, Persuasion 2, Stealth 4 (Stalking), Survival 4 (Forest, Tracking), Weaponry 4 (Chainsaw)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Demolisher 2, Fleet of Foot 3, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Forest), Iron Stamina 3, Language (French), Professional Training 3 (Lumberjack; Athletics, Survival, Weaponry), Style: Heavy Weapons 3, Weaponry Obsession (Chainsaw) 1<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency</b> 3, <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 5, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Chainsaw [+5L melee, -6 Initiative; 9 dice, 8-again]<br /> Hatchet [+1L melee, -2 Initiative, 8 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Living Legend <b>Frailty:</b> Narrative Chains (Cannot refuse a toast in his honor)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Maze, Regenerate, Unnatural Step (Unimpeded by Plants/Wooden Objects)<br /> <br /> <b>Living Legend:</b> Once per scene, when someone fulfills one of the tenets of the Legend\u2019s \u201crules,\u201d the player can roll the slasher\u2019s chosen Attribute + Occult. Successes on this roll may be applied on one of the following: restoring spent Willpower, healing damage (one success for a bashing wound, two for lethal, three for aggravated), or applying the bonuses to rolls in pursuit of their goal. After this has been activated, successes that haven\u2019t been spent are discarded. They may not be banked to use in a following scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Narrative Chains:</b> The Legend gains a unique and specific frailty enforced by the nature of the tales surrounding them. Additionally, characters investigating the scourge\u2019s Tell gain an exceptional success on three successes rather than five.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Relic: Charlie\u2019s Chainsaw</span></b><br /> This well used STIHL chainsaw is said to belong to Sawtooth Charlie, and reputed killer spoken of in urban legend. When revved, it unleashes a guttural roar with a rhythmic, almost musical quality. The chainsaw is battered, rusted and drips oil constantly. Despite this, it never snags, jams, starts clean with each pull, and rarely needs refueling.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Memento:</b> Charlie\u2019s Chainsaw is soaked in bloodshed and death, which has made it strangely impervious. It is never damaged by accidents or environmental hazards, has a Durability of 5 and twice its normal Structure. If using Geist: The Sin-Eaters 2nd Edition, Charlie\u2019s Chainsaw gives access to the Key of Blood.<br /> <b>Damage:</b> 5L <b>Initiative:</b> -6 <b>Strength:</b> 4 <b>Size:</b> 3 <b>Durability:</b> 5 <b>Quality:</b> 9-again, two-handed <b>Availability:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve + (Crafts or Weaponry)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Success:</b> The chainsaw cuts cleanly through wood and rips through flesh and bone like butter. When activated, the chainsaw gains the Armor Piecing 2 quality until the end of the scene. Once activated, the wielder is overcome by a rush of adrenaline and a berserk fury, and gains the Traumatized Tilt. Damage dealt by Charlie\u2019s Chainsaw is considered supernatural damage and can injure ghosts and other such ephemeral beings.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The wielder does not suffer the Traumatized tilt.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The relic does not activate.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The chainsaw runs out of gas. It cannot be restarted or it\u2019s powers activated until it is refueled. A stopped chainsaw can only be used as an improvised weapon.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T20:14:12-07:00","id":1484571,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Silencer</b></span><br /> Before the diagnosis, Meredith Conway was a gifted alto singer, who took great pride and delight in the power and range of her voice. But a rare degenerative condition slowly destroyed her vocal cords. By the time she was in her mid-thirties, her voice had been reduced to a horse whisper. This took a toll on her mind, and she became obsessed with talented singers, torn between admiration, and blistering jealousy. She lives as a recluse, having made enough money during her career to live comfortably. When she can no longer bear the strain, she ventures out, only finding relief in taking someone\u2019s gift as hers was taken from. If given the choice, she prefers to cripple rather than kill, but accidents happen...<br /> On first impression, Meredith is a tall, thin woman, who uses sign language to communicate. Perhaps a great beauty once, obsession has given her features a worried cast and her focused gaze lingers too intensely. She is frequently wracked with a rasping cough and what remains of her voice is an unpleasant, wavering hiss. She typically wears a wrap or shawl to hide the scars from the many failed surgeries she endured to save her voice. Despite her frail appearance, she is far stronger than she looks and moves with fluid grace.<br /> <i>** Meredith has the Mute (Persistent) Condition.</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Undesirable; <b>Virtue:</b> Reserved; <b>Vice:</b> Sadistic<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Share her pain with other artists<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Targets those with musical or oratory abilities; severing throats, puncturing eardrums and cutting out tongues.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Brawl 2, Empathy 3 (Read the Audience), Expression 4 (Act, Sing), Larceny 2, Medicine 2, Persuasion 2, Socialize 2 (Musical Theater), Stealth 4(Slip Away), Subterfuge 3 (Misdirection), Weaponry 4 (Knife)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Sing), Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Fame 1 (Musical Theater), Fighting Finesse (Knife), Language (American Sign), Professional Training 4 (Performer; Empathy, Expression, Socialize), Resources 2, Safe Place 2 (Recluse\u2019s Den), Sympathetic, Untouchable<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 8, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 5 dice]<br /> Scalpel [+0L melee, 10 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Natural Compass; <b>Frailty:</b> Rejection<br /> <br /> <b>Natural Compass:</b> An Undesirable has a near-perfect sense of direction, and gains a +3 bonus to Perception, Athletics, Investigation, and Survival rolls when present in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Rejection:</b> The Undesirable suffers a \u22124 penalty on Social rolls that do not involve slashers and other monsters.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: The Recluse\u2019s Den</b></span><br /> From the outside, the home is typical. It is well maintained and in good repair, and the lawn is mowed regularly by a Lawn Care service. However, the neighbors have noticed that the person who lives there is rarely seen. No one is ever invited in, and if the owner is seen outside, she never waves or smiles or even looks in your direction. On the inside, the home is a shrine to past glories, with walls lined with articles, awards, and trophies accumulated from a stellar career, now a fading memory. Most of the time, the home is dimly lit, but one particular room is always bright. It holds trophies not of Meredith, but of her victims, both past and future.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Home Security, Trophy Room*<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Trophy Room:</b> The Trophy Room is a macabre gallery of objects and souvenirs that remind the slasher of their greatest conquests. When the slasher is present, they may gain the <i>Steadfast</i> Condition until the end of the Scene. The collected objects are also strangely compelling to investigators; those investigating the Safe Place must make a Resolve +Composure roll or gain the <i>Spooked</i> Condition. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T10:43:29-07:00","id":1484784,"title":"","content":"Today's Post <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Sniper</span></b><br /> Samuel Carson was a decorated army sniper who, after being honorably discharged from the military, went into mercenary work when civilian life proved to be far too boring. After an indent in Africa where he survived an encounter with\u2026 inexplicable things, he returned home with holes in his mind and holes in his spirit. Now the only thing that quiets his mind and provides any measure of peace and comfort is finding a target in his sights,, and pulling the trigger. At first, he could gain relief by target shooting or hunting game, but now only living, human targets provide any satisfaction.<br /> Once outgoing, Sam has become increasingly withdrawn. He has had trouble holding a job, and mostly lives off the money he earned from his military and mercenary careers. He moves frequently, leaving an area after one or two confirmed kills, making him difficult for the authorities to track.<br /> Samuel is a tall, athletic African American man in his late thirties, with close cropped hair and deep brown eyes. Years of active combat duty have aged him before his time, and his face is lined and scarred.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Brute; <b>Virtue:</b> Precise; <b>Vice:</b> Anti-Social<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To sooth his mind through killing<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Kills with rifle or other long range weapons<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3(Climb), Brawl 3, Crafts 2, Drive 2, Firearms 5(Rifle), Intimidation 3, Larceny 2, Medicine 2, Science 2, Stealth 4 (Evade Capture, Sniper\u2019s Nest), Streetwise 2 (Black Market), Survival 3 (Off Grid), Weaponry 2 (Knife)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Contacts 2 (Black Market, Veterans), Damnable Certainty, Fixer, Language (Arabic, Afrikaans, Others),Professional Training 4(Soldier; Firearms, Survival, Stealth), Style: Marksmanship 4, Style: Street-Fighting 2, Tactical Insight, Trained Observer 1<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 9, <b>Armor:</b> 1/3 (Kevlar Vest), <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 6 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 10 dice; 9 again]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> Rifle [+4L ranged; -5 Initiative; 11 dice; 9 again]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Unstoppable <b>Frailty:</b> Tunnel Vision<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable:</b> A Brute never suffers wound penalties for any reason, and automatically passes any roll to remain conscious due to damage or pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Tunnel Vision:</b> A Brute suffers a \u22123 penalty to all Perception rolls, and to rolls to avoid being surprised in combat.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T10:49:29-07:00","id":1484785,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Taxidermist</span></b><br /> From the first time Corben Verril poked a road-killed raccoon with a stick, he has been obsessed with death. As a youth, he would collect the carcasses of dead animals, becoming a self-taught expert at embalming and taxidermy. Already homely and socially anxious, his curious hobbies did not do much to endear him to his classmates, who taunted him cruelly. His preserved specimens became his only friends as he withdrew further away from society.<br /> The first time he killed, it was an accident. He had become enamored with a young man and stalked him from afar. When he revealed himself, the incident quickly turned violent and ended with him throttling the object of his desires to death. In a fugue, he applied his skills as a taxidermist to preserve the beauty of his victim. He now seeks out attractive men and women to add to his private gallery, considering them to be the friends he never had growing up.<br /> Corben is a man in his early thirties with a compact, muscular build. His skin is marked with acne scars, his eyes are watery and he carries an unpleasant odor from embalming chemicals and infrequent baths. He is shy and soft spoken, muttering apologies even as he wrings the necks of his victims.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking</b>: Undesirable; <b>Virtue:</b> Earnest; <b>Vice:</b> Needy<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Make Friends<br /> <b>Tell:</b> His victims are always attractive. He prefers to kill by strangulation and always preserves the corpses (either whole, or in part).<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Athletics 2(Manual Labor), Brawl 4(Strangle), Crafts 4(Taxidermy), Larceny 2, Medicine 2, Persuasion 2 (Pitiable), Science (Chemistry) 2, Stealth 4, Survival 3(Wildlife), Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Choke Hold, Cover Tracks, Fast Reflexes 1, Professional Training 2 (Laborer; Athletics, Crafts), Striking Looks 1 (Homely), Style: Close Quarters Combat 2, Safe Place 3 (Roadside Attraction Shop), Sympathetic<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 9 dice]<br /> Skinning Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Natural Compass; <b>Frailty:</b> Rejection<br /> <br /> <b>Natural Compass:</b> An Undesirable has a near-perfect sense of direction, and gains a +3 bonus to Perception, Athletics, Investigation, and Survival rolls when present in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Rejection:</b> The Undesirable suffers a \u22124 penalty on Social rolls that do not involve slashers and other monsters.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nest: The Roadside Attraction</span></b><br /> Off the side of a country road used by hikers and campers on their way to the back country, is the Verril Station. In addition to being the last stop for gas, snacks, and supplies for at least thirty miles, the Verril Station has a room that contains a gallery of taxidermied animals, specimens preserved in formaldehyde and other oddities. Corben maintains a private shack on the back acres of the property where he keeps his \u201cspecial\u201d collection.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Home Security, Innocent Facade*,Trophy Room*<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Innocent Facade:</b> To casual observation, a Safe Place with Innocent Facade appears perfectly normal, with not even a hint of anything unusual happening. Any attempts to Investigate or use abilities to detect criminal, supernatural or otherwise unusual activity suffer a penalty equal to dots purchased in the Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Trophy Room:</b> The Trophy Room is a macabre gallery of objects and souvenirs that remind the slasher of their greatest conquests. When the slasher is present, they may gain the Steadfast Condition until the end of the Scene. The collected objects are also strangely compelling to investigators; those investigating the Safe Place must make a Resolve +Composure roll or gain the Spooked Condition. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T19:34:43-07:00","id":1485003,"title":"","content":"I could imagine the Sniper taking trophies from those he hunted to make his own custom sniper rifle, a way to &quot;retake control over his own life from the hunters in the dark&quot;.<br /> <br /> If he killed a werewolf, for example, he could take a fetish. Since it was made with manzanita wood that once imprisoned a lightning spirit, he could use it to make a grip. Had he killed a mage, he would loot some &quot;meteoric iron&quot; (siderite) found in their Sanctum and use it in to make a custom polymer for his rifling. If he kills a Sin Eater (which might be a huge headache), maybe his lens becomes a Memento. Killing a Demon would probably allow him to transform it into a steampunk wonder. Not sure what he could make from a vampire though, they only leave ashes behind , plus vitae is hard to collect unwillingly (especially with a rifle) and denatures very quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T15:47:14-07:00","id":1485144,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: The Sniper</b><br /> The Sniper escalates. If not stopped, he will reach a point where human victims no longer satisfy him. He is already deadly enough to represent a treat to even hardy supernaturals, given a weapon that can counter supernatural protection moves him up to the next level of dangerous.<br /> <br /> for today's post ... <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Thrill Killer</span></b><br /> Cory Michaels was raised in an upper-middle class suburban home, with a stable family life and upper-middle class conservative values. But even at a young age, Cory was prone to rebellion and trouble making. As he grew, mischief escalated to petty and (occasionally violent) crime. All attempts to reform his behavior failed, seeming to only reinforce his contempt for authority. After one crime to many, he has kicked out of his home and never looked back. He supported himself for years with drag racing, drug dealing, extortion, and theft. The first time he committed murder was as a paid hit man tasked with making the client\u2019s husband \u201cdisappear\u201d. This gave him a rush that he has been try to recapture ever since. There is no greater goal or philosophy behind what Cory does, the pure thrill of taking a life is the only justification he wants or needs. Cory has no particular preference for victims, choosing them almost at random, seeking those who are physically or emotionally vulnerable. He moves frequently and keeps a low profile. Since becoming an adult, he has never been arrested for any major crimes and wants to keep it that was as long as possible.<br /> Cory is a fit and good looking Caucasian man in his late twenties. He is clean-shaven, gray-eyed, and his hair is currently cut short and dyed blond. He likes music, and will change his sense of style to match a particular scene. He currently favors a \u201crockabilly\u201d look, with boots, cuffed jeans, crisp t-shirts, and pack of Monument(tm) cigarettes rolled in the sleeve. He has a charming (if somewhat intense) personality, but can become cruel and threatening (and back again) at a moments notice, and has a well-rehearsed story of an abusive and neglectful upbringing when he wants to earn some sympathy with a good sob story.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Confidence; <b>Vice:</b> Rebellious<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Defy Authority, The Joy of the Kill<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Most of his victims are \u201cpeople that won\u2019t be missed\u201d, such as transients, sex workers and other criminals. He occasionally \u201ctreats\u201d himself to someone more high-profile, and savors the experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 2<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 4, Crafts 2, Drive 3 (Drag Race), Expression 1 (Guitar), Firearms 2, Intimidate 3 (Intense), Larceny 3 (Car Theft), Socialize 2, Streetwise 3 (Drugs, Stolen Goods), Subterfuge 2 (Gain Sympathy), Weaponry 2 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 2, Bar Fly, Crack Driver 2, Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Hands of a Killer, Professional Training 3 (Criminal; Brawl, Larceny, Streetwise), Shiv 1, Style: Street Fighting 3, Striking Looks 1 (Handsome)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Brass Knuckles [+0L melee, 7 dice, Brawl]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> Switchblade [+0L melee, 5 dice, Shiv]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Telling him What to Do)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T15:58:42-07:00","id":1485146,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Toymaker</span></b><br /> Polaris Toys was founded by Johanna W\u00f3jcik\u2019s grandfather, and specialized in electronic toys, especially software and remote control devices. They were pioneering in walkies-talkies, remote control cars, and were early on the market with affordable drones. She had expected to inherit the company from her father, but the company was purchased in a hostile takeover by several of their more unscrupulous investors. The company\u2019s assets were divided and their coveted patents sold off. Johanna was at her father's bedside as he died, swearing vengeance on those that had stolen their family\u2019s legacy.<br /> It took time to learn the necessary skills. While already a talented programmer and engineer, Johanna went to school to hone these abilities, as well becoming a self-taught expert with explosives. She is now working her way through a list of targets; deceivers, manipulators and betrayers one and all. When the last one is dead, who knows? Perhaps there are others deserving her brand of retribution.<br /> Johanna is a Caucasian woman in her early thirties of average height and slim build, with brown hair and green eyes. She rarely dresses in anything other than jeans and t-shirts, and wears flattering glasses. While most of her hobbies keep her indoors, she runs and skateboards to stay in shape and has become fairly good at at. She is personable; with an easy smile and quick with a joke, even when frustrated or experiencing a setback. But she nurses grudges and will payback anyone that has crossed her...with interest.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Avenger; <b>Virtue:</b> Friendly; <b>Vice:</b> Vindictive<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To make those that betrayed her family pay.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Toymaker always uses indirect methods to kill, such as drones, explosives and sabotage.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Athletics 2, Computers 3(Programming), Crafts 4 (Electronics, Explosives, Toys), Drive 3 (Drone), Firearms 3 (Remote), Investigation 2, Larceny 2, Politics 2, Science 3(Chemistry), Socialize 2 (Humor), Streetwise 2 (Contraband), Subterfuge 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Cover-Up, Fast Reflexes 2, Fleet Of Foot 1, Patient, Professional Training 3 (Engineer; Computers, Crafts, Science), Resources 3, Style: Drone Control 3*, Trained Observer 1<br /> <i>*Chronicles of Darkness: Hurt Locker p.55</i><br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 8, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 2 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> Remote Mine [Damage +3, Blast Area 1, Force 2. 7 dice to trigger if contested]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Working the Room; <b>Frailty:</b> Nothing but the Mission<br /> <br /> <b>Working the Room:</b> Avengers might try to kill their victims one by one, but sooner or later they wind up with a roomful of people that require their attention. The rules for Defense vs. multiple opponents do not apply to Avengers. No matter how many times in a turn an Avenger is attacked, apply his full Defense to all incoming attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Nothing but the Mission:</b> Most slashers are obsessive, but Avengers take it to a whole new level. The Avenger has the Obsession Condition in regards to pursuing their chosen targets. When faced with the choice between pursuing a target and taking some other course of action, the Storyteller\u2019s must roll Resolve + Composure. If this roll succeeds, the Avenger can choose to let the target go (for now). If the roll fails, the Avenger remains focused on his mission and ignores the other situation.<br /> <br /> <b>Drones:</b> The Toymaker makes use of a variety of modified R/C vehicles and flying drones. She often disguises them as toys or other innocuous seeming objects. Most of them use the following stats and are modified by task. Johanna uses Wits+Drive to pilot a drone.<br /> <b>Dice Modifier:</b> +0, <b>Size:</b> 2, <b>Durability/Structure:</b> 1/3, <b>Speed:</b> 10, <b>Range:</b> 100, <b>Availability:</b> 2<br /> <i>*Modifications:</i> +2 Dice, +1 Durability, Audio/Visual Feedback<br /> \u2022 <i><b>Explosive Drone:</b></i> The explosive drone is a modified R/C car that carries and explosive device. It has a speed of 20. The explosive has the following traits. Damage +3, Blast Area 1, Force 2.<br /> Trigger: The explosive has a remote detonator that can be activated as an Instant action.<br /> \u2022 <i><b>Spy Drone:</b></i> The spy is flying drone designed to move silently and is considerably miniaturized. The Spy Drone is Size 1, has a range of 200 meters, and gains a +1 dice modifier and a +2 bonus to rolls involving moving the drone quietly or unobtrusively. <br /> \u2022 <i><b>Weapon Drone:</b></i> The weapon drone is built flying drone for stability and is mounted with a modified light pistol. The weapon carries three rounds of ammunition and makes attacks using the pilot\u2019s Wits+Firearms dice pool.<br /> <i>*modifications are factored into statistics when appropriate.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Explosives:</b> The Toymaker favors explosives, and is endlessly creative in what she can build into a bomb. She often assumes the guise of a cleaning woman, mail carrier, or other civic servant to gain access to places where she can plant devices. These are built as Traps (<i>Hunter: The Vigil, 2nd edition, p. 286</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>Style: Drone Control:</b> The Toymaker knows how to operate weapon systems via remote. These maneuvers work independently of the sophistication of the actual device.<br /> \u2022 <i><b>Remote Immersion:</b></i> When the Toymaker accesses her drone she enters a focused state that lets her perceive and react to things as if she were physically present. Perception rolls made using the drone gain the 9-again quality.<br /> \u2022 <i><b>Interface:</b></i> The Toymaker has honed her control over her drones to the level of instinct. Spend a point of Willpower; she can take an additional instant action per turn with her drone. Drones capable of attacking can only make one attacking action per turn.<br /> \u2022 <i><b>Overclock:</b></i> The Toymaker can push her drone past the boundaries of its hardware. By sacrificing a point of Structure, she can add +2 to Physical actions the drone makes that turn.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T15:30:00-07:00","id":1485420,"title":"","content":"today's posts <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Transient</span></b><br /> Born into poverty, John Smith struggled with finding purpose and direction in his life. His unremarkable childhood bloomed into an unremarkable adulthood as he left school early and drifted from job to job, never making much of a mark in his world or on those around him. His dissatisfaction eventually led to a drug problem, which eventually led to his living on the streets. His lifelong dissatisfied became a boiling rage directed at those that had been given so much while he had been given so little. His first victim was a banker who sneeringly told him to \u201cGet a Job\u201d. He followed him home, broke into his house, and shot him in the face with a cheap pistol. Since then he has begun targeting other wealthy people, showing an uncanny knack for getting past the security that wealth and privilege can normally buy. Finally, something he was good at.<br /> John Smith is the definition of nondescript. A Caucasian man of average height in his early forties with brown hair and brown eyes. He has no distinguishing marks and dresses in rugged second hand clothing. Despite using the same light revolver in all of his crimes, the authorities have had difficulty trying the homicides together.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Avenger; <b>Virtue:</b> Righteous; <b>Vice:</b> Envious<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To make those that flaunt their wealth suffer<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Only targets the wealthy (or seemingly wealthy)<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 2<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Crafts 3 (Handyman), Firearms 3 (Close Range), Investigation 2(Locate Victim), Larceny 3 (Breaking and Entering), Persuasion 2 (Panhandle), Stealth 3(Lost in a Crowd), Streetwise 4, Subterfuge 2, Survival 2 (Urban), Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Cover Tracks, Cover Up, Face in the Crowd, Sleight of Hand, Professional Training 3(Vagrant; Larceny, Streetwise, Survival), Trained Observer 3<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 8, <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 6 dice]<br /> .38 Revolver [+1L ranged; 8 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Working the Room; <b>Frailty:</b> Nothing but the Mission<br /> <br /> <b>Working the Room:</b> Avengers might try to kill their victims one by one, but sooner or later they wind up with a roomful of people that require their attention. The rules for Defense vs. multiple opponents do not apply to Avengers. No matter how many times in a turn an Avenger is attacked, apply his full Defense to all incoming attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Nothing but the Mission:</b> Most slashers are obsessive, but Avengers take it to a whole new level. The Avenger has the Obsession Condition in regards to pursuing their chosen targets. When faced with the choice between pursuing a target and taking some other course of action, the Storyteller\u2019s must roll Resolve + Composure. If this roll succeeds, the Avenger can choose to let the target go (for now). If the roll fails, the Avenger remains focused on his mission and ignores the other situation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Relic: The Phantom Gun</b></span><br /> This pistol is a gunmetal gray snub-nosed revolver of unknown make. The serial numbers and other identifying marks have been meticulously sanded off, and the weapon shows signs of heavy use. The Phantom Gun was used extensively as a \u201clibrary gun\u201d; shared among gang members and used for many crimes to obscure its forensic trial. Those who know of this particular weapon estimate it has been used in conjunction with well over 100 felonies. The weapon has been confiscated by the authorities on numerous occasions, but always seems to disappear from the evidence locker in short order.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The Phantom Gun is difficult to track; it retains no fingerprints (ballistic or otherwise) and any roll to investigate it or to tie its wielder to a crime suffers a -2 die penalty. If the Phantom Gun is not discarded within 24 hours of committing a crime, the wielder draws the attention of the authorities. The wielder\u2019s very presence raises suspicion even if there is no proof of wrongdoing. The wielder gains the <i>Notoriety</i> (Law Enforcement) Condition, which must be resolved normally even if the pistol leaves their possession.<br /> If the weapon is ever lost, discarded, or confiscated by the authorities, it vanishes from the scene. The Storyteller may then place the Phantom Gun into a scene with a character that is likely to use it to commit a crime.<br /> <b>Damage:</b> +1L, <b>Initiative:</b> 0, <b>Size:</b> 1 <b>Durability:</b> 3 <b>Clip:</b> 6 <b>Range:</b> 20/40/80 <b>Availability:</b> 2<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T15:35:41-07:00","id":1485421,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Vogue</span></b><br /> Fifteen years ago, the fashion world was taken by storm by a young, ambitious German designer named Siegfried Lange (later choosing to simply go by \u201cSiegfried\u201d). Outspoken and often controversial, Siegfried backed it up with a rare talent for both high fashion and ready-to-wear clothing. To be their chosen \u201cMuse\u201d was an honor, even if only for a few months. But fashion moves quickly and time is unforgiving. While still a respected figure in the world of fashion, Siegfried has fallen out of the limelight. When a nasty fight with their current muse and paramour turned deadly, Siegfried found their artistic passions re-invigorated. They are already working on a collection that will allow them to once again rule the fashion world. They are discreet, and have thus far managed to make most their murders look like accidents, disappearances or suicides, it is only a matter of time before their deeds are uncovered. They are already plotting ways to stage their own death or disappearance. The posthumous renown will be glorious.<br /> Siegfried is a fit and attractive non-binary person in their late thirties. They are slender, with (currently) blond hair, high cheekbones, and startling blue eyes. They dress to impress at all times, and their sense of fashion favors slim suits made of expensive fabrics. They wear a variety of stylish glasses to correct their mild nearsightedness.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Innovative; <b>Vice:</b> Perfectionist<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To find the perfect Muse.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Victims are all people involved in the fashion industry, and are typically exceptionally good looking.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Crafts 3 (Tailoring), Expression 4 (Fashion, Photography), Firearms 2 (Pistols), Investigation 2, Persuasion 3 (Bribe, Seduce), Socialize 3, Stealth 3, Streetwise 2 (Drugs), Subterfuge 3 (Lying to Cops), Weaponry 3 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 3 (Fashion Industry), Area of Expertise (Fashion), Cover-Up, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Fame 1 (Fashion Industry), Hardy 1, Hands of a Killer, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Fashion), Language (English, French), Professional Training 4 (Fashion Designer; Crafts, Expression, Socialize), Resources 4, Striking Looks 2 (Stylish), Taste (Fashion), Untouchable<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, Defense: 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 2 dice]<br /> Scissors [+0L melee, - 1 Initiative; 6 dice, Improvised]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 7 dice]<br /> Liquor Bottle [+0L melee, - 1 Initiative; 6 dice, Improvised, Stun]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Suggesting they are \u201cOut of Style\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: The Penthouse</b></span><br /> This expensive, spacious apartment sits on the top floor of of a multi-story building. It is accessed through either a secured stairwell or an elevator that requires a key or pass code to access the floor. The apartment is comfortable, well decorated and has access to all the most modern amenities. Above all else, it is private; people with the means to live in the penthouse value discretion in all their affairs.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Home Security, Privacy<br /> <br /> <b>Feature-Privacy:</b> The Safe Place is built with an eye towards discretion, even in the heart of a teaming city. The windows tint or drop a shade with the push of a button, the walls are sound-proofed, and even waste disposal is managed to prevent unwanted parties from picking through refuse looking for clues. In addition to penalties imposed by Home Security, anyone outside of the Safe Place that attempts to observe or investigate events or persons inside the Safe Place suffer an additional -2 penalty. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T15:38:08-07:00","id":1485422,"title":"","content":"...And that is the end for the first set of slashers! Hopefully at least one of these rogues can be used as is, or inspire some ideas for your own games. I still have plenty more ideas that I am working on,, so stay tuned to this thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T15:01:53-07:00","id":1508489,"title":"","content":"... And time for a new set of &quot;All Killer, No Filler&quot; Slashers! <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Apex</b></span><br /> Modi Bjornson is the type of person who has triumphed at everything he tried his hand at. Raised in an upper-middle class home in his native Iceland, he excelled in academics and sports, and showed a particular skill at power-lifting. Graduating from college with high marks, he traveled the world, voraciously seeking new opportunities, and trying his hand at many different careers. Over his travels, he saw the weaknesses of humanity all across the world, and developed a philosophy of personal fulfillment and accomplishment that allows it\u2019s practitioner to reach the \u201cApex\u201d of human potential. With the publication of his book \u201cThe Apex Principle\u201d, he has created a small empire, with online classes, speaking engagements, and a line of dietary supplements. His success has made him famous (especially among those who decry the loss of \u201ctraditional\u201d masculinity), wealthy, and has attracted a throng of loyal devotees to his philosophy.<br /> Modi also harbors the dark secret that he enjoys culling the weak from humanity. He uses his resources to find targets (typically drug addicts, homeless people, and the similarly under-privileged), and takes them to a remote wilderness area to hunt them down over the course of several days. If they survive, they will have proven their worth and would be rewarded with a large sum of cash. So far he has never had to pay.<br /> Modi is a handsome, heavily muscled man in his early forties. He has dark hair (stylishly cut), a full beard, and piercing blue eyes. He has distinctive tattoos with a dragon motif on his back and arms. He is well dressed in fashionable clothing that is cut to show off his impressive physique. He is a fanatic about fitness and diet, shunning any intoxicants, eating a carefully balanced diet, and is voluntarily celibate (at least until he can find an equally superior woman to be his mate).<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Puppeteer; <b>Virtue:</b> Edifying; <b>Vice:</b> Ambitious<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Raise up a superior human race<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Modi believes in culling the \u201cweak\u201d and inferior\u201d; most of his victims come from marginalized and under-privileged communities, but he has occasionally hunted those he has deemed \u201cunworthy\u201d of their wealth and privilege.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3 (Business), Athletics 3 (Weight Lifting), Brawl 3 (Overpower), Crafts 2, Computers 2, Drive 1, Empathy 2, Firearms 3 (Rifle), Intimidate 3, Investigation 3, Medicine 1(Nutrition), Persuasion 4 (Sales), Science 1, Socialize 2 (Social Media), Subterfuge 3, Survival 3, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Contacts 3 (Investors, Men\u2019s Rights, Publishers), Cover-Up, Fame 1, Inspiring, Language (English, German, Japanese, Russian), Professional Training 3(Entrepreneur; Academics, Persuasion, Socialize), Resources 5, Safe Place 3 (Palatial Estate), Staff 2 (Devotees), Striking Looks 2 (Handsome), Style: Martial Arts 3, Style: Strength Performance 2<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 2, <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 8 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> Rifle [+4L ranged; -5 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling <b>Frailty:</b> Falter<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Hypnotic Gaze, Supernatural Merit (Biokinesis 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling:</b> A Puppeteer can profile a victim much like a Virtuoso, but additionally benefits from the 8-again quality on any contested roll against a profiled target. They also impose a penalty equal to the scourge\u2019s Intelligence on victims\u2019 rolls to notice traps or react to ambushes set for them in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Falter:</b> Whenever a Puppeteer fails a Social roll, it becomes a dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> <b>Hypnotic Gaze:</b> The scourge\u2019s gaze can charm and beguile. When meeting the target\u2019s gaze, he can spend 1 Willpower and roll Presence + Persuasion contested by the target\u2019s Composure. If successful, the scourge counts as having a perfect impression against the target for Social maneuvers until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Style: Strength Performance: </b>Modi has specifically trained in lifting, pushing, and pulling enormous weights.<br /> \u2022 Strength Tricks (\u2022): Modi combines trained strength with a practical knowledge of physics to perform impressive, if minor, feats of strength. He can rip phone books in half, bend rebar, and smash bricks with his bare hands. He benefits from a +2 bonus to Expression and Intimidation rolls where he can demonstrate his talents, and an additional +1 to other non-combat feats of Strength.<br /> \u2022 Lifting (\u2022\u2022): Modi can perform incredible feats of raw strength. When attempting a feat of strength that requires a Strength + Stamina roll, he gains the Rote benefit \u2014 re-roll failed dice. This does not aid running, jumping, or combat rolls, but does aid in attempts to damage relatively immobile, inanimate objects. In that case he gains the Rote benefit on a combat dice pool no larger than his Strength + Stamina.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: Palatial Estate</b></span><br /> A large home sits on acres of carefully manicured lawns and topiary, and has all the trappings of luxury. The property is surrounded by high walls and fences, and is protected by a professional security service that responds quickly to intruders or any other unusual disturbances.<br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Escape Hatch, Home Security, Privacy<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Privacy (Feature):</b> The Safe Place is built with an eye towards discretion. The windows tint or drop a shade with the push of a button, the walls are sound-proofed, and even waste disposal is managed to prevent unwanted parties from picking through refuse looking for clues. In addition to penalties imposed by Home Security, anyone outside of the Safe Place that attempt to observe or investigate events or persons inside the Safe Place suffer an additional -2 penalty.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: Hunting Grounds</b></span><br /> The Hunting Grounds are a remote forest miles from anything resembling civilization. The area is filled with a variety of natural hazards and dangerous wildlife. During the winter months, these hazards are compounded by freezing temperatures and sudden storms that will kill anyone unprepared for the harsh conditions and can challenge even seasoned and well-equipped survivalists.<br /> <b>Tilts:</b> Blizzard (Winter), Extreme Cold (Winter), Maze, Stinging (Summer), Undergrowth<br /> <b>Traps:</b> Pit Trap<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Maze (Environmental): </b>The terrain twists and turns without readily available landmarks, disorienting and confusing affected characters. Characters attempting to trace their steps or find a way out of the area must succeed at an Intelligence + Composure roll with a 2 dice penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Pit Trap (Trap):</b> A deep pit lined with sharped stakes and concealed beneath a tarp and piles of leaves. trap comprised of large rocks and lumber hand suspended from the dense canopy of trees. Once the trap is triggered, the victims suffers a point of lethal damage from the fall and the spikes, or one point of aggravated damage on a dramatic failure. Escaping a pit trap requires a Strength + Athletics \u2013 2 roll to climb or jump out.<br /> Trigger: False Floor. A successful Wits + Composure roll with a -2 penalty avoids the trap.<br /> <br /> <b>Stinging (Environmental):</b> Mild toxins in undergrowth or stinging insects can irritate the skin and eyes of victims, impeding their efforts. The stinging or itching isn\u2019t enough to cause injury, but imposes a \u20131 dice \u201cwound penalty\u201d on all rolls as though the affected character were in the third-to-last box of Health.<br /> <br /> <b>Undergrowth (Environmental): </b>Dense undergrowth provides cover and entangles characters moving through it. Characters attempting to move through the undergrowth must succeed at a Strength + Athletics roll penalized by the<br /> undergrowth\u2019s Durability rating (typically 1-2 for roots, shrubs, and other vegetation).\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T07:23:24-07:00","id":1508529,"title":"","content":"<b><b><b>Slashers With The Predator Undertaking</b></b>\u200b?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/11z_eQFQF0BwXBNJ3knjLqP71GvD_AZ9o/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/11z_eQFQF0BwXBNJ3knjLqP71GvD_AZ9o/view\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/11z_eQFQF0BwXBNJ3knjLqP71GvD_AZ9o/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/11z_eQFQF0BwXBNJ3knjLqP71GvD_AZ9o/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","user":"Phoenix853457","date":". 04-16-2023, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T19:22:32-07:00","id":1508705,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: New Undertakings</b><br /> <br /> Those look pretty neat! Is this a fan-work or are these official from a supplement I missed?<br /> <br /> Today's slasher posted below. <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Badge Collector</span></b><br /> Deidre \u201cDee Cee\u201d Carter had a difficult upbringing in the inner city. Raised by a drug-addict mother with a father that spent most of his time in and out of prison, she had to grow up fast. After fatally shooting her mother's boyfriend when he tried to force himself on her, she ran away from home and did not look back. Falling in with a crew of small-time drug dealers, she quickly gained a reputation for being a cold-blooded enforcer. As the gang grew in size and power, they gained the attention of the authorities, who planned to shut them down for good. A police raid took a violent turned that killed her entire gang and burned their hideout to the ground. Though injured, Dee Cee escaped the massacre. With the loss of the only people she ever cared about, she swore bloody revenge on anyone wearing a badge. She isn\u2019t stupid, preferring to attack by ambush, and she doesn\u2019t care a single damn for civilians caught in the crossfire. The local police know they are being stalked by a cop-murdering serial killer, and task force is being assemble to hunt her down. She expects to die fighting, and wants to take as many cops as possible with her.<br /> Dee Cee is African-American woman in her mid twenties, but the haunted look in her dark eyes makes her seem older. She wears her hair in braids and dresses in dark, functional clothing. She is in exceptional physical condition, as she has few interests beyond exercise and teaching herself the skills necessary to aid her vendetta. She lives comfortably off the hidden stashes of cash left behind by her gang and occasionally accepts payment as a hit woman.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking: </b>Avenger; <b>Virtue:</b> Loyal; <b>Vice:</b> Focused<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Kill every mf\u2019er wearing a badge.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Dee Cee collects badges; and claims the badges of her victims as trophies.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 5 Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 3 (Boxing), Crafts 2, Drive 2, Firearms 3 (Pistols, Shotguns), Intimidation 3, Investigation 2, Larceny 3, Science 2, Streetwise 3 (Gangs), Stealth 3 (Ambush), Subterfuge 2, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 3 (Gangs), Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Professional Training 3 (Criminal), Resources 2, Style: Firefight 1, Style: Street Fighting 3, Trained Observer 1<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 8, <b>Armor:</b> 1/3 (Kevlar Vest), <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Machete [+2L melee; -2 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 9 dice]<br /> Shotgun [+3L ranged; -4 Initiative; 9 dice, 9-again]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Working the Room; <b>Frailty:</b> Nothing but the Mission<br /> <br /> <b>Working the Room:</b> Avengers might try to kill their victims one by one, but sooner or later they wind up with a roomful of people that require their attention. The rules for Defense vs. multiple opponents do not apply to Avengers. No matter how many times in a turn an Avenger is attacked, apply his full Defense to all incoming attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Nothing but the Mission:</b> Most slashers are obsessive, but Avengers take it to a whole new level. The Avenger has the Obsession Condition in regards to pursuing their chosen targets. When faced with the choice between pursuing a target and taking some other course of action, the Storyteller\u2019s must roll Resolve + Composure. If this roll succeeds, the Avenger can choose to let the target go (for now). If the roll fails, the Avenger remains focused on his mission and ignores the other situation.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T21:12:19-07:00","id":1508830,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Bakemono</span></b><br /> Death has been stalking the streets of Tokyo for nearly five years, with no signs of stopping. The victims are varied; men and women, wealthy and poor, police and criminals. All have been found dead and decapitated. Only occasionally is the victim\u2019s head recovered. The press and authorities have dubbed the killer \u201cThe Bakemono\u201d, which roughly translates to \u201cMonster\u201d. The Bakemono has been confronted by authorities once, and was described as a man in dark clothing, with a sword and a demonic mask. During the altercation, the killer wounded several officers and despite being shot several times, the escaped by crashing through a window (several stories up) and vanished into the night. So far the Bakemono has claimed ten victims, with seemingly no connection between them, and it is only a matter of time before he strikes again.<br /> Some of the urban legends that have grown around the Bakemono state that he was an emotionally disturbed youth from a wealthy home that was committed to an asylum who later escaped. Others paint him as a member of a doomsday cult ushering in the apocalypse. Still others claim he is a betrayed assassin returned from the dead to seek revenge upon those responsible. The truth remains unknown. A police task force has been assembled to track down the killer and put an end to his rampage, but have made little progress.<br /> The Bakemono is presumably a Japanese man of average height and athletic physique. He dresses in dark clothing that allows for motion and physical activity, and wears a mask with a demonic motif. He carries a sword as his main killing tool, but has engaged in a firefight with several police offices and shows proficiency with firearms. He has been baffling to investigate, leaving little evidence of who he might be, and what his true motives are.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Mask; <b>Virtue:</b> Driven; <b>Vice:</b> Excessive<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To bring death to those that have earned it.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Bakemono decapitates each of his victims. In addition, unknown to the authorities, the Bakemono knows each of his victims personally, and has good reason (by Slasher standards) to see them all dead.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Academics 2, Athletics 4 (Climbing), Brawl 4, Firearms 3 (Pistols), Intimidation 4, Larceny 3 (Intrusion), Occult 2, Stealth 5 (Escape), Streetwise 2, Survival 3, Weaponry 5 (Blades)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 3, Atavism, Cover Tracks, Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Fleet of Foot 2, Lucky Charm (Mask), Seizing the Edge, Style: Armed Defense 3, Style: Parkour 3, Weaponry Obsession (Sword)<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency</b> 3, <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 8, <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 9 dice]<br /> Sword [+3L melee;-2 Initiative; 10 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Killing Machine <b>Frailty:</b> Only the Kill<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Glitch, Shadow Attraction, Surprise Entrance<br /> <br /> <b>Killing Machine:</b> Like a Brute, a Mask does not suffer wound penalties and passes rolls to remain conscious due to damage or pain. Additionally, the Mask does not need to sleep or eat, and only suffers a single point of damage from any attack regardless of the damage or number of successes. This applies to mundane and supernatural forms of attack; only environmental damage such as fire, electrocution, or falling bricks applies damage normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Only the Kill:</b> A Mask has lost the ability to communicate. They are illiterate and are limited to simple gestures or grunts. To understand what\u2019s been said to them, they must succeed at an Intelligence + Composure roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Surprise Entrance:</b> No matter how secure its victims think they are, by spending 1 Willpower the scourge may suddenly appear in the scene. Any character witnessing this entrance must succeed on a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll or gain the Shaken Condition. If the characters have actively taken appropriate measures to keep the Slasher out (barring and locking the door, smashing all the mirrors they can find, etc.) it will take them one full turn to break through, giving the characters time to react. If not, it\u2019s just there as a reflexive action and can take one more action before anyone can react.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T22:43:33-07:00","id":1508997,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Blank</b></span><br /> Every year, untold numbers of people disappear without a trace. And many of these disappearances can be attributed to a figure known as \u201cBlank\u201d. The first cases were documented in the late seventies, when three students (two male, one female) vanished from the campus of their north-eastern university over a long holiday weekend. The students were all popular and well-liked, with sterling reputations among their family and friends. Over the next few weeks, their ID\u2019s and driver\u2019s licenses began appear in the mail, all with the photo of the victim marked out with a dark pen. Despite extensive time and resources dedicated to the search, the students were never found. Similar abductions across the east coast and south of the United States persisted into the early nineties before stopping abruptly.<br /> Recently, a well-known and popular internet personality (known online as \u201cTravelKat94\u201d) vanished in a similar fashion; her defaced driver\u2019s license arriving in the mail days after her disappearance. Authorities believe that an imitator has adopted the signature taunt of Blank, but others believe that after thirty years, the original Blank has returned.<br /> No one knows who Blank really is. The only element tying Blank\u2019s victims together is that all of them were well-liked, \u201cdecent\u201d people, and their abductions inflicted deep and lasting emotional wounds on everyone in their immediate social circles. The only surviving victim of an abduction speaks of a figure in a dark coat, wearing an eye-less black mask, and speaking in a voice that never rose above a whisper. While her testimony was considered suspect at the time due to the vagueness of her descriptions and the gaps in her memory, she is the only known person to have encountered Blank and lived. While Blank was in all likelihood was once a mortal criminal who delighted in pain they caused, decades of rumors and legend have forged them into something \u2026.else.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Legend; <b>Virtue:</b> Patient; <b>Vice:</b> Cruel<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To cause suffering through social networks by abducting and murdering beloved individuals.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Sending the victim\u2019s defaced ID card to their family, friends, or local authorities.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Brawl 4 (Restrain), Crafts 2, Drive 2, Firearms 2, Intimidation 2, Investigation 3 (Police Procedure), Larceny 3 (Breaking and Entering), Medicine 2, Occult 1 (Urban Legends), Science 2, Stealth 4 (Avoid Surveillance, Silence), Streetwise 3 (Body Disposal), Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 3, Choke Hold, Cover-Up, Cover Tracks, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Professional Training 4 (Criminal; Investigation, Larceny, Streetwise), Resources 3, Sleight of Hand, Untouchable<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency</b> 4, <b>Willpower:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 5 dice]<br /> Sap [+0L melee; -1 Initiative; 6 dice; Stun]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Living Legend <b>Frailty:</b> Narrative Chains (Can only be harmed by the anonymous and forgotten)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Blackout, Camera Shy, Reality Stutter<br /> <br /> <b>Living Legend:</b> Once per scene, when someone fulfills one of the tenets of the Legend\u2019s \u201crules,\u201d the player can roll the slasher\u2019s chosen Attribute + Occult. Successes on this roll may be applied on one of the following: restoring spent Willpower, healing damage (one success for a bashing wound, two for lethal, three for aggravated), or applying the bonuses to rolls in pursuit of their goal. After this has been activated, successes that haven\u2019t been spent are discarded. They may not be banked to use in a following scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Narrative Chains:</b> The Legend gains a unique and specific frailty enforced by the nature of the tales surrounding them. Additionally, characters investigating the scourge\u2019s Tell gain an exceptional success on three successes rather than five.<br /> <br /> <b>Camera Shy:</b> The creature only ever appear on camera as a blurred silhouette of their actual shape and mortals have a hard time remembering exact detail about it. Rolls to accurately describe or recall such events are made at a \u20133 modifier.<br /> <br /> <b>Reality Stutter:</b> The creature\u2019s presence sets reality stuttering and convulsing, allowing it to flicker from place to place. By reflexively spending 1 Willpower when it moves, the creature can translocate itself to any location it can see up to its Speed in meters away, seeming to observers to just spasm in and out of reality as it goes. Doing so adds +2 to its Defense for the turn.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T21:12:50-07:00","id":1509132,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Botanist</span></b><br /> Genevieve Gallo grew up in a home on the outskirts of town, on a plot of land inherited from her immigrant grandparents. She was an only child, and witnessed her parent\u2019s deteriorating relationship; their traditional values would not condone a divorce. From her father, she gained a lifelong love of growing plants, and spent much of her youth in the family greenhouse, and eventually left home to study botany. She was often lonely and made every attempt to find companionship, but ended up drifting in and out of entanglements that were emotionally (and often physically) abusive. With the death of her father she moved back home to care for her ailing mother. Her mother was a difficult woman, and her infirmity only made her behavior worse. After an intense argument, a lifetime of frustrations boiled over and she stabbed her mother to death with a spade. After mulching her mother\u2019s corpse and using it to fertilize her plants, Genevieve experienced a great sense of calm. Since that day, she makes a point to keep a stock of her \u201cspecial\u201d mulch on hand. Her garden has never been greener.<br /> Genevieve is a thin Mediterranean woman in her early forties, with dark hair and brown eyes. She is plain-faced and has a mousy demeanor. Her over-sized glasses and old-fashioned mode of dress makes her seem older than she is. Despite her slender frame, she knows how to leverage her strength and is capable of surprising feats of brute force. Over the years, she has become reclusive and is out of practice with many social queues and expectations. She rarely makes eye contact and often mumbles when she speaks. If discussing topics related to plants, botany or gardening, she becomes animated and speaks with confidence, authority, and humor.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Undesirable; <b>Virtue:</b> Patient; <b>Vice:</b> Violence<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To make her garden grow.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Genevieve limits her depredations to trespassers and those she can lure to her property (typically gardening enthusiasts and day laborers). She mulches or composts the corpses and uses them to feed her plants.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 5, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Athletics 2 (Manual Labor), Crafts 3, Drive 1,Empathy 2, Firearms 2, Investigation 2 (Research), Medicine 1, Persuasion 2 (Everything\u2019s Fine), Science 3 (Botany), Stealth 3 (Ambush), Subterfuge 2 (Lies), Survival 2, Weaponry 3 (Gardening Tools)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Botany), Atavism, Cover-Up, Face in the Crowd, Hands of a Killer, Holistic Awareness, Language (Italian), Professional Training 3 (Botanist; Investigation, Science, Survival), Safe Place 3 (Green House), Resources 2, Sympathetic<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> Gardening Tools [+0L melee; +2 Initiative; 7 dice; Improvised]<br /> Light Revolver [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> Shovel [+1L melee;-3 Initiative; 6 dice; Knockdown]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Natural Compass; <b>Frailty:</b> Rejection<br /> <br /> <b>Natural Compass:</b> An Undesirable has a near-perfect sense of direction, and gains a +3 bonus to Perception, Athletics, Investigation, and Survival rolls when present in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Rejection:</b> The Undesirable suffers a \u22124 penalty on Social rolls that do not involve slashers and other monsters.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nest: The Greenhouse</span></b><br /> The Greenhouse is built on a large plot of land, purposely overgrown to provide privacy and dissuade trespassers. The greenhouse itself is large and well-maintained, and nearly every planting box is teeming with life. Warm light beams from the windows during the day and the air inside is uncomfortably humid. Any variety of garden vegetables, medicinal herbs, and other interesting horticulture can be found by those that know what to look for. The Greenhouse has an adjoining shed filled with well-maintained tools, including a high-end mulcher. After all, if there is no body, there is no crime.<br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Arsenal, Concealed, Innocent Facade<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Innocent Facade (Feature): </b>To casual observation, a Safe Place with Innocent Facade appears perfectly normal, with not even a hint of anything unusual happening. Any attempts to Investigate or use abilities to detect criminal, supernatural or otherwise unusual activity suffer a penalty equal to dots purchased in the Merit.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T20:37:12-07:00","id":1509248,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Champion</b></span><br /> David Carpenter was fascinated by death at an early age, and his youth was marked by incidents of animal cruelty and violence against his peers. As he matured, he demonstrated a keen mind and natural athletic talent, but his anti social and violent tendencies always undermined his potential to live a normal life. By his mid twenties, he had committed several murders, and was looking forward to committing more. David see\u2019s himself as a \u201cgrim reaper\u201d, and will study his victims his days, if not weeks, before deciding to make a kill. He chooses his victims on whim and instinct, preferring those who might present a challenge. He is almost disappointed if they die easily, and truly relishes when they fight back. He is well read, and has studied everything from true crime to anatomy; anything that he can apply to being a better killer.<br /> David makes a decent living by managing a run-down apartment building and supplements his income by taking occasional work as a killer for hire. He is obsessive about being \u201cThe Best\u201d, and memorizes the details of each and every murder he has committed in exacting detail. He imagines that he will be apprehended one day, and looks forward to sharing the lurid details with the authorities and (especially) the press.<br /> David is a Caucasian man of above average height in his early forties. He has dark brown eyes and his dark, close cropped hair has begun to go gray. He takes exercise and conditioning very seriously, and has the lean, honed physique of a professional athlete. His clothing is rugged and practical, and he will go shirtless when closing in for the kill. He is oddly talkative, and enjoys engaging his victims in almost genial banter, all while making his murderous intentions completely clear.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Brute; <b>Virtue:</b> Competitive; <b>Vice:</b> Philosophical<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To be the best killer in the world<br /> <b>Tell:</b> There is no joy in a swift kill. The Champion will stalk and harass his target for hours before finishing them.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Athletics 4 (Endurance), Brawl 4 (Strangle), Crafts 1 (Sabotage), Drive 2, Empathy 2, Intimidation 3, Investigation 2, Larceny 2, Medicine 1, Stealth 3 (Stalking), Streetwise 2, Survival 2, Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 4 (Knives)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 2 (Wealthy Patrons), Damnable Certainty, Eidetic Memory, Fleet of Foot 2, Hardy 1, Professional Training 2 (Athlete; Athletics, Medicine), Resources 2, Shiv 2, Style: Street Fighting 3<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 8 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 9 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Unstoppable <b>Frailty:</b> Tunnel Vision<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable:</b> A Brute never suffers wound penalties for any reason, and automatically passes any roll to remain conscious due to damage or pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Tunnel Vision:</b> A Brute suffers a \u22123 penalty to all Perception rolls, and to rolls to avoid being surprised in combat.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T20:03:04-07:00","id":1509434,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Chessmaster</span></b><br /> Jahanjir \u201cJohn\u201d Malhotra was fascinated by games. He played everything from board-games to video-games, but had a special love for chess, and few things pleased him as much as playing against a worthy opponent. Despite his great intelligence, John never became as successful as he would have hoped. Nearing middle age, his career as a mathematics professor was stalled and his marriage ended in divorce. One evening, after an ugly argument with his ex-spouse, John canceled his credit cards, emptied his savings, and vanished. A month later, his chief departmental rival was found dead in their bathroom, after what appears to have been a fatal slip on wet tile. From behind the scenes, John had begun to orchestrate the deaths of those he felt had wronged him.<br /> John is an Indian man in his late thirties. He wears his dark hair long and keeps a neatly trimmed beard. He is well-dressed, preferring a casual, comfortable style. He is a native Hindi speaker, but speaks other languages with only a faint accent. John had been planning to take revenge on those responsible for his frustrations for several years. When he finally walked away from his life, his network of allies, contacts, and blackmail victims had been well established. He uses blackmail, bribery, extortion, to recruit desperate individuals to do his bidding. He delivers their orders by dead-drop and none of them know who is pulling their strings. Now that all of his original targets are dead, John still has a taste for murder, and looks forward to playing his game on a larger board.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Virtuoso; <b>Virtue:</b> Insightful; Vice: Controlling<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To outmaneuver worthy opponents.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> John considers every death a move in a chess game; killing without a plan shows a lack of discipline.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3, Athletics 1, Computers 3, Crafts 2, Empathy 4 (Opponents), Firearms 3 (Revolver), Intimidate 2 (Demoralize), Investigation 5 (Planning), Persuasion 3 (Blackmail), Politics 2, Science 3 (Mathematics), Socialize 2, Stealth 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 4 (Misdirection)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 2 (Ex Wife - Secret Accomplice), Anonymity 3, Area of Expertise (Planning), Cover-Up, Eidetic Memory, Patient, Language (Arabic, English, French), Professional Training 4 (Mathematician; Computers, Investigation, Science), Resources 3, Staff 3 (Weaponry; Proxy Killers), Telltale Murder, Trained Observer 1, Untouchable<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 2 dice]<br /> Heavy Revolver [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Profiling; <b>Frailty:</b> Control Freak<br /> <br /> <b>Profiling:</b> Roll Intelligence + Empathy, contested by the victim\u2019s Manipulation + Subterfuge if they are actively attempting to conceal their motives or disguise their nature. Should the Virtuoso succeed, they can predict the victim\u2019s actions; they win ties in contested rolls against them, may raise Initiative one higher than the target\u2019s Initiative result at the beginning of combat. If able to spend an entire scene socially interacting with the target before making a roll, the ripper learns one unique trait: Virtue, Vice, Integrity or Willpower rating, Conditions suffered, Endowments, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Control Freak:</b> Whenever a Virtuoso fails on an Intelligence-based roll, or on a roll using one of the Skills bolstered by their Undertaking, they lose two points of Willpower.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T05:32:13-07:00","id":1509471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1481552-case-files-slashers?p=1508705#post1508705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: New Undertakings</b><br /> Those look pretty neat! Is this a fan-work or are these official from a supplement I missed?<br /> [/spoiler]</div> </div> </div> </div>It A Fan-work for slashers and can you do Slashers With The Predator Undertaking\u200b?\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/155637-slasher-gmc-port\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...asher-gmc-port</a>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","user":"Phoenix853457","date":". 04-24-2023, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T20:33:46-07:00","id":1509550,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Predator Undertaking</b><br /> <br /> I will give this some thought. The Undertakings in this supplement were done in a first edition style and might need to be tweaked for 2nd edition (and of course coming up with a new killer).<br /> <br /> In the meantime, today's post is below. <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Comedian</span></b><br /> Devin Swain was an awkward, chubby child, torn between his father\u2019s disapproval and his mother\u2019s suffocating affection. Jokes helped him cope with his difficult home life, and he found his knack for comedy ingratiated him to his peers. He developed a reputation as a class clown, but graduated high school and college with good grades. He eventually settled into a stable office job, got married to his college sweetheart, and was soon expecting a child. On weekends, he performed stand up at local comedy clubs, and garnered a fan base that enjoyed his wry observations and confused outrage at the absurdities of modern life.<br /> Something changed in him after his wife and unborn child were killed in an auto accident. To cope with grief, he focused on his comedy, abandoning his day job to become a full-time comedian. One evening, a particularly aggressive heckler got under his skin. After his set, he followed the heckler back to their car, and beat them to death with his bare hands. With that murder, he felt a great sense of peace and relief, and started to to search out ways to recapture that sensation. After his first few murders, Devin became methodical, holding on to his urges for months at a time before indulging. He is good at making connections with people, always trying a few jokes to see how they respond. He only kills those that do not laugh.<br /> Devin is a Caucasian man in his early thirties, with brown hair and brown eyes. He is tall, broad shouldered, and weighs nearly 300lbs. He dresses nicely and likes expensive wristwatches. His inheritances from the deaths of his parents and his wife have left him comfortably wealthy, but he still prefers to \u201cearn his keep\u201d, even though what he earns as a comedian is often meager.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Humorous; <b>Vice:</b> Grieving<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To relieve the pain of losing his family.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Comedian tests people he meets with jokes, and marks those that \u201cfail\u201d for death. He slashes the victims mouths into a grisly smile.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Brawl 3 (Bulk), Computers 2 (Programming), Empathy 3 (Read the Room), Expression 3 (Comedy), Firearms 2, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 3, Socialize 3, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 3, Weaponry 2 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Comedy), Barfly, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Professional Training 2 (Comedian; Empathy, Expression), Resources 3, Spin Doctor, Style: Fast Talking 2, Table Turner<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6, <b>Initiative:</b> 5, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 4 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Not Laughing at his Jokes)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T19:42:19-07:00","id":1509677,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Drifter</b></span><br /> Michael \u201cCoyote\u201d Nakai was drawn to the freedom of the open road at the age of sixteen, and has never looked back. Over the course of the following decades, he has crossed the country several times. And along the way he has left a trail of death. Coyote kills when the mood strikes. Sometimes, it\u2019s in anger, sometimes it\u2019s to steal valuables, other times it\u2019s for no reason at all. There is no consistency to his methods, and he can be brutally creative when the urge to kill strikes. After a kill, he moves on to the next town; waiting several years before returning to that location (if he ever returns at all). Coyote never stays in one place for long, never more than a few months. He travels by land, using whatever conveyance is convenient, typically by bus or passenger train, but he has covered countless miles just by walking. He hates air travel and avoids it whenever possible. His erratic methods and wide-ranging movement patterns have kept the authorities from tying his crimes together.<br /> Coyote is a Native-American man in his late-forties; his weathered skin and long, graying hair make him seem older. He is of average height and of wiry build. He sets people at ease with an air of effortless cool and is also an entertaining storyteller and harmonica player. He dresses in sturdy clothing suited to life on the road, a well-traveled denim jacket covered in buttons, and a wide-brimmed leather hat. Everything he owns is carried in an old duffel bag, and keeps few things that cannot be replaced easily. He supports himself by working odd jobs, petty larceny, and robbing his victims. Coyote rarely thinks about friends or family anymore, and considers himself as a wolf among hares.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Hypno;<b> Virtue:</b> Free-Spirit; <b>Vice:</b> Wanderer<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To never be caged or tied down<br /> <b>Tell:</b> After killing, Micheal moves on to his next destination, usually within 24 hours.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 5, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2 (Endurance), Brawl 2, Crafts 2 (Short Order Cook), Drive 2, Empathy 3, Expression 2 (Storytelling), Firearms 2, Larceny 2 (Theft), Occult 2, Persuasion 3, Socialize 2, Stealth 2, Streetwise 3 (Local Authorities), Subterfuge 2, Survival 2 (Urban), Weaponry 4 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 2, Atavism, Back Roads Atlas, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Hands of a Killer, Iron Stamina 2, Multilingual (French, Spanish), Language (Navajo), Professional Training 3 (Vagrant; Larceny, Streetwise, Survival), Sympathetic, Style: Street Fighting 2, Trained Observer 1<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency</b> 1, <b>Willpower</b> 8<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 5 dice]<br /> Hunting Knife [+1L melee;-1 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling Words; <b>Frailty:</b> Can\u2019t Let Go<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Glitch, Numen (Innocuous, Pathfinder)<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling Words:</b> When making a Social roll of any kind to get a target to drop their guard for a moment or to heed the slasher\u2019s words, the Hypno treats any success as an exceptional success. If using this moment to get close to the target and attack them, the scourge treats the victim as vulnerable to a Killing Blow, dealing damage equal to their dice pool for the attack plus any bonus for a weapon, with no roll required. If using this to demoralize or sow doubt in a target\u2019s mind, the scourge can instead drain a point of Willpower from the victim to regain it; they cannot drain Willpower from a target more than once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Can\u2019t Let Go:</b> Whenever a Hypno experiences a failure on a Social roll against a target she intends to kill, she becomes absolutely obsessed with the desired victim. She loses a point of Willpower at the end of every scene wherein she does not directly attempt to torment or attack the target. This effect ends when the target dies, or if the target manages to inflict damage on the Hypno.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:32:29-07:00","id":1509723,"title":"","content":"can you do Slashers With The Stranger and Transcendent Undertaking\u200bs?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/19KgVw1nbjo8z6WSTLTN_ZwGcWNJ-ejds/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/19KgVw1nbjo8z6WSTLTN_ZwGcWNJ-ejds/view\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/19KgVw1nbjo8z6WSTLTN_ZwGcWNJ-ejds/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/19KgVw1nbjo8z6WSTLTN_ZwGcWNJ-ejds/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/193jiordeMdS8FOWbAVbgUyfnV_nMIEOO/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/193jiordeMdS8FOWbAVbgUyfnV_nMIEOO/view\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/193jiordeMdS8FOWbAVbgUyfnV_nMIEOO/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/193jiordeMdS8FOWbAVbgUyfnV_nMIEOO/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","user":"Phoenix853457","date":". 04-26-2023, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T10:03:54-07:00","id":1509741,"title":"","content":"I wanted to tell you I really enjoy reading these. I haven't read every one of them yet, but I do check in when this thread pops up and read the ones that pique my interest. I don't normally look at the stats when I do, but I did with Coyote and I noticed you gave him his tribal language as one of his languages. That's a nice touch I feel a lot of people would have missed and thank you for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T21:34:49-07:00","id":1509834,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Stranger and Transcendent</b><br /> <br /> My plan is to play with these fan-generated undertakings at some point (probably when I start my third volume of slashers). All in due time..<br /> <br /> <b>RE: The Drifter</b><br /> <br /> Glad you noticed! I always try to build little bits of storytelling into the stat block, otherwise they start to all feel the same. Thanks and keep reading! <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Grandmother</span></b><br /> Esmeralda Ortega has left a trail of shattered lives in two countries over several decades. She is fascinated by and obsessed with children, and feels she can give them the things that their parents cannot. In her time, she has used falsified credentials to gain employment as a caregiver, typically as a nanny, nurse or as a daycare worker. Occasionally she has resorted to outright kidnapping, but she considers gaining the trust of parents and guardians as a key way to \u201crescue\u201d their children. Once she gains access to the child, she spoils them with attention and heaps praise upon them, quickly earning the child\u2019s trust. However, this invariable curdles once the child does something \u201cbad\u201d. The actual offense matters little and can be amazingly trivial, but once she decides that the child needs discipline, her imagination and cruelty know few limits. Such children are abducted or otherwise separated from their families. Over the course of hours, days, or even weeks,, she subjects her victims to all manner of physical and emotional torments. Most of her victims expire from this treatment, but some survive, left alive for days after Esmeralda has fled the area to seek new victims. While children are her preferred victims, she will not hesitate to kill an adult that threatens her, and what she lacks in strength and size, she more than makes up in deviousness and brutal cunning.<br /> Several bereaved families have offered significant rewards for her capture (or in some cases, her death).<br /> Esmeralda is a pleasant-faced Latina woman in her early fifties. She has deep brown eyes and she dyes her still-dark hair gray. She is of average height, slightly overweight and adopts a style of dress and mode of behavior that makes it easy to assume she is significantly older. She is native Spanish speaker, but speaks flawless English and can adopt several regional accents in both languages.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Maternal; <b>Vice:</b> Fickle<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To love and care for children<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Grandmother targets children under the age of 13; especially those arguing or fighting with their parents or guardians.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 5, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1 (Psychology), Athletics 1, Brawl 2, Empathy 4, Firearms 2, Investigation 2 (Cold Read), Larceny 2, Medicine 2 (Drugs), Persuasion 4 (Gain Trust), Politics 2 (Child Welfare), Socialize 2 (Parents), Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 4 (Children), Stealth 2 (Ambush), Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Alternate Identity (multiple 1 and 2 dot aliases), Closed Book 2, Damnable Certainty, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Children), Language (English), Professional Training 3(Caregiver; Empathy, Medicine, Persuasion), Spin Doctor, Striking Looks 1 (Maternal), Sympathetic<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 4 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> Stun Gun [+1L melee; +1 Initiative; 4 dice; Stun. Does not add successes to damage]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Disobedient Children)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.<br /> <br /> <b>Poison:</b> Grandmother uses a variety of over the counter and prescription medications to impair and incapacitate. She routinely tricks victims into ingesting sedative-laced food and drink. She also enjoys force feeding victims emetics and laxatives as a form of torture. Such drugs are typically Toxicity 4 poisons that deal bashing damage each minute until the victim accumulates a total of 4 successes on the resistance rolls.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T19:36:31-07:00","id":1509916,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Mariner</span></b><br /> Micheal Ngo has always loved the water. His family made their living working fishing boats and by the time he had joined the Navy, he was already a talented swimmer and sailor. After his military service, Micheal traveled the world, offering his skills as a fisherman and sailor to pay his way. One fateful night, he and his crew were caught out at sea in a brutal storm. Their ship was battered and Micheal suffered a severe head injury that left him near death. Upon recovery, his behavior changed. No longer the gregarious and dependable person he had been, he become short-tempered, withdrawn, and prone to morbid fascinations. He claims that after his injury, he began seeing visions of the gods and monsters that dwell in the deep, and that he was spared by them for a reason. Micheal now acts as a self-appointed agent of these gods, offering sacrifices and working towards some inscrutable greater purpose.<br /> Micheal prefers to drown his victims; luring them on to his boat or to a nearby body of water. While he prefers to subdue his victims, bind them with rope or netting, and throw them into the deep water, he is just as capable of holding someone under with his bare hands. He moves frequently, typically traveling by boat and always tries to remain within a days travel of open water.<br /> Micheal is a Vietnamese man in his late thirties. He is of average height, with close-cropped hair, and athletic physique, and skin weathered by a life spent on the water. He swims regularly and is skilled at SCUBA, free diving, and other techniques. He dresses in the rugged clothing of a fisherman, and prefers to ply his trade in warm tropical waters, but will go wherever his \u201cgods\u201d need him.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Brute; <b>Virtue:</b> Devoted; <b>Vice:</b> Irritable<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To be rewarded for his service to the Gods.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Mariner drowns all of his victims. He prefers to use a large body of water such as a river or ocean, but has made do with as little as a sink full of dishwater.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3 (Swimming), Brawl 3 (Grapple), Crafts 3 (Repair), Drive 3 (Water Vessel), Firearms 2, Intimidate 2, Occult 1 (Aquatic), Survival 3 (Nautical), Persuasion 2 (Lure), Socialize 2, Stealth 3, Subterfuge 2, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Cover Tracks, Crack Driver 2, Damnable Certainty, Hardy 2, Language (English, Vietnamese, many others), Professional Training 3 (Sailor; Athletics, Drive, Survival), Resources 2, Robust Health, Style: Close Quarter Combat 2, Style: Subdual 3<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Unstoppable <b>Frailty:</b> Tunnel Vision<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable:</b> A Brute never suffers wound penalties for any reason, and automatically passes any roll to remain conscious due to damage or pain.<br /> <b>Tunnel Vision:</b> A Brute suffers a \u22123 penalty to all Perception rolls, and to rolls to avoid being surprised in combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Fishing Yacht:</b> The Mariner currently pilots a medium-sized fishing yacht with sails and an onboard motor; the latest in a long line of vessels he has used as his home and primary mode of transport.<br /> Dice Modifier: -2, Size: 18, Durability/Structure: 2/20, Speed: 45, Availability: 3<br /> <br /> <b>Hold Breath (Stamina + Composure)</b><br /> A character may hold their breath for 30 seconds for each dot of Stamina without needing to make a roll. While in combat (or similar dramatic scenes), a character may hold their breath for 1 turn for each dot of Stamina they possess. Supernatural creatures capable of regeneration cannot heal damage caused by suffocation until they can get to a source of air.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> You can no longer hold your breath, the gaining the Drowning Tilt if submerged.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> You struggle to hold your breath, suffering a point of Bashing damage and imposing a cumulative -1 penalty on any subsequent rolls to hold your breath.<br /> <b>Success:</b> You successfully hold your breath, each success adds an additional 30 seconds (or extra turn if in combat) of holding your breath.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Add one minute or 3 rounds of holding your breath. This is in addition to time gained from rolled successes.<br /> <br /> <b>Swimming (Dexterity or Stamina + Athletics)</b><br /> Most actions are harder when done in water. When attempting anything underwater, swimmers suffer a -2 to their dice pools and Defense. Treading water, however, is a reflexive action that any character with a dot of Athletics can do automatically without penalty.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The succumb to injury, fatigue, or circumstance, and gain the Drowning Tilt.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> You make no real headway, effectively swimming in place.<br /> <b>Success:</b> You swim at a Speed equal to Strength + Athletics.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> At Storyteller\u2019s discretion, your character may attempt an instant action without suffering any penalties to dice pools or defense.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nest: Open Water</span></b><br /> Open Water is an area of ocean or lake where land is far enough away to either be very distant, or not seen at all. To be thrown into open water without a watercraft, flotation device, or exceptional swimming skill, is essentially a death sentence. Besides the grim possibility of simple drowning, hypothermia, dehydration, unpredictable tides and predatory animals are also common perils. Most actions in such an environment require successful Athletics rolls and dramatic failures lead to drowning.<br /> <b>Tilts:</b> Currents, Drowning, Extreme Cold<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Currents (Environmental):</b> Flowing water, inexorably push characters along a route, be it to danger or salvation.<br /> The Storyteller chooses the direction and strength of the currents, giving the latter a Strength rating of 1 to 5. Characters may resist the current\u2019s pull with a Strength + Athletics roll penalized by the current\u2019s Strength, but any who fail, cannot, or do not try to resist are carried by the flow with a Speed of the current\u2019s Strength x 5.<br /> <br /> <b>Drowning (Environmental):</b> You\u2019re surrounded by more water than you can presently cope with. Either you\u2019re in some sort of container or room filled with liquid, or you\u2019re simply exhausted by swimming through a large body of water. Regardless, your lungs are starting to fill with water, which is a losing proposition for most.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character suffers one point of bashing damage each turn he spends drowning, as oxygen loss takes its toll on your body.<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> Any form of immersion in a liquid is enough to cause the Tilt.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> Getting to a source of air and removing any liquid from your lungs is sufficient to end the ongoing damage from this Tilt.\u200b<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T21:48:41-07:00","id":1509919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1481552-case-files-slashers?p=1508489#post1508489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... And time for a new set of &quot;All Killer, No Filler&quot; Slashers! <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Apex</b></span><br /> Modi Bjornson is the type of person who has triumphed at everything he tried his hand at. Raised in an upper-middle class home in his native Iceland, he excelled in academics and sports, and showed a particular skill at power-lifting. Graduating from college with high marks, he traveled the world, voraciously seeking new opportunities, and trying his hand at many different careers. Over his travels, he saw the weaknesses of humanity all across the world, and developed a philosophy of personal fulfillment and accomplishment that allows it\u2019s practitioner to reach the \u201cApex\u201d of human potential. With the publication of his book \u201cThe Apex Principle\u201d, he has created a small empire, with online classes, speaking engagements, and a line of dietary supplements. His success has made him famous (especially among those who decry the loss of \u201ctraditional\u201d masculinity), wealthy, and has attracted a throng of loyal devotees to his philosophy.<br /> Modi also harbors the dark secret that he enjoys culling the weak from humanity. He uses his resources to find targets (typically drug addicts, homeless people, and the similarly under-privileged), and takes them to a remote wilderness area to hunt them down over the course of several days. If they survive, they will have proven their worth and would be rewarded with a large sum of cash. So far he has never had to pay.<br /> Modi is a handsome, heavily muscled man in his early forties. He has dark hair (stylishly cut), a full beard, and piercing blue eyes. He has distinctive tattoos with a dragon motif on his back and arms. He is well dressed in fashionable clothing that is cut to show off his impressive physique. He is a fanatic about fitness and diet, shunning any intoxicants, eating a carefully balanced diet, and is voluntarily celibate (at least until he can find an equally superior woman to be his mate).<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Puppeteer; <b>Virtue:</b> Edifying; <b>Vice:</b> Ambitious<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Raise up a superior human race<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Modi believes in culling the \u201cweak\u201d and inferior\u201d; most of his victims come from marginalized and under-privileged communities, but he has occasionally hunted those he has deemed \u201cunworthy\u201d of their wealth and privilege.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3 (Business), Athletics 3 (Weight Lifting), Brawl 3 (Overpower), Crafts 2, Computers 2, Drive 1, Empathy 2, Firearms 3 (Rifle), Intimidate 3, Investigation 3, Medicine 1(Nutrition), Persuasion 4 (Sales), Science 1, Socialize 2 (Social Media), Subterfuge 3, Survival 3, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Contacts 3 (Investors, Men\u2019s Rights, Publishers), Cover-Up, Fame 1, Inspiring, Language (English, German, Japanese, Russian), Professional Training 3(Entrepreneur; Academics, Persuasion, Socialize), Resources 5, Safe Place 3 (Palatial Estate), Staff 2 (Devotees), Striking Looks 2 (Handsome), Style: Martial Arts 3, Style: Strength Performance 2<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 2, <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 8 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged; -2 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> Rifle [+4L ranged; -5 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling <b>Frailty:</b> Falter<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Hypnotic Gaze, Supernatural Merit (Biokinesis 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling:</b> A Puppeteer can profile a victim much like a Virtuoso, but additionally benefits from the 8-again quality on any contested roll against a profiled target. They also impose a penalty equal to the scourge\u2019s Intelligence on victims\u2019 rolls to notice traps or react to ambushes set for them in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Falter:</b> Whenever a Puppeteer fails a Social roll, it becomes a dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> <b>Hypnotic Gaze:</b> The scourge\u2019s gaze can charm and beguile. When meeting the target\u2019s gaze, he can spend 1 Willpower and roll Presence + Persuasion contested by the target\u2019s Composure. If successful, the scourge counts as having a perfect impression against the target for Social maneuvers until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Style: Strength Performance: </b>Modi has specifically trained in lifting, pushing, and pulling enormous weights.<br /> \u2022 Strength Tricks (\u2022): Modi combines trained strength with a practical knowledge of physics to perform impressive, if minor, feats of strength. He can rip phone books in half, bend rebar, and smash bricks with his bare hands. He benefits from a +2 bonus to Expression and Intimidation rolls where he can demonstrate his talents, and an additional +1 to other non-combat feats of Strength.<br /> \u2022 Lifting (\u2022\u2022): Modi can perform incredible feats of raw strength. When attempting a feat of strength that requires a Strength + Stamina roll, he gains the Rote benefit \u2014 re-roll failed dice. This does not aid running, jumping, or combat rolls, but does aid in attempts to damage relatively immobile, inanimate objects. In that case he gains the Rote benefit on a combat dice pool no larger than his Strength + Stamina.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: Palatial Estate</b></span><br /> A large home sits on acres of carefully manicured lawns and topiary, and has all the trappings of luxury. The property is surrounded by high walls and fences, and is protected by a professional security service that responds quickly to intruders or any other unusual disturbances.<br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Escape Hatch, Home Security, Privacy<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Privacy (Feature):</b> The Safe Place is built with an eye towards discretion. The windows tint or drop a shade with the push of a button, the walls are sound-proofed, and even waste disposal is managed to prevent unwanted parties from picking through refuse looking for clues. In addition to penalties imposed by Home Security, anyone outside of the Safe Place that attempt to observe or investigate events or persons inside the Safe Place suffer an additional -2 penalty.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nest: Hunting Grounds</b></span><br /> The Hunting Grounds are a remote forest miles from anything resembling civilization. The area is filled with a variety of natural hazards and dangerous wildlife. During the winter months, these hazards are compounded by freezing temperatures and sudden storms that will kill anyone unprepared for the harsh conditions and can challenge even seasoned and well-equipped survivalists.<br /> <b>Tilts:</b> Blizzard (Winter), Extreme Cold (Winter), Maze, Stinging (Summer), Undergrowth<br /> <b>Traps:</b> Pit Trap<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Maze (Environmental): </b>The terrain twists and turns without readily available landmarks, disorienting and confusing affected characters. Characters attempting to trace their steps or find a way out of the area must succeed at an Intelligence + Composure roll with a 2 dice penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Pit Trap (Trap):</b> A deep pit lined with sharped stakes and concealed beneath a tarp and piles of leaves. trap comprised of large rocks and lumber hand suspended from the dense canopy of trees. Once the trap is triggered, the victims suffers a point of lethal damage from the fall and the spikes, or one point of aggravated damage on a dramatic failure. Escaping a pit trap requires a Strength + Athletics \u2013 2 roll to climb or jump out.<br /> Trigger: False Floor. A successful Wits + Composure roll with a -2 penalty avoids the trap.<br /> <br /> <b>Stinging (Environmental):</b> Mild toxins in undergrowth or stinging insects can irritate the skin and eyes of victims, impeding their efforts. The stinging or itching isn\u2019t enough to cause injury, but imposes a \u20131 dice \u201cwound penalty\u201d on all rolls as though the affected character were in the third-to-last box of Health.<br /> <br /> <b>Undergrowth (Environmental): </b>Dense undergrowth provides cover and entangles characters moving through it. Characters attempting to move through the undergrowth must succeed at a Strength + Athletics roll penalized by the<br /> undergrowth\u2019s Durability rating (typically 1-2 for roots, shrubs, and other vegetation).\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Is that..... Is that Andrew Tate as a slasher? I approve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T19:05:08-07:00","id":1510010,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: The Apex</b><br /> <br /> For Modi, I took inspiration from man-fluencers like Tate and his ilk. It's the main reason I cast him as a Puppeteer. While dangerous by himself, his greatest threat is the ability to pour his rhetoric into the ears of a legion of impressionable followers.<br /> <br /> For something less disturbing, here's a vicious cannibal! <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Ogre</span></b><br /> Oskar Baumann has always been hungry. And the more he ate, the more he grew. By the time he started secondary school, he was already a foot taller than his peers. Any that might of mocked him for his appearance quickly learned of his formidable strength. Though nicknamed \u201cOgre\u201d, few dared to say it his face. Despite his strong work ethic and good grades, Oskar decided had enough of formal education, and found steady work as a local repairman and settled into a routine of relative comfort. But the hunger remained.<br /> A craving lingered; no matter what or how much he ate, he never felt satisfied. He began having intense fantasies about cannibalism, and joined an online community of people who shared his interests. When a role-playing meet up spun out of control, Oskar finally got to indulge himself and there was no turning back. After several close-calls with the authorities, he now travels frequently, living out of a camper and finding work as a laborer when money is needed (supplemented by stealing from his victims).<br /> He typically stalks and abducts transients, and occasionally hires sex workers to satiate his craving (he has little actual interest in sex, but finds them convenient victims). He used to take the time to to cook and prepare his meals, but has become comfortable eating them warm and raw. Oskar suffers from misophonia, and cannot tolerate the sound of barking dogs.<br /> Oskar is a huge man, standing nearly seven feet tall, with a thick muscular body. He wears his brown hair long and has blue eyes. He has a thick jawline and heavy brow that makes his small eyes seem even smaller, and wears glasses with dark frames. His hands are large, and his teeth, though crooked, are hard and sharp. He pays little attention to his clothing, typically wearing overalls, work boots, and flannel shirts, but makes an effort to stay neat (which is a challenge; he is a messy eater). He has started to develop a skin condition and is plagued with acne, psoriasis, and dandruff.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Mutant; <b>Virtue:</b> Crafty; <b>Vice:</b> Hungry<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To sate his hunger<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Oskar is an unrepentant cannibal, and all of his victims will be partially consumed (starting with the heart and liver). If possible, he will extract meat and organs to \u201csave for later\u201d.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 2, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 4 (Grapple), Computers 2, Crafts 3 (Home Repair), Drive 2, Intimidate 4, Medicine 1, Persuasion 2 (Find Employment), Occult 1 (Folklore), Stealth 2 (Stalking), Streetwise 2, Survival 2 (Backwoods), Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Back Road Atlas, Damnable Certainty, Demolisher 2, Eidetic Memory, Hardy 2, Professional Training 2 (Laborer; Athletics, Crafts), Resources 1, Safe Place 2 (Camper), Striking Looks 2 (Brutish), Style: Brute Force 3<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, Potency: 1, Willpower: 8<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6, <b>Initiative:</b> 5, <b>Armor:</b> 2, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 12<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 7 dice]<br /> Vicious Bite [+2L melee; 6 dice; Armor Piercing 2]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Warped Form (Vicious Bite) <b>Frailty:</b> Sensitivity (Barking Dogs)<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Hidden Movement, Regeneration, Unholy Prowess (Stamina)<br /> <br /> <b>Warped Form:</b> A Mutant possesses natural weaponry that has a weapon modifier and armor-piercing quality of 2, with no Initiative modifier, as well as 2 points of Armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Sensitivity:</b> As well as the Social penalty suffered by Undesirables, a Mutant is sensitive to a stimulus chosen by the Storyteller. This might include bright light, the scent of roses, the feel of velvet, the sound of classical music, cats, extreme heat, etc. When exposed to the stimulus, the Mutant must spend a Willpower point or attempt to flee the scene immediately; if unable to flee, they either attempt to hide, or lash out to destroy or remove the stimulus. Regardless of spent Willpower, they suffer a \u22122 penalty on all dice pools provided the stimulus remains present.<br /> <br /> <b>Hidden Movement:</b> The scourge can move quicker than normal, as long as he is hiding. Whenever the scourge is completely alone or unobserved, he can move at twice his normal speed. Cameras do not function as proper observers, as the scourge\u2019s power is fueled by the fear of those he stalks.<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Prowess:</b> The scourge is quicker, stronger and hardier than he looks. The scourge adds one dot of Strength, Dexterity or Stamina per dot of Unholy Prowess.<br /> <br /> <b>Style: Brute Force:</b> Oskar embraces the devastating monster within himself and knows how to let it loose on the world around him. Brute Force attacks may only be made with bare hands or with fist-based weapons, such as bladed gloves or fist packs.<br /> \u2022 <b>Falling Pillar(\u2022):</b> Oskar clenches both hands high above his head, then brings them crushing down. Make an all-out attack to use Falling Pillar. In addition to the normal +2 dice bonus, Oskar benefits from the 8-again quality on his roll. If the attack causes damage equal to or greater than the opponent\u2019s Stamina, he suffers the Knocked Down Tilt<br /> \u2022 <b>Crush and Bite (\u2022\u2022):</b> Oskar clinches his victim and bites off a chunk of flesh, which bleeds profusely. This maneuver becomes an option as part of a grapple, replacing the normal bite maneuver. Not only does Oskar cause lethal damage equal to the successes rolled on the grapple, but the wound bleeds out, causing an additional level of lethal damage in the next turn. This effect does not apply to things that don\u2019t bleed.<br /> \u2022 <b>Juggernaut (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> With this ability, Oskar rushes his opponent, strikes, and knocks him away. If the Oskar can charge an opponent (moving at least 10 feet to build up momentum), any successful unarmed attack causes the Knocked Down Tilt.\u200b<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T19:34:18-07:00","id":1510012,"title":"","content":"On the other side of the disturbing flip-coin, what Undertaking would be a Slasher who \u2018suicides\u2019 victims after socially isolating them via false accusations (almost always of the sexual stuff) and public rage/shame campaigns? Thought Hypno first, but that Puppeteer sounds too nice to pass up\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T22:29:16-07:00","id":1510161,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Slaying by Slander</b><br /> <br /> A few thoughts on this. A slasher that socially isolates their victim by making accusations that ruins the victims credibility and rives them to suicide lines up closer to the Puppeteer. While a Charmer/Hypno could also use these tactics, the Charmer/Hypno tends to operate in a more up close and personal method - they would likely not be satisfied with such an indirect way of killing. A Puppeteer can use their profiling ability to find a vulnerable victim, and they are adept at spreading their ideology and getting others to do their dirty work. The right victim is key if the ultimate goal is death by suicide. Some people will never cave to social pressure, while others cannot live with their reputation in tatters. The biggest limitation is that a slander campaign can only be launched <b>once</b>, and puts the accuser under as much (if not more) scrutiny. A slasher wants to avoid that kind of attention and isn't going to be satisfied after just one victim. A Puppeteer would need to weave a network of proxies and dupes to spread their rumors and accusations. Cult of &quot;stans willing to viciously attack the accused socially, and perhaps physically) would be almost necessary or a slasher with this MO.<br /> <br /> Below is today's post. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Red Anne</b></span><br /> Anne MacLean was born and raised in Scotland, and she spent her early life in desperate poverty and turned to crime at a young age to help support the family. She quickly gained a reputation for her clever scams, imposing looks, and a wide mean streak. She has spent most of her life in an out of prison for any number of minor offenses. After her last stint in jail, she has \u201cgone straight\u201d, and opened a hotel catering to tourists and travelers. The first guest she killed was after she flew into a rage in an argument over the bill. After selling her victim\u2019s belongings and identification for a significant amount of money, she realized this was something she could get used to. Now the profit she makes is almost secondary to the satisfaction she feels from the kill, and grows surly when she has to contain her impulses.<br /> She has gathered a small ring of local small-time criminals to help sell property and dispose of evidence, and keeps them in line with a healthy cut of the money (and the looming threat of brutal violence). Anne\u2019s victims are always selected by their profitability, looking for those carrying assets that can easily be liquidated. She is prudent enough to avoid those whose disappearance might invite police, federal agents, and other nuisances. She also makes money loan sharking, selling drugs, and managing a small stable of prostitutes.<br /> Anne is a Caucasian woman in her mid-forties. She is tall, with a square, muscular frame and has a pale, freckled complexion. Her eyes are dark gray, her teeth are yellowed from years of smoking, and her hair is a wild, red mane. She dresses in rugged jeans and leather jackets, but likes feminine touches like painted nails, low-cut tops, and bright red lipstick. She likes to enjoy herself, and can frequently be found at a tavern, rugby game, or in the company of her current partner.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Brute; <b>Virtue:</b> Opportunistic; <b>Vice:</b> Avaricious<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To make money by any necessary means.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Anne\u2019s kills are rarely personal, and the victim must have something on them that can be resold for a profit.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2 (Feats of Strength), Brawl 4 (Sudden Violence), Crafts 1 (Repair), Empathy 1, Intimidate 4, Investigation 2, Larceny 2 (Lock Picking), Persuasion 2, Science 1, Socialize 3(Criminals, Guests), Streetwise 4 (Stolen Goods), Subterfuge 3 (Scam), Weaponry 2 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Air of Menace, Closed Book 2, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Hands of a Killer, Hobbyist Clique (Crime Ring; Streetwise), Professional Training 2 (Criminal; Larceny, Streetwise), Resources 3, Safe Place 2 (Hotel), Staff 2 (Criminals; Larceny), Striking Looks 1 (Formidable), Style: Close Quarters Combat 2, Style: Relentless Assault 2<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 5, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 9 dice]<br /> Brass Knuckles [+0L melee; 9 dice; Brawl]<br /> Kitchen Knife [+1L melee;-1 Initiative; 9 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Unstoppable <b>Frailty:</b> Tunnel Vision<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable:</b> A Brute never suffers wound penalties for any reason, and automatically passes any roll to remain conscious due to damage or pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Tunnel Vision:</b> A Brute suffers a \u22123 penalty to all Perception rolls, and to rolls to avoid being surprised in combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Style: Relentless Assault:</b> Red Anne fights with reckless abandon and barely restrained fury.<br /> <b>\u2022 Drop of a Hat (\u2022):</b> Red Anne goes from zero to ballistic at the start of a fight. She always moves to strike first. In the first turn of a fight, she adds 3 to her Initiative score, so long as she intends to make an all-out attack. After the first turn, this bonus fades.<br /> <b>\u2022 Eye of the Tiger (\u2022\u2022):</b> Red Anne can hone in on a single target, to the exclusion of all others. Choose a target. When making an all-out attack against that target, she retains her Defense against him. She still loses it against other characters. She\u2019s still considered to have sacrificed her Defense for the purpose of using other Style maneuvers.\u200b<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T23:04:54-07:00","id":1510566,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Silver Starr the Clown</span></b><br /> Zachariah Marx\u2019s family had been in the carnival business for generations, passed on from father to son. Zachariah himself took a great deal of pride in upholding the traditions of the traveling show, and knew every role intimately. But his favorite part of the show was the clowns, and he adopted the character of \u201cSilver Starr the Clown\u201d to entertain and amuse the crowds. But even in his youth, the traveling carnival was a dying institution. Disposing of several bothersome would-be buyers only delayed the inevitable. By the time the carnival was sold and his troupe was forced to disband, there was hardly any carnival left to speak of.<br /> Life among the \u201cmarks\u201d was difficult for Zachariah, many of the personal habits that no one noticed in the carnival marked him as a stranger in polite society, and he was shunned for it. Deep in his cups and contemplating suicide, he was approached by a tall, well dressed man who introduced himself as \u201cMr. Levesque\u201d. The man offered Zachariah a job with his traveling show, a place where he could stay the rest of his days with others like himself. Now, he rarely answers to Zachariah anymore, preferring to be called Silver Starr. He is happy and comfortable in his new home, with a family that he would do anything to protect. If Mr. Levesque knows anything about the occasional rude patron that goes missing, he hasn\u2019t said anything about it.<br /> Silver Starr is a heavy-set Caucasian man in his late forties with brown eyes and his head shaved bald. Despite his seeming girth he is strong and quick on his feet. He wears his signature face-paint with a silver stars over his eyes and dresses in shades of the evening sky with a field of stars on his black coat. Silver Starr is nearly always fully dressed and in character, even when making a rare trip beyond the carnival grounds. He presents himself as a whimsical, clever fellow, always ready with a witty joke or a magic trick, and isn\u2019t above some tumbling or slapstick to get a laugh. Disrespecting him or any of his found family incurs his wrath, and few can dissuade him from taking bloody vengeance on the offender. Despite his considerable skill as a performer, many find there to be something unsettling about his personae and are left with nightmare about the star-spangled clown.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Undesirable; <b>Virtue:</b> Entertaining; <b>Vice:</b> Proud<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Protect the Carnival and punish those that do not respect it.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Silver Starr only targets those that disrespect the carnival or jeopardize it\u2019s well being.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 5, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 2 (Juggling, Tumbling), Brawl 2, Crafts 3 (Arrange Accident), Empathy 2, Expression 4 (Jokes), Intimidation 3, Larceny 3 (Sleight of Hand), Occult 1, Socialize 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 3 (Misdirection), Weaponry 3 (Clubs)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 4 (Carnival Family), Atavism, Damnable Certainty, Professional Training 4 (Carny; Expression, Larceny, Subterfuge), Safe Place 4 (The Carnival), Sleight of Hand, Trained Observer 1<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 6 dice]<br /> Wooden Mallet [+3L, -4 Initiative; 8 dice; Knock Down, Stun]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Natural Compass; <b>Frailty:</b> Rejection<br /> <br /> <b>Natural Compass:</b> An Undesirable has a near-perfect sense of direction, and gains a +3 bonus to Perception, Athletics, Investigation, and Survival rolls when present in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Rejection:</b> The Undesirable suffers a \u22124 penalty on Social rolls that do not involve slashers and other monsters.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nest: The Carnival</span></b><br /> In this sophisticated age, The Carnival seems like a quaint relic of a bygone time. It appears in an open field or fairground near the outskirts of town every few years in the spring or fall, its presence announced by the smells of popcorn and funnel cake, and the sounds of the calliope. Despite its turn of the century aesthetics, the Carnival is a marvel, where even the occasional tarnished knob or frayed banner seems to add to the over all appeal. The Carnival boasts rides, games, and a multitude of shows and attractions, with acrobats, clowns, jugglers, fortune tellers and several more...unique oddities and amusements.<br /> The Carnival is the home and sanctuary of a troupe of performers and a menagerie of exotic beasts. All visitors to the Carnival are treated courteously, with the performers making every effort to entertain their audience, but there are several rules that must be observed - pay for your ticket (with exceptions made for special guests), respect the performers, and always applaud. Minor violations warrant a few scares and a stern warning. Those responsible for more...egregious violations often go missing.<br /> The Carnival remains for 3 days, typically over a weekend, packing up and disappearing into the night as quickly and quietly as it arrived.<br /> <b>Safe Place Features:</b> Escape Hatch, Home Security<br /> <b>Conditions/Tilts:</b> Crowded (Environmental), Lured, Maze<br /> <b>Traps:</b> Dangerous Amusements<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Crowded (Environmental):</b> The Carnival is packed with people, giving you little room to move. After every missed attack, roll a chance die. On a dramatic failure, something or someone in the background gets harmed. Ranged attacks are also made at a \u22121 penalty, as aiming for a specific target is difficult when droves of others are in the way.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> Waiting until the crowd clears or taking the fight elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <b>Dangerous Amusements (Trap):</b> The Carnival boasts several rides (such as the Ferris Wheel or the tilt-o-whirl) that might fail spectacularly (either due to shoddy maintenance or deliberate sabotage), becoming a deadly hazard. Once triggered, the ride speeds up and moves erratically, inflicting deals three levels of lethal damage and often inflict the Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt to reflect the battering a person takes from the malfunctioning ride. Dramatic failures impose the Immobilized Tilt, as the victim is pinned beneath the wreckage. If immobilized, escaping requires a Strength+ Athletics roll to shift aside the rubble. Dramatic failures often inflict the Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt to reflect twisted ankles and the like.<br /> <b>Trigger:</b> Sabotage/Malfunction. A successful Dexterity + Athletics roll with a -2 penalty downgrades to bashing damage and an exceptional success negates the damage entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Lured (Condition):</b> From the attractions to the treats, The Carnival is filled with things that captivate the imagination and compel the senses, making it easy for one to wander away, following the latest thing to catch their fancy. She will move away from a group of allies who are not also Lured without informing them; calling for back-up won\u2019t even cross her mind until an actual threat makes itself real. If allies who are not Lured notice what she is doing and try to get her to stay with the group, she will give the best argument she can as to why they should let her split off, and attempts to convince her otherwise suffer a \u20132 penalty.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The character investigates the lure and encounters a threat. An hour passes.<br /> <br /> <b>Maze (Environmental):</b> The terrain twists and turns without readily available landmarks, disorienting and confusing affected characters. Characters attempting to trace their steps or find a way out of the area must succeed at an Intelligence + Composure roll with a 2 dice penalty.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T20:32:35-07:00","id":1510663,"title":"","content":"Odd question to ask here buy how do you do the drop down boxes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T20:34:17-07:00","id":1510664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1481552-case-files-slashers?p=1510663#post1510663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd question to ask here buy how do you do the drop down boxes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoiler and /spoiler in [brackets].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T06:18:50-07:00","id":1510696,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Thank you, this is going to be a big help</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T22:24:50-07:00","id":1510757,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Student</span></b><br /> Noah Callahan is a sixteen year old student at the Spencer Academy private school. He makes good grades and is well liked by his peers. Both of his parents have successful careers, but their demanding jobs mean that Noah is often left to his own devices. He has developed a dangerous fixation on the cases and exploits of famous criminals, particularly mass murderers and serial killers. He frequently fantasized about killing, until one day he decided to make those gruesome imaginings a reality.<br /> His first victim was a homeless man, not much older than himself. He lured his victim to a secluded spot with the promise of money and food. When he let his guard down, Noah struck. The man struggled, but Noah was able to strike him down with a lose stone. This filled Noah with an exhilaration he had never felt before, while something within his heart died. He now seeks to recreate that sensation, but is being far more careful. He cleaned up the scene of his crime, but the fact it hasn\u2019t been traced back to him is more due to luck than anything else.<br /> Noah is a slim Caucasian teenager, already tall, and still growing into himself. He has fair skin, dark hair, and piercing blue eyes. He is athletic, and has earned a spot on the track team. He spends much of his free time listening to true-crime podcasts and watching serial killer documentaries. Noah has an uncanny knack for finding the balance of melee weapons, and constantly thinks about how to weaponize items in his environment. So far, he only has one victim to his credit, but he intends for that to be merely the first of many.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Inventive; <b>Vice:</b> Opportunistic<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Kill Again<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Noah\u2019s only regret is that his first kill was rushed and sloppy. The next time he will sign his work properly.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 5, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3 Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1 (Catholicism), Athletics 2 (Skateboard, Track and Field), Brawl 1, Computers 2, Crafts 1 (Weapons), Empathy 2, Investigation 2, Persuasion 3, Science 2, Stealth 2, Streetwise 2, Survival 1, Subterfuge 3 (Alibi), Weaponry 4 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Encyclopedic Knowledge (Crime), Fleet of Foot 2, Hands of a Killer, Language (Spanish), Striking Looks 1 (Handsome), Style: Improvised Weaponry 2, Sympathetic, Untouchable<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 3 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> Skateboard[+1L melee; +2 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> Improvised Object (Size 1) [+0L melee; +3 Initiative; 7 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Accusations)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.<br /> <br /> <b>Skateboard:</b> Until he gets his driver\u2019s license, Noah\u2019s preferred method of travel is his trusty skateboard. It also makes a decent improved weapon.<br /> Dice Modifier: -1, Size: 2, Durability/Structure: 2/4, Speed: Speed+5(17), Availability: 1\u200b<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T23:30:11-07:00","id":1511110,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Trouble</span></b><br /> Lucia \u201cTrouble\u201d Guerra has always felt like she was born too late, and models herself after the hard-living rock stars of the seventies and eighties. As a child, she was a popular and well-liked student. She was prone to bouts selfishness and cruelty, but learned to hide it behind an exciting and fun-loving persona. After high school, she earned entry to a prestigious performing arts academy, but dropped out to become a touring musician. She has played with many bands, but nothing stable or long term, and indulged fully in the rock and roll lifestyle, earning the nickname \u201cTrouble\u201d. The first person she killed was a lover who suggested that she \u201cslow down a bit\u201d, injecting them with a large dose of opiates. Since then, she has adopted a nomadic lifestyle, staying in an area long enough to work a few gigs, find the best drugs and parties, and move on when things get stale (usually leaving a corpse or two in her wake).<br /> Trouble is an attractive Latina in her late twenties. She is flamboyant and fashionable, mixing throwback glam rock and punk style with more modern trends. She changes her hair color often, and has several tattoos and piercings. She works out and eats well in order to maintain a trim and attractive physique, but years of substance abuse are starting to take their toll. Trouble expected to be dead before the age of thirty, and believes she is living on borrowed time. This realization has only made her hedonism and recklessness more pronounced, and if she makes it to thirty, she intends to go out in a violent blaze of glory.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Charmer; <b>Virtue:</b> Adventurous; <b>Vice:</b> Addict<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To live fast, die young, and don\u2019t let anyone get in your way.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Trouble is drawn to attractive, hard\u2014partying personalities; disposing of them if they can\u2019t keep up with her or if she simply gets bored of them. She particularly enjoys dosing her victims with tainted narcotics, or staging the murder to look like a suicide.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 2<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Athletics 1, Brawl 2, Crafts 3 (Electrician), Drive 2, Empathy 2, Expression 4 (Guitar), Firearms 2 (Pistol), Larceny 1, Medicine 1, Persuasion 4 (Peer Pressure), Socialize 3 (Party), Streetwise 3 (Drugs), Weaponry 2 (Blades)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Atavism, Area of Expertise (Guitar, Drugs), Barfly, Contacts 2 (Drug Dealers, Rehab), Cover-Up, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Hardy 3, Professional Training 3 (Musician; Academics, Expression, Persuasion), Pusher, Resources 2, Striking Looks 2 (Cool AF)<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 5 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 7 dice]<br /> Guitar [+1L melee;-2 Initiative; 5 dice, Improvised]<br /> Straight Razor [+0L melee, 6 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Disarming; <b>Frailty:</b> Thin Veneer (Buzz Kills)<br /> <br /> <b>Disarming:</b> The Charmer is a master manipulator and knows how to use Social Maneuvers to produce excellent results. They enjoy +2 dice when rolling to open a Door, and get a bonus die when making a first impression.<br /> <br /> <b>Thin Veneer:</b> During a scene, when a Charmer fails to maintain their persona after falling prey to their unique trigger, the ripper must spend a point of Willpower or lash out at the target of their ire. Further consequences to their Social Maneuvers may result depending upon which character the Charmer has shown their \u201ctrue face\u201d to.<br /> <br /> <b>Drugs</b>: Trouble abuses alcohol, narcotics and prescription medications. Being under the influence induces the <b>Drugged</b>, <b>Insensate</b>, or <b>Traumatized</b> Tilt. Tainted substances and overdoses inflict the <b>Poisoned (Grave)</b> Tilt. Outside of an action scene, a lethal overdose is a Toxicity 3 (Toxicity 4 for tainted substances) poison that deals damage once each minute for a duration of (Toxicity) minutes.\u200b<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T23:15:20-07:00","id":1511429,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Violent Heart</b></span><br /> Rosemary Kaye was by all accounts a normal girl throughout her youth and young adulthood. She was popular and attractive, and participated in gymnastics, cheer-leading, and student government. While she did have reputation of toying with the hearts and minds of those around her, nothing gave indication of the path she would take. Then one late night in college, while laying next to her boyfriend, she wondered \u201cwhat would happen if I killed him?\u201d After washing the blood from her body, she grabbed what resources she could and disappeared into the night. She has been asking herself the same question ever since.<br /> Rosemary thinks of herself as an avatar of desire and death, and is beginning to have trouble remembering her life prior to her first kill. She moves frequently, and is skilled with clothing, hair and makeup to radically change her look as she see\u2019s fit. She survives by stealing money from her victims and pawning their valuables. She has a collection of forged identification to help her evade the authorities. While she favors bars and night clubs as her stalking grounds, she has found plenty of targets at concerts, sporting events, and even church services. She uses a variety of methods to kill her victims, most commonly stabbing, strangulation, and occasionally drugging her victim and setting their residence on fire. All is fair in love and war.<br /> Rosemary is a petite Caucasian woman in her mid-thirties, with blond hair and blue eyes. Her small frame and her style of dress makes her seem much younger then her actual years, and she often passes as a teenager. She has a background in gymnastics and cheer-leading and is much stronger than she looks. While her victims include both men and women, she prefers to target men, especially those that fall for her seductive charms and seem traditionally masculine. The relative morality of her victims matters little to her; she has killed as many (if not more) of the kind and upstanding as she has killed of the cruel and selfish.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Hypno; <b>Virtue:</b> Disarming; <b>Vice:</b> Impulsive<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To find someone she cares about enough to not kill.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Rosemary targets single men (and occasionally women) that are socially isolated and desperate for company.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 2, Athletics 4 (Gymnastics), Brawl 3, Empathy 3 (Loneliness), Expression 1 (Dance), Larceny 3 (Forgery), Persuasion 4 (Seduction), Politics 1, Socialize 2, Subterfuge 4 (Disguise), Stealth 2, Streetwise 2, Weaponry 3 (Killing Blow)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anonymity 2, Barfly, Double Jointed, Fleet of Foot 1, Professional Training 3 (Criminal; Larceny, Streetwise, Subterfuge), Striking Looks 2 (Beauty), Spin Doctor, Style: Parkour 2, Sympathetic, Trained Observer 1<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency</b> 1, <b>Willpower</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 6 dice]<br /> Knife [+0L melee;-1 Initiative; 6 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling Words; <b>Frailty:</b> Can\u2019t Let Go<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Glitch 1, Hypnotic Gaze, Know Soul<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling Words:</b> When making a Social roll of any kind to get a target to drop their guard for a moment or to heed the slasher\u2019s words, the Hypno treats any success as an exceptional success. If using this moment to get close to the target and attack them, the scourge treats the victim as vulnerable to a Killing Blow, dealing damage equal to their dice pool for the attack plus any bonus for a weapon, with no roll required. If using this to demoralize or sow doubt in a target\u2019s mind, the scourge can instead drain a point of Willpower from the victim to regain it; they cannot drain Willpower from a target more than once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Can\u2019t Let Go:</b> Whenever a Hypno experiences a failure on a Social roll against a target she intends to kill, she becomes absolutely obsessed with the desired victim. She loses a point of Willpower at the end of every scene wherein she does not directly attempt to torment or attack the target. This effect ends when the target dies, or if the target manages to inflict damage on the Hypno.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T21:20:52-07:00","id":1511690,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Vivisectionist</b></span><br /> The individual known as \u201cThe Vivisectionist\u201d is a member of an international human trafficking and organ theft syndicate. He is the grisly truth behind the urban legends of drugged tourists waking up with missing kidneys. Catering to a wealthy and exclusive clientele, The Vivisectionist is a brilliant surgeon, and is said to maintain a respectable private practice, but savors the challenge and thrill of operating outside the law. With stolen medical records and meticulous research, victims are selected based upon his client\u2019s needs. Selected targets are kidnapped and sedated. In a grimy, makeshift operating room, the unfortunate individual\u2019s are operated upon, their organs transplanted on the spot, or harvested and sold to waiting buyers. Whatever remains of the victims is incinerated, dumped, or simply left behind like refuse.<br /> Little is truly known about the Vivisectionist, and his identity is fiercely protected by his criminal associates. Rumor has it that he was born to an impoverished family, and worked his way through college and medical school. To make ends meet, he dealt drugs and wrote bogus prescriptions, ending up in debt to a criminal syndicate. Realizing they had an asset, the syndicate pressed the Vivisectionist into using his skills to work off what he owed. In time, he came to enjoy the work, and remained with the organization long after his debt was settled.<br /> The Vivisectionist firmly believes that there are winners and losers in this life, and he intends to be a winner. Power and wealth are the only things he truly respects. They Vivisectionist is a male of average height with a lean build. They wear a mask and gloves, making it difficult to determine his race or age. When working he dresses in surgical scrubs or a black vinyl apron. Otherwise, he favors tailored fashions and is said to enjoy expensive food, lodging, and companionship.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Virtuoso; <b>Virtue:</b> Confidence; <b>Vice:</b> Avaricious<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To get paid to do what he loves<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Victims suffer some degree of medical mutilation; typically limb or organ removal.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3 (Research), Brawl 2, Crafts 2, Empathy 2, Investigation 2, Larceny 2 (Forgery), Medicine 5 (Surgery), Persuasion 2, Socialize 2, Science 3 (Chemistry), Stealth 2, Subterfuge 2, Weaponry 2 (Medical Tools)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 4 (Criminal Syndicate), Allies 3 (Wealthy Clients), Alternate Identity 2, Area of Expertise (Surgery), Damnable Certainty, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Fighting Finesse, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Surgery), Professional Training 4(Surgeon; Medicine, Science, Weaponry), Resources 4, Staff 3 (Henchmen)<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 9, <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 5 dice]<br /> Medical Implements [+1L melee, -2 Initiative; 7 dice, Improvised, 9-again]<br /> Scalpel [+0L melee, 8 dice, 9-again]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Profiling; <b>Frailty:</b> Control Freak<br /> <br /> <b>Profiling:</b> Roll Intelligence + Empathy, contested by the victim\u2019s Manipulation + Subterfuge if they are actively attempting to conceal their motives or disguise their nature. Should the Virtuoso succeed, they can predict the victim\u2019s actions; they win ties in contested rolls against them, may raise Initiative one higher than the target\u2019s Initiative result at the beginning of combat. If able to spend an entire scene socially interacting with the target before making a roll, the ripper learns one unique trait: Virtue, Vice, Integrity or Willpower rating, Conditions suffered, Endowments, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Control Freak:</b> Whenever a Virtuoso fails on an Intelligence-based roll, or on a roll using one of the Skills bolstered by their Undertaking, they lose two points of Willpower.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T17:12:02-07:00","id":1511941,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">War Dog</span></b><br /> Orphaned at an early age and raised by relatives that considered him a burden, Eddie \u201cWar Dog\u201d Brandt enlisted as soon as he was able. Rising through the ranks, he eventually joined the British Special Air Service (SAS), and served with distinction. Over his career, he witnessed horrors that have convinced him of the bleak meaninglessness of existence. Such a realization shook him to his core and awakened a darkness within him. Leaving the service, he became a mercenary and found solace in violence. Now semi-retired, he lives comfortably on the money he has saved over his career as a soldier-of-fortune. He finds civilian life intensely boring and still craves the danger and excitement of battle. For a time he stalked and murdered non-combatants, but found it unsatisfying. He now limits his kills to other \u201cwarriors\u201d. Once a suitable opponent is chosen, he will harass, intimidate, or kill someone close to his target to draw them into conflict.<br /> He travels frequently, with contacts (and victims) all over the globe. This makes his crimes difficult to trace. He lives hard; when not on a \u201cmission\u201d, he indulges in booze, drugs, gambling, and sex. He retains citizenship in the UK, and never kills while at home.<br /> Eddie is a tall, muscular Caucasian man in his mid-forties, with dark hair and green eyes. He keeps his hair cropped short and favors jeans and t shirts when off duty. His body is scarred from numerous conflicts and injuries over his lifetime. He has the SAS motto \u201cWho Dares Wins\u201d tattooed over his heart. When expecting a fight,, he dresses in tactical gear, body armor and a ballistic mask. Eddie has also made important connections to several pharmaceutical companies, and has access to small supply of experimental performance enhancing drugs. He will occasionally take special missions on behalf of his benefactors to refresh his supply.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Brute; <b>Virtue:</b> Zeal; <b>Vice:</b> Nihilism<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To drown his existential dread in vice and violence.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Eddie only targets \u201cwarriors\u201d; law enforcement, soldiers, martial artists, and violent criminals are all suitable victims.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Athletics 3, Brawl 4 (Multiple Opponents), Crafts 2, Drive 2, Firearms 4 (Assault Rifle), Intimidate 3, Investigation 2 (Terrorism), Medicine 1, Persuasion 2, Stealth 2, Streetwise (Drugs), Subterfuge 2, Survival 3(Navigation), Weaponry 3 (Knife)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 3 (SAS), Allies 3 (Pharmaceuticals), Contacts 2 (Drugs, Travel), Danger Sense, Defensive Combat (Brawl), Indomitable, Hardy 2, Professional Training 4 (Soldier; Brawl, Firearms, Survival), Style: Firefight 2, Style: Martial Arts 3, Resources 3, Small Unit Tactics<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 6, <b>Armor:</b> 2/4 [Flak Jacket], <b>Defense:</b> 6 [Flak Jacket]<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B, 9 dice]<br /> Heavy Pistol [+2L ranged, -2 Initiative, 7 dice]<br /> Combat Knife [+1L melee, -1 Initiative, 9 dice]<br /> Assault Rifle [+3L ranged, -3 Initiative, 8 dice]<br /> Shotgun [+3L ranged, -4 Initiative, 7 dice; 9-again]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Unstoppable <b>Frailty:</b> Tunnel Vision<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable:</b> A Brute never suffers wound penalties for any reason, and automatically passes any roll to remain conscious due to damage or pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Tunnel Vision:</b> A Brute suffers a \u22123 penalty to all Perception rolls, and to rolls to avoid being surprised in combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Combat Drugs:</b> Against particularity challenging opponents, Eddie uses experimental combat drugs to enhance his performance.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Demon:</b> Beta Adrinocine is a combination of steroids, amphetamines and painkillers. The drug is a black fluid and is administered via injection or inhaler.<br /> When taken, Eddie spends one point of Willpower to catalyze the drug. Until the end of the scene, Eddie gains a +2 bonus to Strength and Stamina rolls, he negates up to three points of negative modifiers from fatigue, injury or pain, and gains 1 point of Armor. Once the effect has worn off, he suffers 1 point of Lethal damage and gains the <b>Sick (Moderate)</b> Tilt for (10 \u2013 users Stamina + Resolve) hours due to nausea, muscle strain, heart palpitations and headaches. Demon is addictive and can cause the <b>Addicted</b> Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Hydra:</b> The compound known as Hydraxaline Omega is a chemical agent that radically boosts a user\u2019s cellular regeneration, allowing them to recover from injury in miraculously short periods of time. The drug is a milky white fluid that is administered via injection.<br /> When taken, Eddie spends two points of Willpower to catalyze the drug. Hydra immediately heals 2 points of bashing damage or 1 point of lethal damage (if any). Over the course of the next 24 hours, he halves all healing times. His metabolism skyrockets after using the drug, making him ravenously hungry and thirsty. The user gains the <b>Deprived</b> Condition until they can sate their appetite (usually by consuming approximately 2000 calories per dot of Stamina).<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Red Rush:</b> Ampheterex is an amphetamine compound that affects the user\u2019s neurochemistry, triggering a boost in energy level and reflexes. A dose of the drug comes in the form of a red-tinted fluid administered via inhaler. When taken, Eddie spends one point of Willpower to catalyze the drug. Until the end of the Scene, Red Rush grants a +3 bonus to Initiative and suppresses any Tilt or Conditions related to exhaustion or fatigue. Red Rush is an appetite suppressant; for (10 \u2013 users Stamina + Resolve) hours after usage, attempting to eat anything more substantial than a thin broth causes the <b>Sick (Moderate)</b> Tilt.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T21:24:13-07:00","id":1512329,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Warlock</span></b><br /> Danial \u201cDani\u201d Blake was an unusual child, prone to strange (and often morbid) flights of fancy. Even at an early age, he never conformed to the expectations of his conservative upbringing. The only person in his young life that made him feel accepted was his uncle, a fellow outsider who dabbled in stage magic and the occult, and he spent much of his adolescence working at his uncle\u2019s magic shop and occult bookstore. As time went on, Dani become more heavily involved in the occult, especially darker, left-hand practices, and gathered a coven of like minded souls. Danny craved real power, and with every successful ritual, with every new insight, he only wanted more. His practices led him to believe that more power could be obtained by sacrifice, claiming to souls of other practitioners of the craft. With the aid of his coven, he tracked down and sacrificed several other sorcerers. With the final sacrifice (his uncle, the only person he ever loved), Dani finally gained a measure of the power he craved, but at the cost of his soul. He now operates from the magic shop he inherited, serving as the leader of a cabal of occult practitioners as dedicated to the pursuit of power as he is. They continues to hunt magicians, mediums, and sorcerers, taking their their souls and stealing their power.<br /> Dani is Caucasian man in his late thirties. He has a lean build, but recent improvements to his exercise routine have packed on pounds of muscle. His sense of style is gender-fluid; he favors dramatic makeup, dark colors, ornate jewelry, elaborate tattoos, and bleaches his hair platinum blond. He is obsessive about gathering new lore, and has purchased (and stolen) and impressive collection of occult knowledge. He also maintains lifestyle of hard partying and sexual indulgence with his coven. He derives little joy from such acts, going through the motions to keep up appearances and assert control. His only real pleasure is the act of claiming a soul and binding it to a talisman.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking:</b> Puppeteer; <b>Virtue:</b> Ambitious; <b>Vice:</b> Megalomaniac<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To gain greater occult power.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> All of Dani\u2019s victims are slain through a specific (and grisly) occult ceremony.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3 (Macabre History, Linguistics), Athletics 1 (Weight-Lifting), Brawl 2, Crafts 1 (Talismans), Expression 2, Intimidation 3, Investigation 2, Firearms 2, Larceny 2 (Sleight of Hand), Occult 4 (Left-Hand Occultism, Rituals), Persuasion 3 (Seduce), Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 3 (Lies), Weaponry 3 (Knife)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Alternate Identity 1, Damnable Certainty, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Language (French, German, Latin, Spanish), Library 3 (Occult), Mystery Cult 4 (Apostles of the Dark One), Professional Training 3 (Occultist; Academics, Occult, Weaponry), Resources 3, Staff 2 (Occult; Coven), Striking Looks 1 (Provocative); *Ritual Sorcerer<br /> <i>* Mummy: The Cursed 2nd Edition, p.120</i><br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 3, <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11, <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee; 5 dice]<br /> Light Pistol [+1L ranged; 5 dice]<br /> Ritual Dagger [+1L melee; Initiative -1; 7 dice, 9-again]<br /> <br /> <b>Talent:</b> Compelling <b>Frailty:</b> Falter<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Agonize, Hex, Soul Stealer<br /> <br /> <b>Compelling:</b> A Puppeteer can profile a victim much like a Virtuoso, but additionally benefits from the 8-again quality on any contested roll against a profiled target. They also impose a penalty equal to the scourge\u2019s Intelligence on victims\u2019 rolls to notice traps or react to ambushes set for them in their nest.<br /> <br /> <b>Falter:</b> Whenever a Puppeteer fails a Social roll, it becomes a dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> <b>Talismonger:</b> Dani has a talent for crafting an assortment of amulets, charms, and talismans. Creating these objects uses the Build Equipment action (Chronicles of Darkness, p. 101-102). This requires a Wits+Occult roll, an hour of work, and grants a +2 equipment bonus to mundane rolls with a specific Skill. Dani also uses a talisman as a phylactery to hold the souls of his victims. As long as he carries a captured soul in a phylactery, he retains use of his Ritual Sorcerer Merit despite having an Integrity of 0. The power of a talisman fades after a week, after which the bonuses fade or the soul dissipates (or returns back to it\u2019s owner if they are still alive).<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mystery Cult: The Apostles of the Dark One</b></span><br /> For disciples of the left-hand path, before there was light, there was darkness, and thus the darkness is the source of all that came after it. By communing with this primordial darkness, the disciple seeks to gain ultimate knowledge and wisdom. For some, this is an attempt to improve the self so that they may express their inner divinity. Less ethical practitioners desire power so they might gain whatever else they want. In either case, personal ambitions are upheld over society, and the importance of self is emphasized. They often reject societal convention and the status quo, and embrace magical techniques that would traditionally be viewed as taboo, such using necromancy, demonology and other forbidden arts. Many embrace dark imagery and cultivate a macabre, mysterious, and sometimes menacing personae.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Purpose:</b> Central to practices of apostles is the effort to achieve communion with the Dark One.<br /> <b>Relic:</b> Rituals to establish communion usually involve a symbol important to a thaumaturge on a personal level, or one that\u2019s made important by its popularization and empowerment. Apostles draw on the practices of ceremonial magicians and hedge witches, and often find use in the rituals of ancient religious faiths they feel reflect the Dark One, whether as an adversarial being such as Satan or a once-accepted divinity such as the Egyptian god Set.<br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> Do what thou wilt shall be the whole of the law. An apostle learns to use his arts to fulfill personal desires. An apostle can conclude that society\u2019s rules are little more than shackles to be cast off should they be a hindrance to his advancement in knowledge and self-awareness. Without the safety net of shared morality, a thaumaturge can easily spiral out of control or sink into personal damnation.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation Benefits</b><br /> \u25cf - The new apostle delves deeper into the collected knowledge of their path. Gain an Academics or Occult specialty in \u201cLeft Hand Occultism\u201d.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - The apostle creates a larger then life persona, under which they practice their craft. Gain a dot of the Alternate Identity Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - The apostle has spent weeks, months, and years studying dark insights and esoteric lore. Gain a dot in Occult.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - No longer a mere dabbler, the apostle has obtained true insight and power. Gain the Ritual Sorcerer Merit.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf- The apostle has achieved true communion with the primordial darkness. The apostle enacts a personalized ritual, focusing on a symbolic representation of the darkness, and makes Composure + Occult roll. If successful, contact with the entity is initiated. Such communication grants knowledge and wisdom; until the apostle next sleeps, they gain the rote action benefit on a single mundane action (not roll; extended actions receive it for each roll). It is wise to avoid initiating communication too often (no more than once or twice a week, lest the apostle aggravate their patron and lose favor.)\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T04:34:06-07:00","id":1512345,"title":"","content":"The Ritual Sorcerer merit gained at level 4 of the cult, is that the merit from Mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T19:28:19-07:00","id":1512399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1481552-case-files-slashers?p=1512345#post1512345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ritual Sorcerer merit gained at level 4 of the cult, is that the merit from Mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct! It felt appropriate for this write up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T20:22:29-07:00","id":1512404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1481552-case-files-slashers?p=1512399#post1512399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct! It felt appropriate for this write up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. I just wanted to make sure I was following along with the class. Lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T17:11:31-07:00","id":1512796,"title":"","content":"This is the last one for a while, but keep watching this space! <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Waxman</b></span><br /> When a wild blaze encroached upon a wealthy community, a team of firefighters saw an opportunity to commit the perfect robbery. They singled out a particular home, owned by a reclusive multi-millionaire. When the old man refused to leave his home, even as flame and smoke began to engulf the building, what began as a heist quickly turned to murder. However, one of the crew had a crisis of conscience; and when he threatened to reveal their plot, he was knocked unconscious and left to burn, while the rest of the crew escaped with a small fortune in valuables. In the aftermath, no body was found.<br /> Months, and then years passed, and the investigation into the missing fireman grew cold. Then, the fire fighter\u2019s began seeing an apparition; a fireman, hideously burned, standing outside their windows, watching them. Because of his scarred and melted visage, this figure was named \u201cThe Waxman\u201d. Then the fires began. One by one, the homes of each member of the heist crew burned to the ground; the charred remains of the victims broken and hacked apart well before the fire claimed them. Even years after every member of the heist crew was dead, the mangled and burned bodies of doctors, police officers, soldiers, and other civic servants appear. Those that break their oath of service, for even the most minor and trivial reasons, might draw the attention of the Waxman.<br /> The Waxman is a broad-shouldered African American man of indeterminate age. His face and body are horrifically burn scarred, with an appearance reminiscent of melted wax. His lips are pulled back in a rictus grin and he takes deep, wheezing breaths. He wears a soot-stained fire fighter\u2019s coat over his sturdy, practical clothing.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undertaking: </b>Legend; <b>Virtue:</b> Just; <b>Vice:</b> Harsh<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To punish the Corrupt<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The Waxman\u2019s victims are always dismembered and burned.<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3 (Feats of Strength), Brawl 2 (Grapple), Crafts 2, Drive 2, Empathy 2, Intimidate 2, Investigation 3 (Arson), Medicine 2 (First Aid), Persuasion 2, Science 2 (Fire), Stealth 2, Survival 2 (Direction Sense), Weaponry 3 (Axe)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Demolisher 2, Hardy 2, Iron Stamina 2, Professional Training 3 (Fire Fighter; Athletics, Survival, Weaponry), Relentless, Striking Looks 2 (Horrific), Style: Heavy Weapons 2<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 0, <b>Potency:</b> 4, <b>Willpower:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5, <b>Initiative:</b> 7, <b>Armor:</b> 1/1 (Fire Fighter\u2019s Coat, +1 v. fire), <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Unarmed [+0B melee, 5 dice]<br /> Fire Axe [+2L melee, -4 Initiative; 9 dice, 9-again]<br /> <b>Talent:</b> Living Legend <b>Frailty:</b> Narrative Chains (can be hurt by molten gold or silver)<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Predator\u2019s Sense (Oathbreakers), Surprise Entrance, Weathervane (Fire)<br /> <br /> <b>Living Legend:</b> Once per scene, when someone fulfills one of the tenets of the Legend\u2019s \u201crules,\u201d the player can roll the slasher\u2019s chosen Attribute + Occult. Successes on this roll may be applied on one of the following: restoring spent Willpower, healing damage (one success for a bashing wound, two for lethal, three for aggravated), or applying the bonuses to rolls in pursuit of their goal. After this has been activated, successes that haven\u2019t been spent are discarded. They may not be banked to use in a following scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Narrative Chains:</b> The Legend gains a unique and specific frailty enforced by the nature of the tales surrounding them. Additionally, characters investigating the scourge\u2019s Tell gain an exceptional success on three successes rather than five.<br /> <br /> <b>Surprise Entrance:</b> No matter how secure its victims think they are, by spending 1 Willpower the creature may suddenly appear in the scene. Perhaps it can manifest out of higher-dimensional space via any right angle, emerge from any reflective surface, or it can simply burst through the wall. Any character witnessing this entrance must succeed on a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll or gain the Shaken Condition. If the characters have actively taken appropriate measures to keep the Horror out (barring and locking the door, smashing all the mirrors they can find, etc.) it will take the creature one full turn to break through, giving the characters time to react. If not, it\u2019s just there as a reflexive action and can take one more action before anyone can react.\u200b<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T10:07:18-07:00","id":1519968,"title":"","content":"How about a Brute and Mask that Go around spreading a plague?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/cor